{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Title 1 GENERAL PROVISIONS Chapter 1.1 Authority. \u00a7\u00a7 1.1.1.010 \u2013 1.1.4.060 Chapter 1.2 Name of the Pueblo. \u00a7\u00a7 1.2.1.010 \u2013 1.2.2.020 Chapter 1.3 Government Organization. \u00a7\u00a7 1.3.1.010 \u2013 1.3.4.050", "num": "1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1", "title": "Title 1 GENERAL PROVISIONS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 1.1 Authority. Part 1.1.1 Preamble \u00a7\u00a7 1.1.1.010 \u2013 1.1.1.010 Part 1.1.2 Adoption and Amendment \u00a7\u00a7 1.1.2.010 \u2013 1.1.2.020 Part 1.1.3 Interpretation of This Code \u00a7\u00a7 1.1.3.010 \u2013 1.1.3.010 Part 1.1.4 Code Reform and Approval Act of 2016 \u00a7\u00a7 1.1.4.010 \u2013 1.1.4.060", "num": "1.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1", "title": "Chapter 1.1 Authority.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 1.1.1 Preamble 1.1.1.010 General", "num": "1.1.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.1", "title": "Part 1.1.1 Preamble", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.1.010 General We, the people of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso, in order to establish justice, promote the common welfare and preserve the advantages of self-government, do hereby establish the Civil and Criminal Code of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso (1) to protect the peace and order of all person and their property within the territorial boundaries of the pueblo of San Ildefonso; (2) to protect the traditions, customs, landbase and human resources of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso; (3) to protect the natural resources and beauty of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso; (4) to preserve the life ways and natural resources of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso for future generations so that they may have the benefits that will be theirs to enjoy and keep. (1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.1|1.1.1.010", "title": "1.1.1.010 General", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 1.1.2 Adoption and Amendment 1.1.2.010 Authority 1.1.2.020 Repeal of Prior Inconsistent Ordinances", "num": "1.1.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.2", "title": "Part 1.1.2 Adoption and Amendment", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.2.010 Authority (a) This Civil and Criminal Code shall become effective when adopted by Resolution of the San Ildefonso Pueblo Council pursuant to the power invested in the Pueblo of San Ildefonso under the laws of the United States of America and applicable, treaties, and the will of the people of San Ildefonso, and shall apply to all persons who, through their residence, presence, business dealings, acts or omissions, have significant contacts with the Pueblo of San Ildefonso or its residents or incur civil obligations to persons or entities entitled to the protection of the judicial system at the Pueblo of San Ildefonso, and to all persons who commit criminal offenses against the Pueblo of or against its members, residents of other persons within the jurisdiction and on the lands of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso, under the traditions, customs and laws of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso and the laws of the United States of America. (b) The power to preserve internal order within the exterior boundaries of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso by punishing when necessary those under its jurisdiction who violate Pueblo civil or criminal law is absolutely essential to the existing sovereignty of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso. Further, the Pueblo of San Ildefonso has neither waived or surrendered its civil jurisdiction over non-Indians within the jurisdiction and/or on the lands of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso and no treaty or federal law has withdrawn the civil jurisdiction of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso over non-Indians found on the lands of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso. ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-013 ; 1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.2|1.1.2.010", "title": "1.1.2.010 Authority", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.2.020 Repeal of Prior Inconsistent Ordinances Any and all ordinances or portions thereof heretofore enacted by the San Ildefonso Pueblo council which is any way in conflict with the provisions of this Civil and Criminal Code are hereby repealed. (1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.2|1.1.2.020", "title": "1.1.2.020 Repeal of Prior Inconsistent Ordinances", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 1.1.3 Interpretation of This Code 1.1.3.010 General", "num": "1.1.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.3", "title": "Part 1.1.3 Interpretation of This Code", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.3.010 General This Code shall be interpreted pursuant to the traditions and customs of the San Ildefonso Tribe. Where any doubt arises as to these traditions and customs, the Court may request the advise of elders as counselors whom are familiar with these traditions and customs. If none such exists, then the Court may use applicable federal and state case law and statutory law, adopting those principles and procedures not in conflict with the laws, customs and traditions of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso. (1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.3|1.1.3.010", "title": "1.1.3.010 General", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 1.1.4 Code Reform and Approval Act of 2016 1.1.4.010 Findings 1.1.4.020 Short Title 1.1.4.030 Definitions 1.1.4.040 Purpose 1.1.4.050 Findings 1.1.4.060 Approval of Code Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R16-013, dated July 7, 2016.", "num": "1.1.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.4", "title": "Part 1.1.4 Code Reform and Approval Act of 2016", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.4.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Pueblo') is a sovereign and self-governing Tribe, recognized as such by the United States of America; (b) In 2011, the Pueblo approved a new governing Agreement (\"Agreement\") that separates the different duties and functions for the Governor, Council, and Courts; (c) The Agreement places the responsibility to write laws and approve budgets in the Council; (d) The Agreement requires the Council to pass laws and approve budgets in meetings that are open to the public, and to codify and publish all Council enactments; (e) The Pueblo enacted a \"Law and Order Code\" in 1984, and has passed various laws and resolutions since 1984; (f) The Council finds the need to update the Code to create a master, comprehensive Code to include not only the 1984 Code but also the enactments of the Pueblo since 2012. (g) The Council hereby enacts the attached law entitled, \"Code Reform and Approval Act of 2016.\" (h) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves and adopts this resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor, or his designee, to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this resolution. ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-013 ; 1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.4|1.1.4.010", "title": "1.1.4.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.4.020 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the, \"Code Reform and Approval Act of 2016.\" ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-013 ; 1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.4.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.4|1.1.4.020", "title": "1.1.4.020 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.4.030 Definitions (a) \"Code\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code of laws. (b) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. (c) \"PSIC\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code. ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-013 ; 1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.4.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.4|1.1.4.030", "title": "1.1.4.030 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.4.040 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to approve the Code, and to establish a process to maintain and update the Code as laws and budgets are enacted by the Council. ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-013 ; 1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.4.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.4|1.1.4.040", "title": "1.1.4.040 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.4.050 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) In 2011, t he Pueblo approved a new Governing Agreement (\"Agreement\") that separates the different duties and functions for the Governor, Council, and Courts; (b) The Agreement places the responsibility to write laws and approve budgets in the Council; (c) The Agreement requires the Council to pass laws and approve budgets in meetings that are open to the public, and to codify and publish all Council enactments; (d) The Pueblo enacted a \"Law and Order Code\" in 1984, and has passed various laws and resolutions since 1984; (e) The Council finds the need to update the Code to create a master, comprehensive Code to not only include the 1984 Code but also to include all Council enactments since 2012; (f) The Council finds that the Code requires constant updating to maintain an up-to-date, comprehensive record of all enactments of the Council including all laws and budgets. ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-013 ; 1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.4.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.4|1.1.4.050", "title": "1.1.4.050 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.1.4.060 Approval of Code Section 1.2.1 of the Code shall read as follows: (a) This Code, which includes both civil and criminal laws, shall become effective upon enactment and shall apply to all persons and property within the jurisdiction of the Pueblo. (b) The power to preserve internal order within the exterior boundaries of the Pueblo by punishing, when necessary, those persons under its jurisdiction who violate Pueblo civil or criminal law is absolutely essential to the existing sovereignty of the Pueblo. The Pueblo has neither waived nor surrendered its civil jurisdiction over non-Indians within its jurisdiction and/or on the lands of the Pueblo, and no treaty or federal law has withdrawn the civil jurisdiction of the Pueblo over non-Indians found within the jurisdiction of the Pueblo. (c) The Legislative Clerk, under the direction of the Lt. Governor or Council designee, shall maintain and update the Code as necessary. The Legislative Clerk shall have the power to number, renumber, cite, and reorganize the Code in order to maintain a comprehensive set of laws and budgets that are accessible to the public; provided, that the Legislative Clerk shall not have the power to modify any substantive provision of a law or budget enacted or approved by the Council. The Legislative Clerk shall redact from all Resolutions and laws the dollar amount or price that the Pueblo paid for any land purchase; provided that a member of the Pueblo shall be entitled to obtain the redacted purchase price(s) pursuant to an administrative process, which shall be established by the Governor to protect the proprietary and governmental interests of the Pueblo. In the absence of a Legislative Clerk, the Secretary shall assume the duties of the Legislative Clerk. (d) The Legislative Clerk shall provide official notice in writing of the enactment of a law, or approval of a budget or budget modification, by providing an official copy of such law or budget to the Executive and Judicial branches of government. ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-013 ; 1984 Code.)", "num": "1.1.4.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.1|1.1.4|1.1.4.060", "title": "1.1.4.060 Approval of Code", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.1.4.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 1.2 Name of the Pueblo. Part 1.2.1 Findings \u00a7\u00a7 1.2.1.010 \u2013 1.2.1.050 Part 1.2.2 Name \u00a7\u00a7 1.2.2.010 \u2013 1.2.2.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R13-017, dated May 7, 2013.", "num": "1.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2", "title": "Chapter 1.2 Name of the Pueblo.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 1.2.1 Findings 1.2.1.010 1.2.1.020 1.2.1.030 1.2.1.040 1.2.1.050", "num": "1.2.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.1", "title": "Part 1.2.1 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.2.1.010 The Pueblo is currently recognized by the Department of the Interior, Bureau of Indian Affairs (BIA) as the \"Pueblo of San Ildefonso\"; ( May 7, 2013, SI-R13-017 .)", "num": "1.2.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.1|1.2.1.010", "title": "1.2.1.010", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.2.1.020 Subsequently, the Pueblo is identified as the \"Pueblo of San Ildefonso\" on the list of tribes published annually in the Federal Register, pursuant to the Federally Recognized Indian Tribe List Act of 1994, Public Law 103-454; \u00a7103(4), 108 Stat. 4791; ( May 7, 2013, SI-R13-017 .)", "num": "1.2.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.1|1.2.1.020", "title": "1.2.1.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.2.1.030 The list of Federally Recognized Indian Tribes is used by Federal agencies and departments to determine eligibility for services; ( May 7, 2013, SI-R13-017 .)", "num": "1.2.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.1|1.2.1.030", "title": "1.2.1.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.2.1.040 The name \"the Pueblo de San Ildefonso\" is used in the Agreement, as approved by the BIA; ( May 7, 2013, SI-R13-017 .)", "num": "1.2.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.1|1.2.1.040", "title": "1.2.1.040", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.2.1.050 The Council recognizes the need to formally adopt an official name, such that there is consistency between the Pueblo's Governance Agreement, recognition by the BIA, listing in the Federal Register, and all other Pueblo documents. ( May 7, 2013, SI-R13-017 .)", "num": "1.2.1.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.1|1.2.1.050", "title": "1.2.1.050", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.1.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 1.2.2 Name 1.2.2.010 1.2.2.020", "num": "1.2.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.2", "title": "Part 1.2.2 Name", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.2.2.010 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby formally adopts the \"Pueblo de San Ildefonso\" as the official name of the Pueblo; ( May 7, 2013, SI-R13-017 .)", "num": "1.2.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.2|1.2.2.010", "title": "1.2.2.010", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.2.2.020 The Council requests that the United States Department of Interior acknowledge and change the name of the Pueblo to Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( May 7, 2013, SI-R13-017 .)", "num": "1.2.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.2|1.2.2|1.2.2.020", "title": "1.2.2.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.2.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 1.3 Government Organization. Part 1.3.1 Findings \u00a7\u00a7 1.3.1.010 \u2013 1.3.1.020 Part 1.3.2 Governmental Organizational Act \u00a7\u00a7 1.3.2.010 \u2013 1.3.2.070 Part 1.3.3 Governmental Organizational Act of 2016 \u00a7\u00a7 1.3.3.010 \u2013 1.3.3.050 Part 1.3.4 Typographical Correction Act of 2016 \u00a7\u00a7 1.3.4.010 \u2013 1.3.4.050 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R12-031, dated August 20, 2012.", "num": "1.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.3", "title": "Chapter 1.3 Government Organization.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.3.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 1.3.1 Findings 1.3.1.010 1.3.1.020", "num": "1.3.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.3|1.3.1", "title": "Part 1.3.1 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.3.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.3.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 1.3.1.010 The Council finds that well organized governments promote efficient provision of services to members; ( August 20, 2012, SI-R12-031 .)", "num": "1.3.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|1|1.3|1.3.1|1.3.1.010", "title": "1.3.1.010", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/1.3.1.010"}
