{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 2.1.2 Signatory Authority Act 2.1.2.010 Short Title 2.1.2.020 Definitions 2.1.2.030 Purpose 2.1.2.040 Jurisdiction 2.1.2.050 Findings 2.1.2.060 General Policy 2.1.2.070 Sovereign Immunity 2.1.2.080 Severability", "num": "2.1.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2", "title": "Part 2.1.2 Signatory Authority Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the Signatory Authority Act (\"Act\"). ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.010", "title": "2.1.2.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.020 Definitions (a) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (b) \"Governor\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governor. (c) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.020", "title": "2.1.2.020 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.030 Purpose This Act sets forth uniform standards and procedures for signatory authority for all government operations and activities. All Officers and employees of the Pueblo shall comply with the provisions of this Act. ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.030", "title": "2.1.2.030 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.040 Jurisdiction The Pueblo is a sovereign and self-governing Nation, with the authority to govern its people, lands, and resources. The Council is a duly recognized governmental entity acting primarily with the legislative authority for the Pueblo and shares the responsibility for the Pueblo's exercise of its sovereign governmental powers. ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.040", "title": "2.1.2.040 Jurisdiction", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.050 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) The Pueblo government affects accountability every day in the day-to-day operations of the Pueblo and its departments, authorities, and programs; (b) Various signatures of Pueblo officials and employees are required on a daily basis in order to process paperwork and implement our various programs; (c) The Pueblo does not explain the reason for including each signature, which undermines accountability of each Department, Authority, and Program to the Pueblo People; (d) Each signature may affect accountability to the Pueblo de San Ildefonso People and legal liabilities of the Pueblo or the signing official or employee; (e) The Pueblo finds and declares that pursuant to the Agreement, the Council has an obligation to the Pueblo to oversee the Pueblo's operations; and, (f) As part of this oversight authority, the Council has identified, for the good of the Pueblo, that there is an urgent need to clarify, outline, and further delineate the authority, goals, duties, and responsibilities of the Executive officials and employees and their signatory authority. ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.050", "title": "2.1.2.050 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.060 General Policy Requests for Expenditures of Funds . Any request for expenditures of funds shall be by Purchase Order. Each Purchase Order shall, unless otherwise provided herein, include signatures obtained in the following order: (a) Signature of Department Employee. The signature of a classified employee within any Department or Authority on any purchase order shall mean that the requisitioning Department needs the item being requisitioned. Because the head of a Department or Authority may directly requisition goods or services, the Department Employee signature line may, in those instances, remain blank. (b) Signature of Department Head. The signature of a Department Director or Manager shall mean that the requisitioning Department or Authority is legally authorized to make the expenditure and that the signatory believes the funding is budgeted. Legal authorization for expenditures may be found in: (1) a law or resolution as enacted by the Council; or (2) a contract between the Pueblo and the U.S. federal or state government; or (3) by the terms of the grant from which the funding shall be spent. Authorization can not come from the Annual Budget by itself, but must come from the authorizing laws, contracts, or grants. The Department Head signature line may remain blank only if the Purchase Order is submitted directly by the Office of the Governor for a purchase directly for one of those Offices. (c) Signature of Comptroller/Assistant Controller. The signature of the Comptroller shall mean that actual money is available to complete the purchase and in compliance with the Annual Budget. Additionally, the signature of the Controller shall mean that the Purchase Order complies with all applicable procurement requirements, such as any requirements for sealed bids, a competitive price checks, or Indian preference. (d) Signature of Governor. The signature of the Governor on a Purchase Order originating from any Department shall mean that all other required signatures have been obtained and the Purchase Order is ready for processing. The signature of the Governor on a Purchase Order is required if the Purchase Order is over $500.00. ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.060", "title": "2.1.2.060 General Policy", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.070 Sovereign Immunity Nothing in this Act waives the sovereign immunity of the Pueblo or any of its representatives, officers, or employees. ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.070", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.070", "title": "2.1.2.070 Sovereign Immunity", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 2.1.2.080 Severability If a court of competent jurisdiction finds any provision of this Act to be invalid or illegal under applicable tribal and/or federal law, such provision shall be severed from this Act and the remainder of this Act shall remain in full force and effect. ( April 18, 2012, SI-R12-018 .)", "num": "2.1.2.080", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.1|2.1.2|2.1.2.080", "title": "2.1.2.080 Severability", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.1.2.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 2.2 Authorizations. Part 2.2.1 Authorizing Emergency Powers to Governor \u00a7\u00a7 2.2.1.010 \u2013 2.2.1.030 Part 2.2.2 Authorization \u00a7\u00a7 2.2.2.010 \u2013 2.2.2.020 Part 2.2.3 Law Enforcement Commission Act of 2015 \u00a7\u00a7 2.2.3.010 \u2013 2.2.3.030 Part 2.2.4 Supporting a Strong 2018 Farm Bill for Indian Country \u00a7\u00a7 2.2.4.010 \u2013 2.2.4.030 Part 2.2.5 Authorization of Attorney Contract Act of 2018 \u00a7\u00a7 2.2.5.010 \u2013 2.2.5.030 Part 2.2.17 Act Authorizing the Formation of the Santa Fe Indian School District Governing Council and Adoption of Charter \u00a7\u00a7 2.2.17.010 \u2013 2.2.17.040 Part 2.2.18 Petitioning for a First Amended Federal Charter of Incorporation to Be Issued to Indian Pueblos Marketing, Inc \u00a7\u00a7 2.2.18.010 \u2013 2.2.18.040 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R12-003, dated January 3, 2012.", "num": "2.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|2|2.2", "title": "Chapter 2.2 Authorizations.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/2.2"}
