{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 4.6 Trial Date Deadline Modification Act Part 4.6.1 Trial Date Deadline Modification Act \u00a7\u00a7 4.6.1.010 \u2013 4.6.1.040", "num": "4.6", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|4|4.6", "title": "Chapter 4.6 Trial Date Deadline Modification Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 4.6.1 Trial Date Deadline Modification Act 4.6.1.010 Short Title 4.6.1.020 Purpose 4.6.1.030 Findings 4.6.1.040 Extension of Trial Date Deadline", "num": "4.6.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|4|4.6|4.6.1", "title": "Part 4.6.1 Trial Date Deadline Modification Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 4.6.1.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"TRIAL DATE DEADLINE MODIFICATION ACT.\" ( November 20, 2018, SI-R18-027 .)", "num": "4.6.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|4|4.6|4.6.1|4.6.1.010", "title": "4.6.1.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 4.6.1.020 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to extend the trial date deadline up to 90 days from arraignment in order to allow the parties sufficient time to prepare for trial. ( November 20, 2018, SI-R18-027 .)", "num": "4.6.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|4|4.6|4.6.1|4.6.1.020", "title": "4.6.1.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 4.6.1.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) The 60-day trial date deadline is an insufficient amount of time to allow parties adequate opportunity to prepare for trial; (b) Due to the short deadline set for trial, cases or matters are often dismissed after the 60-day trial deadline passes; (c) The Council has determined that it is in the best interest of the Tribe and for the administration of justice to extend the trial date deadline to allow parties sufficient time to prepare for trial and to avoid dismissal of cases that should go to trial. . ( November 20, 2018, SI-R18-027 .)", "num": "4.6.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|4|4.6|4.6.1|4.6.1.030", "title": "4.6.1.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 4.6.1.040 Extension of Trial Date Deadline If the defendant enters a plea of not guilty, the Court shall set a date for trial, which shall be at least ten (10) days but not more than ninety (90) days from the date of arraignment, unless the court finds good cause pursuant to a written order to provide a further extension of the trial date, but in no case shall the trial date extend beyond one year from the date of arraignment. ( November 20, 2018, SI-R18-027 .)", "num": "4.6.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|4|4.6|4.6.1|4.6.1.040", "title": "4.6.1.040 Extension of Trial Date Deadline", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/4.6.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5", "_type": "page"}}
