{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 5.1 Election Law Part 5.1.1 Background \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.1.010 \u2013 5.1.1.020 Part 5.1.2 ELECTION COMMISSION \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.2.010 \u2013 5.1.2.020 Part 5.1.3 ELECTIONS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.3.010 \u2013 5.1.3.010 Part 5.1.4 NOMINATIONS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.4.010 \u2013 5.1.4.010 Part 5.1.5 CANDIDATE QUALIFICATIONS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.5.010 \u2013 5.1.5.010 Part 5.1.6 VOTING \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.6.010 \u2013 5.1.6.030 Part 5.1.7 BALLOTS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.7.010 \u2013 5.1.7.010 Part 5.1.8 NOTICE OF ELECTIONS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.8.010 \u2013 5.1.8.010 Part 5.1.9 ELECTION PROCEDURES \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.9.010 \u2013 5.1.9.120 Part 5.1.10 CHALLENGES TO THE ELECTION RESULTS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.10.010 \u2013 5.1.10.010 Part 5.1.11 RECALL ELECTIONS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.11.010 \u2013 5.1.11.010 Part 5.1.12 REFERENDUM ELECTIONS \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.12.010 \u2013 5.1.12.010 Part 5.1.13 ELECTIONS TO FILL VACANCIES \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.13.010 \u2013 5.1.13.030 Part 5.1.14 OATH OF OFFICE \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.14.010 \u2013 5.1.14.020 Part 5.1.15 AMENDMENT AND SEVERABILITY \u00a7\u00a7 5.1.15.010 \u2013 5.1.15.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R12-006, dated January 9, 2012, and was amended pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R16-002, dated February 17, 2016.", "num": "5.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1", "title": "Chapter 5.1 Election Law", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.1 Background 5.1.1.010 Findings 5.1.1.020 Council Authorizations", "num": "5.1.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.1", "title": "Part 5.1.1 Background", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.1.010 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) the Pueblo's Election Law governs the scope and process for tribal elections. (b) the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Election Commission (\"Election Commission\") has determined a need to establish absentee voting in situations where students and active military personnel will be out of state at the time of a tribal election, and for homebound tribal elders who will not be able to physically appear at the tribal polling place. (c) the Election Commission has proposed changes to the Election Law to allow for absentee voting, including changes to some deadlines to accommodate timely issuance and return of absentee ballots, as shown on Attachment A hereto. (d) the Council has reviewed the proposed changes to the Election Law and determines it is in the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize amendment of the Election Law to allow for absentee voting in limited situations. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.1|5.1.1.010", "title": "5.1.1.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.1.020 Council Authorizations (a) The Election Law shall be amended to allow for absentee voting in tribal elections in limited situations as shown in Attachment A hereto. (b) The Election Commission is authorized to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this Resolution. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.1|5.1.1.020", "title": "5.1.1.020 Council Authorizations", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.2 ELECTION COMMISSION 5.1.2.010 Election Commission. 5.1.2.020 Authority and Responsibilities.", "num": "5.1.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.2", "title": "Part 5.1.2 ELECTION COMMISSION", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.2.010 Election Commission. The Election Commission shall be established in accordance with ELECTIONS AND VOTING, SECTION 2. ELECTION COMMISSION (a) of the Agreement which states: There shall be an Election Commission comprised of five Commissioners with three Commissioners elected by the people, one Commissioner selected by the Governor, and one Commissioner selected by the Council. The term of office for Election Commissioners shall be four years. Whenever a term expires for the seat of an appointed Commissioner, the Governor or the Council shall appoint a Commissioner within fifteen days after being sworn into office. Election Commissioners shall not be eligible to be a candidate for Governor or Council Representative. (a) Vacancies. If a vacancy occurs on the Election Commission due to resignation or other reason, the remaining members of the Election Commission shall appoint a qualified individual to fill the vacancy for the remainder of the unexpired term. (b) An Election Commissioner does not need to resign from their position in order to run for another term on the Election Commission, provided, the Commissioner shall not be directly involved in election activities at the polling place on the day of the election. (c) Compensation. The Commissioners shall be compensated according to the Agreement at ELECTIONS AND VOTING, Section 2. ELECTION COMMISISON (e) which states: The Election Commission shall be paid a fair compensation as established by the Council by law. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.2|5.1.2.010", "title": "5.1.2.010 Election Commission.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.2.020 Authority and Responsibilities. The Election Commission shall conduct all elections in accordance with Section 3 (b) of the Agreement which states: All elections shall be conducted by the Election Commission in a fair and impartial manner. (a) Elections. The Election Commission shall be responsible for conducting all elections and related activities, including but not limited to: (1) preparing and issuing election notices, ballots and election materials, (2) confirming candidate qualifications, including conducting candidate background investigations and posting results, (3) posting candidate and voter lists, (4) receiving and processing absentee ballot requests, (5) overseeing election day activities at the polling place(s), (6) confirming voter qualifications and determining voter challenges, (7) assisting voters with disabilities and/or language difficulties at the polling place(s), (8) collecting and counting ballots, (9) certifying and posting election results, (10) addressing any election challenges, (11) enforcing election laws and regulations, (12) adopting policies and procedures as necessary; provided, that: (i) any proposed policies and procedures shall be posted for public comment, (2) any public comments shall be reviewed and considered, and (3) any final policies and procedures shall be published and made available for public inspection, (13) appointing and swearing in Election Commission poll watchers and bailiffs if circumstances require, and (14) taking such other actions as necessary to ensure all elections and related activities are conducted properly, efficiently, fairly and impartially. (b) Administrative Duties and Responsibilities. (1) Budget The Election Commission shall work with the Governor and Council Budget Committee to propose an operating budget for the Election Commission to be included in the annual budget or a budget modification. (2) The Election Commission shall prepare all invoices and requisitions for all costs and expenses and shall ensure supporting documentation is included. The Election Commission shall designate a Commissioner as signatory authority for invoicing on behalf of the Commission. By affixing his or her signature to an invoice, the designated Commissioner is confirming that the payment, activity, or materials requested are within the approved Election Commission budget. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.2|5.1.2.020", "title": "5.1.2.020 Authority and Responsibilities.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.3 ELECTIONS 5.1.3.010 Elections.", "num": "5.1.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.3", "title": "Part 5.1.3 ELECTIONS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.3.010 Elections. (a) Types of Elections. There shall be three (3) types of elections: General Election, Primary Election, and Special Election(s). (b) General Election. General Elections shall be held in accordance with Section 3. ELECTIONS of the Agreement which states: ELECTIONS AND VOTING. SECTION 3. ELECTIONS. (a) General Elections shall be held on the first day of December of every year. (c) Primary Election. There shall be a Primary Election on the last Saturday of October of each year beginning in 2016. (1) A Primary Election shall be held for the Office of Governor. In a Primary Election for the Office of Governor, the candidates receiving the two (2) highest number of votes shall proceed to the General Election. (2) A Primary Election shall be held for the available Council Representative seats. In a Primary Election for Council Representative seats, the candidates receiving the ten (10) highest number of votes shall proceed to the General Election. (3) A Primary Election shall be held in all election cycles where a Primary Election is required, even if the number of candidates nominated in the Primary Election is less than the number of candidates who will appear on the ballot in the General Election. (4) No Primary Election shall be held for Special Elections. (d) Special Elections. All elections other than a General Election, or a Primary Election, shall be considered Special Elections, including elections to fill vacancies, Recall elections, and Referendum elections. (1) In a Special Election where there is only one (1) vacancy and there is only one (1) candidate, an election shall be held regardless. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.3|5.1.3.010", "title": "5.1.3.010 Elections.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.4 NOMINATIONS 5.1.4.010 Nominations.", "num": "5.1.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.4", "title": "Part 5.1.4 NOMINATIONS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.4.010 Nominations. (a) Self-Nomination. (1) Any qualified member of the Pueblo may submit his or her name in writing to the Election Commission as a candidate for elective office, along with a non-refundable fee of $25. (2) The Election Commission shall prepare and make publically available a Candidate Nomination form which shall include a release permitting the Election Commission to conduct a criminal background check on each candidate as required by the Agreement. The Election Commission shall use its best efforts to conduct candidate criminal background checks in a timely manner. The Election Commission shall conduct all criminal background checks in accordance with Section 2 (d) of the Agreement which states: The Election Commission shall conduct criminal background checks on all candidates and the results shall be made available to any enrolled Member of the Pueblo. (b) Nomination Period. (1) Nominations of persons seeking elective office shall be accepted by the Election Commission beginning September 1 st each year. Nominations for elective office shall be closed on September 6 th of each year. (2) The Election Commission shall establish and publicly post the dates and deadlines for acceptance of nominations of persons seeking elective office in Special Elections to fill vacancies. (3) The Election Commission shall publicly post the dates and deadlines for acceptance of nominations of persons seeking elective office for the First Election. (c) Candidate List. (1) The Election Commission shall prepare and post a preliminary list of candidates within three (3) days of the closing of the nomination period. (2) From the date of the posting of the preliminary list of candidates through September 12 th , the Election Commission shall accept any written challenges to the qualifications of any candidate or candidates on the preliminary list of candidates. The Election Commission shall make written determinations on any such candidate challenges no later than September 14 th of each year. The Election Commission shall post the final list of candidates no later than September 15 th of each year. (3) In the First Election, upon the close of the nomination period, the Election Commission shall prepare and post a final list of candidates and a final list of voters for the First Election. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.4|5.1.4.010", "title": "5.1.4.010 Nominations.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.5", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.5 CANDIDATE QUALIFICATIONS 5.1.5.010 Qualifications.", "num": "5.1.5", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.5", "title": "Part 5.1.5 CANDIDATE QUALIFICATIONS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.5"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.5.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.5.010 Qualifications. (a) All candidates for the Office of Governor shall meet the minimum qualifications as listed in the Agreement which states: GOVERNOR, SECTION 2. QUALIFICATIONS. Candidates for Governor shall be enrolled Members of the Pueblo, and be at least thirty years old on the deadline date for filing candidacy. Once a candidate is sworn in as Governor, the Governor shall immediately establish residency within the exterior boundaries of the as defined at the time of the adoption of this Agreement. (b) All candidates for the Council Representative shall meet the minimum qualifications as listed in the Agreement which states: THE GOVERNMENT SECTION 3 QUALIFICATIONS Candidates for Council Representatives shall be enrolled Members of the Pueblo, and at least twenty-five years old on the deadline date for filing candidacy. Once a candidate is sworn in as a Representative, the Representative shall have thirty days to establish residency within the exterior boundaries of the as defined at the time of adoption of this Agreement. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.5.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.5|5.1.5.010", "title": "5.1.5.010 Qualifications.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.5.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.6 VOTING 5.1.6.010 Voting Age. 5.1.6.020 Voters List. 5.1.6.030 Voting by Absentee Ballot.", "num": "5.1.6", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.6", "title": "Part 5.1.6 VOTING", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.6.010 Voting Age. (a) The voting age for any election shall be set in accordance with Section 1, Voting of the Agreement which states: ELECTIONS AND VOTING. SECTION 1. VOTING. All enrolled Members of the eighteen years of age or older shall have the right to vote. (b) Any voter who will turn age eighteen (18) by or on the date of the Primary Election shall be eligible to vote. For the First Election, the cut-off date for age eligibility shall be the date of the First Election. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.6.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.6|5.1.6.010", "title": "5.1.6.010 Voting Age.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.6.020 Voters List. (a) The Election Commission shall prepare and post a preliminary list of voters within three (3) days of the closing of the nomination period. (b) From the date of the posting of the preliminary list of voters through September 30 th , the Election Commission shall accept any written challenges to the eligibility of a voter or voters on the preliminary list of voters. The Election Commission shall make written determinations on any such voter challenges no later than October 10 th of each year. The Election Commission shall post the final list of voters no later than October 15 th of each year. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.6.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.6|5.1.6.020", "title": "5.1.6.020 Voters List.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.6.030 Voting by Absentee Ballot. (a) Eligibility. Any eligible voter who meets at least one of the following requirements shall be entitled to vote in any election by absentee ballot: (1) The voter is age fifty-five (55) or older and is homebound and unable to appear physically at the polling place on the date of the election; or (2) The voter is an out-of-state college student or in the military and unable to appear physically at the polling place on the date of the election. (b) Requesting An Absentee Ballot. (1) The eligible voter must request an absentee ballot by submitting a written request, either in the form of a letter or completed Absentee Ballot Request form, to the Election Commission. All requests must be signed by the requesting voter. The voter may be asked for proof they meet the eligibility requirements. (2) The voter may request an absentee ballot by submitting the written request to the Election Commission either by hand-delivery to the Election Commission office, mail to the Election Commission's listed address, or emailing a scanned request to the Election Commission's listed email address. (3) All absentee ballot requests must be received by the Election Commission no later than 4:30 p.m. on the 15th day before the date of the Election. Requests that are not received by the deadline or that do not meet any of the requirements will not be accepted or processed. It is the sole responsibility of the requesting voter to ensure that the voter's mailing address is correct on their written request. (A) In the event of a Special Election to fill a vacancy in an elected position, an eligible voter may request an absentee ballot up to 12:00 noon the day before the Special Election. However, due to the short timeframe of the Special Election, the Election Commission cannot guarantee that the requesting voter will timely receive the absentee ballot or that the returned ballot will be received by the Election Commission by the deadline and voters are encouraged to submit absentee ballot requests as early as possible. (c) The voter shall complete the absentee ballot and return the absentee ballot in accordance with the stated instructions. Ballots may be returned by U.S. mail, private delivery service, or by hand-delivery to the Election Commission office. (d) The deadline for receipt of cast absentee ballots shall be 4:30p.m. on the day before the election. (e) Absentee ballots that do not bear the voter's signature or are not properly enclosed in the envelopes or do not meet the requirements to cast an absentee ballot or are received after the stated deadline shall not be opened, processed or counted. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.6.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.6|5.1.6.030", "title": "5.1.6.030 Voting by Absentee Ballot.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.6.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.7", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.7 BALLOTS 5.1.7.010 Ballots.", "num": "5.1.7", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.7", "title": "Part 5.1.7 BALLOTS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.7"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.7.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.7.010 Ballots. (a) All elections shall be by secret ballot. (b) The Election Commission shall prepare an official ballot for every election. (1) The Election Commission shall ensure that absentee ballots are differentiated from regular ballots and provide space on the ballot to mark the date of issuance to the eligible voter. (c) The ballots shall list the names of the candidates whose names appear on the final list of candidates as established by the Election Commission. The names of candidates on the ballots shall be listed alphabetically by last name. No write-in candidates shall be permitted. This section shall apply to Primary Elections, all General Elections, and applicable Special Elections. (d) In Referendum Elections, the Election Commission shall prepare a ballot that includes the language from the referendum petition on the challenged law. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.7.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.7|5.1.7.010", "title": "5.1.7.010 Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.7.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.8", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.8 NOTICE OF ELECTIONS 5.1.8.010 Notice of Election.", "num": "5.1.8", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.8", "title": "Part 5.1.8 NOTICE OF ELECTIONS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.8"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.8.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.8.010 Notice of Election. (a) The Election Commission shall post a notice at the polling place and in other public locations announcing the date of the election, the location of the polling place, and other pertinent information at least ninety (90) days before the general election. (b) The Election Commission shall publicly post at the polling place and in other public locations a notice announcing the dates for Special Elections, the location and other pertinent information for Special Elections. (c) The Election Commission shall publicly post such dates and deadlines as necessary to hold the First Election within the two (2) month period required under the Agreement. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.8.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.8|5.1.8.010", "title": "5.1.8.010 Notice of Election.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.8.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.9 ELECTION PROCEDURES 5.1.9.010 Polling Place. 5.1.9.020 Hours of Voting. 5.1.9.030 Fifty (50) Foot Limit. 5.1.9.040 Maintaining Peace at Polling Place. 5.1.9.050 Method of Voting. 5.1.9.060 Counting the Ballots. 5.1.9.065 Posting and Notice of Election Results. 5.1.9.070 Tie Votes. 5.1.9.080 Spoiled Ballots. 5.1.9.090 Unused Ballots. 5.1.9.100 Rejected Ballots. 5.1.9.110 Recounts. 5.1.9.120 Other Matters Decided by the Election Commission.", "num": "5.1.9", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9", "title": "Part 5.1.9 ELECTION PROCEDURES", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.010 Polling Place. There shall be one (1) polling place located at the Pueblo. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.010", "title": "5.1.9.010 Polling Place.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.020 Hours of Voting. The polls shall be open at the polling place from 7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. Voters in line at the polling place but unable to cast their ballots before 7:00 p.m. shall be allowed to finish voting. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.020", "title": "5.1.9.020 Hours of Voting.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.030 Fifty (50) Foot Limit. No persons except members of the Election Commission shall be allowed to remain within fifty (50) feet of a polling place, except while actually voting. No campaigning or placement of campaign materials shall be allowed within a fifty (50) foot perimeter around the polling place. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.030", "title": "5.1.9.030 Fifty (50) Foot Limit.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.040 Maintaining Peace at Polling Place. The Election Commission or Bailiff shall keep the peace and protect the voting place by preventing disturbances at the polling place and interference with persons desiring to vote. This includes the authority to remove unruly or uncooperative persons from the polling place or from within the fifty (50) foot limit. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.040", "title": "5.1.9.040 Maintaining Peace at Polling Place.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.050 Method of Voting. (a) Each prospective voter, upon being identified as being on the final list of eligible voters, shall be handed an unused ballot by an Election Commissioner and shall sign his or her name on a form kept for that purpose to acknowledge that he or she has received the ballot. (b) The voter shall vote in privacy and shall place a mark opposite the name of the candidate or issue for whom he or she is voting. The ballot shall be placed in a locked ballot box. (c) The Election Commission may utilize electronic voting machines to conduct elections. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.050", "title": "5.1.9.050 Method of Voting.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.060 Counting the Ballots. (a) At the close of the polls, the Election Commission shall count the votes as marked on the ballots, including absentee ballots. At the end of the tally of in-person vote results, the Election Commission shall count votes as marked on the absentee ballots in accordance with Section (b) below. After the in-person and absentee ballot vote tally, the Election Commission shall determine the total votes cast for each candidate or issue. These unofficial results shall be written down, together with the number of spoiled, rejected and unused ballots, and shall be certified by each member of the Election Commission by signing his or her name thereto. (b) Counting Absentee Ballots (1) The Election Commission shall verify the validity of each cast absentee ballot by reviewing the voter list and list of absentee voters that were issued an absentee ballot and other documents necessary to ensure that the voter cast only a single ballot in the election. (A) In the event that a voter casts more than one absentee ballot, the Election Commission shall reject the older absentee ballot. (B) In the event that the voter has voted in-person at the polling place and also by absentee ballot, the in-person vote shall be counted and the absentee ballot shall be rejected. (2) The Election Commission shall count the votes as marked on the absentee ballots and add to the total vote tally. (c) The tallying of the votes shall be open for public observation, but the public must remain at a distance of at least ten (10) feet from the Election Commissioners and the ballot box. The public must remain quiet and in no way interfere with the orderly tallying of the ballots. If order cannot be kept, the Election Commission shall halt the tallying until such time order has been restored. (d) At the end of the tally, the Election Commission shall place the counted ballots, any spoiled ballots and any rejected ballots, in the ballot box. The ballot box shall be locked and sealed. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.060", "title": "5.1.9.060 Counting the Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.065", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.065 Posting and Notice of Election Results. (a) The unofficial results of an Election shall be posted at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public locations at the earliest possible time after the tallying of the votes. The Election Commission shall notify the Governor and Lieutenant Governor of the unofficial results. (b) The Election Commission shall certify the election results as \"official\" at the end of the election challenge period if no challenge was properly and timely filed, or at the completion of the election challenge appeal process. The Election Commission shall post the official election results at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public locations, along with notice to the Governor and Lieutenant Governor, at the earliest possible time after the end of the challenge period or the completion of the challenge appeal process. (c) In the event of a recount, the Election Commission shall post the results of the recount of ballots at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public locations, along with notice to the Governor and Lieutenant Governor. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.065", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.065", "title": "5.1.9.065 Posting and Notice of Election Results.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.065"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.070 Tie Votes. A tie vote for candidates in any Election shall be decided by a game of chance administered by the Election Commission at the earliest possible time after the election upon notice to the candidates, with notice posted at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public places. This does not prevent the tied candidates from participating in the game of chance immediately following the vote count if both candidates are available and agree to conduct the tie-breaker at that time. In such instance, posting of notice shall not be required. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.070", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.070", "title": "5.1.9.070 Tie Votes.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.080 Spoiled Ballots. If a voter spoils a ballot and obtains another ballot, the spoiled ballot shall be marked \"SPOILED\". Each member of the Election Commission shall sign his or her name below this marking and the spoiled ballot shall be secured by the Election Commission. All spoiled ballots shall be placed in the ballot box at the end of the tallying. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.080", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.080", "title": "5.1.9.080 Spoiled Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.090", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.090 Unused Ballots. Ballots unused at the end of the voting shall be marked \"UNUSED\" and shall be placed in the ballot box at the end of the tallying. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.090", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.090", "title": "5.1.9.090 Unused Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.090"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.100", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.100 Rejected Ballots. If, during the tallying of the votes, the Election Commission is unable to determine from the ballot the choice of the voter, the ballot shall be rejected. All rejected ballots shall be placed in the ballot box at the end of the tallying. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.100", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.100", "title": "5.1.9.100 Rejected Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.100"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.110", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.110 Recounts. Any Candidate for elective office shall have the right to request a recount of the election results within three (3) days of the election. Upon receipt of a written request for a recount, the Election Commission shall promptly conduct a recount and shall post the results of such recount in accordance with Section 7.C. above. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.110", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.110", "title": "5.1.9.110 Recounts.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.110"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.120", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.9.120 Other Matters Decided by the Election Commission. The Election Commission shall control all aspects of elections conducted by the Pueblo regardless of any Federal or State laws. Any other election matters not specifically addressed in this law shall be decided by the Election Commission. The decision of the Election Commission shall be final. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.9.120", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.9|5.1.9.120", "title": "5.1.9.120 Other Matters Decided by the Election Commission.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.9.120"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.10", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.10 CHALLENGES TO THE ELECTION RESULTS 5.1.10.010 Election Results Challenge Process.", "num": "5.1.10", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.10", "title": "Part 5.1.10 CHALLENGES TO THE ELECTION RESULTS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.10"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.10.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.10.010 Election Results Challenge Process. (a) Any eligible voter of the Pueblo shall have the right to challenge the results of any election within three (3) days of the posting of the unofficial election results by filing a written challenge with the Election Commission. (1) A challenge must contain the following information: (A) The voter's name, address, telephone number and email address (if any); (B) Sworn, notarized statement of facts alleged to show the violation or reason for the challenge that includes: (i) Section of Election Law that was violated; (ii) Identity of individual(s) involved in alleged violation(s); (iii) Date, time and location of violation(s); (iv) Estimated number of votes affected by the alleged violation(s); (v) Name and telephone number of any witnesses to the alleged violation(s). (C) Relief requested from the Election Commission. (b) The Election Commission shall make a determination on all election challenges within five (5) days of receipt of a challenge and the decision of the Election Commission shall be final for purposes of judicial review. (1) The following shall be used by the Election Commission when considering submitted complaints: (A) No official election shall be voided by decision of the Election Commission in response to a complaint unless the voter clearly demonstrates that: (i) violation(s) of the Election Law occurred; and (ii) said violation(s) would have changed the outcome of the election. (c) Following receipt and review of a properly executed challenge and such other evidence before the Election Commission, the Election Commission shall issue findings: (1) To dismiss the challenge, or (2) To acknowledge the merit of the challenge but to reaffirm the election in question, or (3) To acknowledge the merit of the challenge and to void the election in question. The Election Commission shall notify the voter of its decision and shall post the decision at appropriate public places. (d) If the voter who brought the challenge is not satisfied with the Election Commission's decision, he or she shall have the right to appeal the final decision made by the Election Commission by filing suit in the Trial Court of the Pueblo within five (5) days of the date of the decision of the Election Commission. The voter may not submit any evidence that was not before the Election Commission. A decision on an election challenge made by the Supreme Court of the Pueblo shall be final and shall not be subject to any further review by any other person or entity. (1) A Court shall not overturn the decision of the Election Commission unless it is shown by clear and convincing evidence that the Petitioner (Voter) is clearly entitled to the relief requested because the Election Commission decision was: (A) arbitrary and capricious; (B) an abuse of discretion; (C) not supported by the evidence of record; or (D) contrary to the Pueblo's law. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.10.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.10|5.1.10.010", "title": "5.1.10.010 Election Results Challenge Process.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.10.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.11", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.11 RECALL ELECTIONS 5.1.11.010 Recall Elections.", "num": "5.1.11", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.11", "title": "Part 5.1.11 RECALL ELECTIONS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.11"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.11.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.11.010 Recall Elections. (a) Recall elections shall be conducted in accordance with the ELECTIONS AND VOTING provision SECTION 4. REMOVAL AND RECALL of the Agreement which states: Recall The people reserve the power to subject any member of the Council or the Governor to a recall election, and the Election Commission shall hold a Recall Election upon a petition signed by at least fifty percent (50%) of the voters. A simple majority of the votes cast shall decide the outcome of the Recall Election. No more than two Members of the Council can be subjected to a Recall Process at one time, and any resulting vacancy shall be filled before any subsequent Recall Election can be held. (b) Upon written request, the Election Commission shall issue an official Recall Petition form to a petitioner. A recall petition shall include a legible name and date of each person signing such petition. A completed Recall Petition shall be filed with the Election Commission. (c) Petitioners have forty-five (45) days to submit a completed petition to the Election Commission. (d) For purposes of determining the validity of the recall petition, fifty percent (50%) of the eligible voters means fifty percent (50%) of all of the eligible voters of the Pueblo who are eighteen (18) or older at the time they signed the petition, and does not mean the number of voters who voted in the last election. (e) An individual who voluntarily places his or her signature on a petition shall not be allowed to later withdraw or remove their signature from the petition. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.11.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.11|5.1.11.010", "title": "5.1.11.010 Recall Elections.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.11.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.12", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.12 REFERENDUM ELECTIONS 5.1.12.010 Referendum Election Process.", "num": "5.1.12", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.12", "title": "Part 5.1.12 REFERENDUM ELECTIONS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.12"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.12.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.12.010 Referendum Election Process. (a) Referendum elections shall be conducted in accordance with the ELECTIONS AND VOTING provision SECTION 6. REFERENDUM of the Agreement which states: The people reserve the power to subject any law to a binding referendum election and the Election Commission shall hold a Referendum Election upon a petition signed by at least fifty percent (50%) of the voters. A simple majority of the votes cast shall decide the outcome of the Referendum Election. (b) Upon written request, the Election Commission shall issue an official Referendum Petition form to a petitioner. A referendum petition shall include a legible name and date of each person signing such petition. A completed Referendum Petition shall be filed with the Election Commission. (c) A tribal member shall have fifteen (15) days after an Act of the Council is signed into law by the Governor or veto override by the Council to request a referendum petition. (d) Petitioners have forty-five (45) days to submit a completed petition to the Election Commission. (e) For purposes of determining the validity of the referendum petition, fifty percent (50%) of the eligible voters means fifty percent (50%) of all of the eligible voters of the Pueblo who are eighteen (18) or older at the time they signed the petition, and does not mean the number of voters who voted in the last election. (f) An individual who voluntarily places his or her signature on a petition shall not be allowed to later withdraw or remove their signature from the petition. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.12.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.12|5.1.12.010", "title": "5.1.12.010 Referendum Election Process.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.12.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.13 ELECTIONS TO FILL VACANCIES 5.1.13.010 Special Election to Fill Vacancy. 5.1.13.020 Vacancy Certification and Election Process. 5.1.13.030 Special Provisions where Elected Official Causes Special Election and Runs as Candidate in Subsequent Special Election.", "num": "5.1.13", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.13", "title": "Part 5.1.13 ELECTIONS TO FILL VACANCIES", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.13.010 Special Election to Fill Vacancy. (a) A Special Election shall be held in accordance with the ELECTIONS AND VOTING provision, Section 5. VACANCIES of the Agreement which states: The Election Commission shall certify all vacancies. Vacancy shall result from removal, recall, physical incapacity, or any circumstance that makes holding office impossible for more than thirty (30) days. (b) A vacancy in an elected office shall also occur when the office holder voluntarily resigns from their position. Such resignation makes holding the office impossible for more than thirty (30) days since the office holder who resigns intends to voluntarily leave their position from the point of resignation forward. (1) Proof of voluntary resignation is a written letter or email correspondence that is offered as the office holder's intent to leave their position. (2) When an office holder voluntarily resigns, such resignation becomes effective immediately, and no formal acceptance by either the Council or Governor is necessary to make the resignation effective. (3) When an office holder voluntarily resigns, the resigning office holder shall notify the Election Commission of the voluntary resignation, or the Council or Governor shall notify the Election Commission in the event the resigning office holder provides notice of their resignation to either the Council or Governor. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.13.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.13|5.1.13.010", "title": "5.1.13.010 Special Election to Fill Vacancy.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.13.020 Vacancy Certification and Election Process. (a) The Election Commission shall certify all vacancies, regardless of how the vacancy occurred. (b) The Election Commission shall call a Special Election to be held within thirty (30) days of the Election Commission's certification of the vacancy. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.13.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.13|5.1.13.020", "title": "5.1.13.020 Vacancy Certification and Election Process.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.13.030 Special Provisions where Elected Official Causes Special Election and Runs as Candidate in Subsequent Special Election. (a) In the event that an elected official voluntarily creates a vacancy in their position for any reason, and then submits their name and intent to run in the Special Election to be held to fill the vacancy caused by that elected official, that candidate shall pay an election fee equal to one-half (1/2) of the cost of the Special Election. Such election fee must be paid in full before the former elected official is placed on the list of candidates for the Special Election. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.13.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.13|5.1.13.030", "title": "5.1.13.030 Special Provisions where Elected Official Causes Special Election and Runs as Candidate in Subsequent Special Election.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.13.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.14", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.14 OATH OF OFFICE 5.1.14.010 Oath of Office. 5.1.14.020 Severability.", "num": "5.1.14", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.14", "title": "Part 5.1.14 OATH OF OFFICE", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.14"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.14.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.14.010 Oath of Office. After the Election Commission has certified the results of the election and the winners are announced, and any challenges are finally decided, a Justice or Judge shall administer the oath of office on January 2 at a location within the Pueblo's lands. An Acknowledgement of the Oath of Office form shall be signed by the candidate, Justice or Judge and the Commission Chair and retained by the Commission. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.14.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.14|5.1.14.010", "title": "5.1.14.010 Oath of Office.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.14.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.14.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.14.020 Severability. The provisions of this law are severable and if any part or provision shall be held void by any court of competent jurisdiction, the decision of the court so holding shall not affect or impair any of the remaining parts or provisions of this law. ( February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.14.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.14|5.1.14.020", "title": "5.1.14.020 Severability.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.14.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.15", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.1.15 AMENDMENT AND SEVERABILITY 5.1.15.010 Amendment. 5.1.15.020 Severability.", "num": "5.1.15", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.15", "title": "Part 5.1.15 AMENDMENT AND SEVERABILITY", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.15"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.15.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.15.010 Amendment. The Council may amend this law upon a majority vote of the Council in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement for making laws. The Election Commission may submit to the Council suggested amendments to the law as deemed necessary. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.15.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.15|5.1.15.010", "title": "5.1.15.010 Amendment.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.15.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.15.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.1.15.020 Severability. The provisions of this law are severable and if any part or provision shall be held void by any court of competent jurisdiction, the decision of the court so holding shall not affect or impair any of the remaining parts or provisions of this law. ( August 1, 2023, SI-R23-011 ; February 17, 2016, SI-R16-002 ; January 9, 2012, SI-R12-006 .)", "num": "5.1.15.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.1|5.1.15|5.1.15.020", "title": "5.1.15.020 Severability.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.1.15.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 5.2 Election Law Amendments and Restatement of 2019 Part 5.2.1 Election Commission \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.1.010 \u2013 5.2.1.020 Part 5.2.2 Elections \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.2.010 \u2013 5.2.2.010 Part 5.2.3 Nominations \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.3.010 \u2013 5.2.3.010 Part 5.2.4 Candidate Qualifications \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.4.010 \u2013 5.2.4.010 Part 5.2.5 Voting \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.5.010 \u2013 5.2.5.020 Part 5.2.6 Ballots \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.6.010 \u2013 5.2.6.010 Part 5.2.7 Notice of Elections \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.7.010 \u2013 5.2.7.010 Part 5.2.8 Election Procedures \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.8.010 \u2013 5.2.8.130 Part 5.2.9 Challenges to the Election Results \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.9.010 \u2013 5.2.9.010 Part 5.2.10 Recall Elections \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.10.010 \u2013 5.2.10.010 Part 5.2.11 Referendum Elections \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.11.010 \u2013 5.2.11.010 Part 5.2.12 Elections to Fill Vacancies \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.12.010 \u2013 5.2.12.030 Part 5.2.13 Oath of Office \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.13.010 \u2013 5.2.13.010 Part 5.2.14 Amendment and Severability \u00a7\u00a7 5.2.14.010 \u2013 5.2.14.020", "num": "5.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2", "title": "Chapter 5.2 Election Law Amendments and Restatement of 2019", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.1 Election Commission 5.2.1.010 Election Commission. 5.2.1.020 Authority and Responsibilities.", "num": "5.2.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.1", "title": "Part 5.2.1 Election Commission", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.1.010 Election Commission. The Election Commission shall be established in accordance with ELECTIONS AND VOTING, SECTION 2. ELECTION COMMISSION (a) of the Agreement which states: There shall be an Election Commission comprised of five Commissioners with three Commissioners elected by the people, one Commissioner selected by the Governor, and one Commissioner selected by the Council. The term of office for Election Commissioners shall be four years. Whenever a term expires for the seat of an appointed Commissioner, the Governor or the Council shall appoint a Commissioner within fifteen days after being sworn into office. Election Commissioners shall not be eligible to be a candidate for Governor or Council Representative. (a) Vacancies. If a vacancy occurs on the Election Commission due to resignation or other reason, the remaining members of the Election Commission shall appoint a qualified individual to fill the vacancy for the remainder of the unexpired term. (b) An Election Commissioner does not need to resign from their position in order to run for another term on the Election Commission, provided, the Commissioner shall not be directly involved in election activities at the polling place on the day of the election. (c) Compensation. The Commissioners shall be compensated according to the Agreement at ELECTIONS AND VOTING, Section 2. ELECTION COMMISISON (e) which states: The Election Commission shall be paid a fair compensation as established by the Council by law. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.1|5.2.1.010", "title": "5.2.1.010 Election Commission.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.1.020 Authority and Responsibilities. The Election Commission shall conduct all elections in accordance with Section 3 (b) of the Agreement which states: All elections shall be conducted by the Election Commission in a fair and impartial manner. (a) Elections. The Election Commission shall be responsible for conducting all elections and related activities, including but not limited to: (1) preparing and issuing election notices, ballots and election materials, (2) confirming candidate qualifications, including conducting candidate background investigations and posting results, (3) posting candidate and voter lists, (4) overseeing election day activities at the polling place(s), (5) confirming voter qualifications and determining voter challenges, (6) assisting voters with disabilities and/or language difficulties at the polling place(s), (7) collecting and counting ballots, (8) certifying and posting election results, (9) addressing any election challenges, (10) enforcing election laws and regulations, (11) adopting policies and procedures as necessary; provided, that: (i) any proposed policies and procedures shall be posted for public comment, (2) any public comments shall be reviewed and considered, and (3) any final policies and procedures shall be published and made available for public inspection, (12) appointing and swearing in Election Commission poll watchers and bailiffs if circumstances require, and (13) taking such other actions as necessary to insure all elections and related activities are conducted properly, efficiently, fairly and impartially. (b) Administrative Duties and Responsibilities. (1) Budget. The Election Commission shall work with the Governor and Council Budget Committee to propose an operating budget for the Election Commission to be included in the annual budget or a budget modification. (2) The Election Commission shall prepare all invoices and requisitions for all costs and expenses, and shall ensure supporting documentation is included. The Election Commission shall designate a Commissioner as signatory authority for invoicing on behalf of the Commission. By affixing his or her signature to an invoice, the designated Commissioner is confirming that the payment, activity, or materials requested are within the approved Election Commission budget. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.1|5.2.1.020", "title": "5.2.1.020 Authority and Responsibilities.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.2 Elections 5.2.2.010 Elections.", "num": "5.2.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.2", "title": "Part 5.2.2 Elections", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.2.010 Elections. (a) Types of Elections. There shall be three (3) types of elections: General Election, Primary Election, and Special Election(s). (b) General Election. General Elections shall be held in accordance with Section 3. ELECTIONS of the Agreement which states: ELECTIONS AND VOTING. SECTION 3. ELECTIONS. (a) General Elections shall be held on the first day of December of every year. (c) Primary Election. There shall be a Primary Election on the last Saturday of October of each year beginning in 2016. (1) A Primary Election shall be held for the Office of Governor. In a Primary Election for the Office of Governor, the candidates receiving the two (2) highest number of votes shall proceed to the General Election. (2) A Primary Election shall be held for the available Council Representative seats. In a Primary Election for Council Representative seats, the candidates receiving the ten (10) highest number of votes shall proceed to the General Election. (3) A Primary Election shall be held in all election cycles where a Primary Election is required, even if the number of candidates nominated in the Primary Election is less than the number of candidates who will appear on the ballot in the General Election. (4) No Primary Election shall be held for Special Elections. (d) Special Elections. All elections other than a General Election, or a Primary Election, shall be considered Special Elections, including elections to fill vacancies, Recall elections, and Referendum elections. (1) In a Special Election where there is only one (1) vacancy and there is only one (1) candidate, an election shall be held regardless. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.2|5.2.2.010", "title": "5.2.2.010 Elections.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.3 Nominations 5.2.3.010 Nominations.", "num": "5.2.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.3", "title": "Part 5.2.3 Nominations", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.3.010 Nominations. (a) Self-Nomination. (1) Any qualified member of the Pueblo may submit his or her name in writing to the Election Commission as a candidate for elective office, along with a non-refundable fee of $25. (2) The Election Commission shall prepare and make publically available a Candidate Nomination form which shall include a release permitting the Election Commission to conduct a criminal background check on each candidate as required by the Agreement. The Election Commission shall use its best efforts to conduct candidate criminal background checks in a timely manner. The Election Commission shall conduct all criminal background checks in accordance with Section 2 (d) of the Agreement which states: The Election Commission shall conduct criminal background checks on all candidates and the results shall be made available to any enrolled Member of the Pueblo. (b) Nomination Period. (1) Nominations of persons seeking elective office shall be accepted by the Election Commission beginning September 1 st each year. Nominations for elective office shall be closed on September 15 th of each year. (2) The Election Commission shall establish and publically post the dates and deadlines for acceptance of nominations of persons seeking elective office in Special Elections to fill vacancies. (3) The Election Commission shall publicly post the dates and deadlines for acceptance of nominations of persons seeking elective office for the First Election. (c) Candidate List. (1) The Election Commission shall prepare and post a preliminary list of candidates within three (3) days of the closing of the nomination period. (2) From the date of the posting of the preliminary list of candidates through September 30 th , the Election Commission shall accept any written challenges to the qualifications of any candidate or candidates on the preliminary list of candidates. The Election Commission shall make written determinations on any such candidate challenges no later than October 10 th of each year. The Election Commission shall post the final list of candidates no later than October 15 th of each year. (3) In the First Election, upon the close of the nomination period, the Election Commission shall prepare and post a final list of candidates and a final list of voters for the First Election. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.3|5.2.3.010", "title": "5.2.3.010 Nominations.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.4 Candidate Qualifications 5.2.4.010 Qualifications.", "num": "5.2.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.4", "title": "Part 5.2.4 Candidate Qualifications", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.4.010 Qualifications. (a) All candidates for the Office of Governor shall meet the minimum qualifications as listed in the Agreement which states: GOVERNOR, SECTION 2. QUALIFICATIONS. Candidates for Governor shall be enrolled Members of the Pueblo, and be at least thirty years old on the deadline date for filing candidacy. Once a candidate is sworn in as Governor, the Governor shall immediately establish residency within the exterior boundaries of the as defined at the time of the adoption of this Agreement. (b) All candidates for the Council Representative shall meet the minimum qualifications as listed in the Agreement which states: THE GOVERNMENT SECTION 3 QUALIFICATIONS Candidates for Council Representatives shall be enrolled Members of the Pueblo, and at least twenty-five years old on the deadline date for filing candidacy. Once a candidate is sworn in as a Representative, the Representative shall have thirty days to establish residency within the exterior boundaries of the as defined at the time of adoption of this Agreement. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.4|5.2.4.010", "title": "5.2.4.010 Qualifications.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.5", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.5 Voting 5.2.5.010 Voting Age. 5.2.5.020 Voters List.", "num": "5.2.5", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.5", "title": "Part 5.2.5 Voting", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.5"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.5.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.5.010 Voting Age. (a) The voting age for any election shall be set in accordance with Section 1, Voting of the Agreement which states: ELECTIONS AND VOTING. SECTION 1. VOTING. All enrolled Members of the eighteen years of age or older shall have the right to vote. (b) Any voter who will turn age eighteen (18) by or on the date of the Primary Election shall be eligible to vote. For the First Election, the cut-off date for age eligibility shall be the date of the First Election. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.5.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.5|5.2.5.010", "title": "5.2.5.010 Voting Age.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.5.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.5.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.5.020 Voters List. (a) The Election Commission shall prepare and post a preliminary list of voters within three (3) days of the closing of the nomination period. (b) From the date of the posting of the preliminary list of voters through September 30 th , the Election Commission shall accept any written challenges to the eligibility of a voter or voters on the preliminary list of voters. The Election Commission shall make written determinations on any such voter challenges no later than October 10 th of each year. The Election Commission shall post the final list of voters no later than October 15 th of each year. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.5.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.5|5.2.5.020", "title": "5.2.5.020 Voters List.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.5.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.6", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.6 Ballots 5.2.6.010 Ballots.", "num": "5.2.6", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.6", "title": "Part 5.2.6 Ballots", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.6.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.6.010 Ballots. (a) All elections shall be by secret ballot. (b) The Election Commission shall prepare an official ballot for every election. (c) The ballots shall list the names of the candidates whose names appear on the final list of candidates as established by the Election Commission. The names of candidates on the ballots shall be listed alphabetically by last name. No write-in candidates shall be permitted. This section shall apply to Primary Elections, all General Elections, and applicable Special Elections. (d) In Referendum Elections, the Election Commission shall prepare a ballot that includes the language from the referendum petition on the challenged law. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.6.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.6|5.2.6.010", "title": "5.2.6.010 Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.6.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.7", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.7 Notice of Elections 5.2.7.010 Notice of Election.", "num": "5.2.7", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.7", "title": "Part 5.2.7 Notice of Elections", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.7"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.7.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.7.010 Notice of Election. (a) The Election Commission shall post a notice at the polling place and in other public locations announcing the date of the election, the location of the polling place, and other pertinent information at least ninety (90) days before the General Election. (b) The Election Commission shall publicly post at the polling place and in other public locations a notice announcing the dates for Special Elections, the location and other pertinent information for Special Elections. (c) The Election Commission shall publicly post such dates and deadlines as necessary to hold the First Election within the two (2) month period required under the Agreement. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.7.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.7|5.2.7.010", "title": "5.2.7.010 Notice of Election.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.7.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.8 Election Procedures 5.2.8.010 Polling Place. 5.2.8.020 Hours of Voting. 5.2.8.030 Fifty (50) Foot Limit. 5.2.8.040 Maintaining Peace at Polling Place. 5.2.8.050 Method of Voting. 5.2.8.060 Counting the Ballots. 5.2.8.070 Posting and Notice of Election Results. 5.2.8.080 Tie Votes. 5.2.8.090 Spoiled Ballots. 5.2.8.100 Unused Ballots. 5.2.8.110 Rejected Ballots. 5.2.8.120 Recounts. 5.2.8.130 Other Matters Decided by the Election Commission.", "num": "5.2.8", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8", "title": "Part 5.2.8 Election Procedures", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.010 Polling Place. There shall be one (1) polling place located at the Pueblo. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.010", "title": "5.2.8.010 Polling Place.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.020 Hours of Voting. The polls shall be open at the polling place from 7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. Voters in line at the polling place but unable to cast their ballots before 7:00 p.m. shall be allowed to finish voting. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.020", "title": "5.2.8.020 Hours of Voting.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.030 Fifty (50) Foot Limit. No persons except members of the Election Commission shall be allowed to remain within fifty (50) feet of a polling place, except while actually voting. No campaigning or placement of campaign materials shall be allowed within a fifty (50) foot perimeter around the polling place. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.030", "title": "5.2.8.030 Fifty (50) Foot Limit.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.040 Maintaining Peace at Polling Place. The Election Commission or Bailiff shall keep the peace and protect the voting place by preventing disturbances at the polling place and interference with persons desiring to vote. This includes the authority to remove unruly or uncooperative persons from the polling place or from within the fifty (50) foot limit. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.040", "title": "5.2.8.040 Maintaining Peace at Polling Place.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.050 Method of Voting. (a) Each prospective voter, upon being identified as being on the final list of eligible voters, shall be handed an unused ballot by an Election Commissioner and shall sign his or her name on a form kept for that purpose to acknowledge that he or she has received the ballot. (b) The voter shall vote in privacy and shall place a mark opposite the name of the candidate or issue for whom he or she is voting. The ballot shall be placed in a locked ballot box. (c) The Election Commission may utilize electronic voting machines to conduct elections. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.050", "title": "5.2.8.050 Method of Voting.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.060 Counting the Ballots. (a) At the close of the polls, the Election Commission shall count the votes as marked on the ballots. At the end of the tally, the Election Commission shall determine the total votes cast for each candidate or issue. These unofficial results shall be written down, together with the number of spoiled, rejected and unused ballots, and shall be certified by each member of the Election Commission by signing his or her name thereto. (b) The tallying of the votes shall be open for public observation, but the public must remain at a distance of at least ten (10) feet from the Election Commissioners and the ballot box. The public must remain quiet and in no way interfere with the orderly tallying of the ballots. If order cannot be kept, the Election Commission shall halt the tallying until such time order has been restored. (c) At the end of the tally, the Election Commission shall place the counted ballots, any spoiled ballots and any rejected ballots, in the ballot box. The ballot box shall be locked and sealed. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.060", "title": "5.2.8.060 Counting the Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.070 Posting and Notice of Election Results. (a) The unofficial results of an Election shall be posted at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public locations at the earliest possible time after the tallying of the votes. The Election Commission shall notify the Governor and Lieutenant Governor of the unofficial results. (b) The Election Commission shall certify the election results as \"official\" at the end of the election challenge period if no challenge was properly and timely filed, or at the completion of the election challenge appeal process. The Election Commission shall post the official election results at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public locations, along with notice to the Governor and Lieutenant Governor, at the earliest possible time after the end of the challenge period or the completion of the challenge appeal process. (c) In the event of a recount, the Election Commission shall post the results of the recount of ballots at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public locations, along with notice to the Governor and Lieutenant Governor. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.070", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.070", "title": "5.2.8.070 Posting and Notice of Election Results.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.080 Tie Votes. A tie vote for candidates in any Election shall be decided by a game of chance administered by the Election Commission at the earliest possible time after the election upon notice to the candidates, with notice posted at the polling place, the Governor's Office, the Tewa Center, public bulletin boards, and other public places. This does not prevent the tied candidates from participating in the game of chance immediately following the vote count if both candidates are available and agree to conduct the tie-breaker at that time. In such instance, posting of notice shall not be required. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.080", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.080", "title": "5.2.8.080 Tie Votes.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.090", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.090 Spoiled Ballots. If a voter spoils a ballot and obtains another ballot, the spoiled ballot shall be marked \"SPOILED\". Each member of the Election Commission shall sign his or her name below this marking and the spoiled ballot shall be secured by the Election Commission. All spoiled ballots shall be placed in the ballot box at the end of the tallying. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.090", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.090", "title": "5.2.8.090 Spoiled Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.090"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.100", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.100 Unused Ballots. Ballots unused at the end of the voting shall be marked \"UNUSED\" and shall be placed in the ballot box at the end of the tallying. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.100", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.100", "title": "5.2.8.100 Unused Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.100"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.110", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.110 Rejected Ballots. If, during the tallying of the votes, the Election Commission is unable to determine from the ballot the choice of the voter, the ballot shall be rejected. All rejected ballots shall be placed in the ballot box at the end of the tallying. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.110", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.110", "title": "5.2.8.110 Rejected Ballots.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.110"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.120", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.120 Recounts. Any Candidate for elective office shall have the right to request a recount of the election results within three (3) days of the election. Upon receipt of a written request for a recount, the Election Commission shall promptly conduct a recount and shall post the results of such recount in accordance with Section 7.C. above. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.120", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.120", "title": "5.2.8.120 Recounts.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.120"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.130", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.8.130 Other Matters Decided by the Election Commission. The Election Commission shall control all aspects of elections conducted by the Pueblo regardless of any Federal or State laws. Any other election matters not specifically addressed in this law shall be decided by the Election Commission. The decision of the Election Commission shall be final. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.8.130", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.8|5.2.8.130", "title": "5.2.8.130 Other Matters Decided by the Election Commission.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.8.130"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.9", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.9 Challenges to the Election Results 5.2.9.010 Election Results Challenge Process.", "num": "5.2.9", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.9", "title": "Part 5.2.9 Challenges to the Election Results", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.9"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.9.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.9.010 Election Results Challenge Process. (a) Any eligible voter of the Pueblo shall have the right to challenge the results of any election within three (3) days of the posting of the unofficial election results by filing a written challenge with the Election Commission. (1) A challenge must contain the following information: (A) The voter's name, address, telephone number and email address (if any); (B) Sworn, notarized statement of facts alleged to show the violation or reason for the challenge that includes: (i) Section of Election Law that was violated; (ii) Identity of individual(s) involved in alleged violation(s); (iii) Date, time and location of violation(s); (iv) Estimated number of votes affected by the alleged violation(s); (v) Name and telephone number of any witnesses to the alleged violation(s). (C) Relief requested from the Election Commission. (b) The Election Commission shall make a determination on all election challenges within five (5) days of receipt of a challenge and the decision of the Election Commission shall be final for purposes of judicial review. (1) The following shall be used by the Election Commission when considering submitted complaints: (A) No official election shall be voided by decision of the Election Commission in response to a complaint unless the voter clearly demonstrates that: (i) violation(s) of the Election Law occurred; and (ii) said violation(s) would have changed the outcome of the election. (c) Following receipt and review of a properly executed challenge and such other evidence before the Election Commission, the Election Commission shall issue findings: (1) To dismiss the challenge, or (2) To acknowledge the merit of the challenge but to reaffirm the election in question, or (3) To acknowledge the merit of the challenge and to void the election in question. The Election Commission shall notify the voter of its decision and shall post the decision at appropriate public places. (d) If the voter who brought the challenge is not satisfied with the Election Commission's decision, he or she shall have the right to appeal the final decision made by the Election Commission by filing suit in the Trial Court of the Pueblo within five (5) days of the date of the decision of the Election Commission. The voter may not submit any evidence that was not before the Election Commission. A decision on an election challenge made by the Supreme Court of the Pueblo shall be final and shall not be subject to any further review by any other person or entity. (1) A Court shall not overturn the decision of the Election Commission unless it is shown by clear and convincing evidence that the Petitioner (Voter) is clearly entitled to the relief requested because the Election Commission decision was: (A) arbitrary and capricious; (B) an abuse of discretion; (C) not supported by the evidence of record; or (D) contrary to the Pueblo's law. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.9.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.9|5.2.9.010", "title": "5.2.9.010 Election Results Challenge Process.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.9.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.10", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.10 Recall Elections 5.2.10.010 Recall Elections.", "num": "5.2.10", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.10", "title": "Part 5.2.10 Recall Elections", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.10"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.10.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.10.010 Recall Elections. (a) Recall elections shall be conducted in accordance with the ELECTIONS AND VOTING provision SECTION 4. REMOVAL AND RECALL of the Agreement which states: Recall The people reserve the power to subject any member of the Council or the Governor to a recall election, and the Election Commission shall hold a Recall Election upon a petition signed by at least fifty percent (50%) of the voters. A simple majority of the votes cast shall decide the outcome of the Recall Election. No more than two Members of the Council can be subjected to a Recall Process at one time, and any resulting vacancy shall be filled before any subsequent Recall Election can be held. (b) Upon written request, the Election Commission shall issue an official Recall Petition form to a petitioner. A recall petition shall include a legible name and date of each person signing such petition. A completed Recall Petition shall be filed with the Election Commission. (c) Petitioners have forty-five (45) days to submit a completed petition to the Election Commission. (d) For purposes of determining the validity of the recall petition, fifty percent (50%) of the eligible voters means fifty percent (50%) of all of the eligible voters of the Pueblo who are eighteen (18) or older at the time they signed the petition, and does not mean the number of voters who voted in the last election. (e) An individual who voluntarily places his or her signature on a petition shall not be allowed to later withdraw or remove their signature from the petition. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.10.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.10|5.2.10.010", "title": "5.2.10.010 Recall Elections.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.10.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.11", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.11 Referendum Elections 5.2.11.010 Referendum Election Process.", "num": "5.2.11", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.11", "title": "Part 5.2.11 Referendum Elections", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.11"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.11.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.11.010 Referendum Election Process. (a) Referendum elections shall be conducted in accordance with the ELECTIONS AND VOTING provision SECTION 6. REFERENDUM of the Agreement which states: The people reserve the power to subject any law to a binding referendum election and the Election Commission shall hold a Referendum Election upon a petition signed by at least fifty percent (50%) of the voters. A simple majority of the votes cast shall decide the outcome of the Referendum Election. (b) Upon written request, the Election Commission shall issue an official Referendum Petition form to a petitioner. A referendum petition shall include a legible name and date of each person signing such petition. A completed Referendum Petition shall be filed with the Election Commission. (c) A tribal member shall have fifteen (15) days after an Act of the Council is signed into law by the Governor or veto override by the Council to request a referendum petition. (d) Petitioners have forty-five (45) days to submit a completed petition to the Election Commission. (e) For purposes of determining the validity of the referendum petition, fifty percent (50%) of the eligible voters means fifty percent (50%) of all of the eligible voters of the Pueblo who are eighteen (18) or older at the time they signed the petition, and does not mean the number of voters who voted in the last election. (f) An individual who voluntarily places his or her signature on a petition shall not be allowed to later withdraw or remove their signature from the petition. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.11.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.11|5.2.11.010", "title": "5.2.11.010 Referendum Election Process.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.11.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.12 Elections to Fill Vacancies 5.2.12.010 Special Election to Fill Vacancy. 5.2.12.020 Vacancy Certification and Election Process. 5.2.12.030 Special Provisions where Elected Official Causes Special Election and Runs as Candidate in Subsequent Special Election.", "num": "5.2.12", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.12", "title": "Part 5.2.12 Elections to Fill Vacancies", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.12.010 Special Election to Fill Vacancy. (a) A Special Election shall be held in accordance with the ELECTIONS AND VOTING provision, Section 5. VACANCIES of the Agreement which states: The Election Commission shall certify all vacancies. Vacancy shall result from removal, recall, physical incapacity, or any circumstance that makes holding office impossible for more than thirty (30) days. (b) A vacancy in an elected office shall also occur when the office holder voluntarily resigns from their position. Such resignation makes holding the office impossible for more than thirty (30) days since the office holder who resigns intends to voluntarily leave their position from the point of resignation forward. (1) Proof of voluntary resignation is a written letter or email correspondence that is offered as the office holder's intent to leave their position. (2) When an office holder voluntarily resigns, such resignation becomes effective immediately, and no formal acceptance by either the Council or Governor is necessary to make the resignation effective. (3) When an office holder voluntarily resigns, the resigning office holder shall notify the Election Commission of the voluntary resignation, or the Council or Governor shall notify the Election Commission in the event the resigning office holder provides notice of their resignation to either the Council or Governor. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.12.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.12|5.2.12.010", "title": "5.2.12.010 Special Election to Fill Vacancy.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.12.020 Vacancy Certification and Election Process. (a) The Election Commission shall certify all vacancies, regardless of how the vacancy occurred. (b) The Election Commission shall call a Special Election to be held within thirty (30) days of the Election Commission's certification of the vacancy. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.12.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.12|5.2.12.020", "title": "5.2.12.020 Vacancy Certification and Election Process.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.12.030 Special Provisions where Elected Official Causes Special Election and Runs as Candidate in Subsequent Special Election. (a) In the event that an elected official voluntarily creates a vacancy in their position for any reason, and then submits their name and intent to run in the Special Election to be held to fill the vacancy caused by that elected official, that candidate shall pay an election fee equal to one-half (1/2) of the cost of the Special Election. Such election fee must be paid in full before the former elected official is placed on the list of candidates for the Special Election. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.12.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.12|5.2.12.030", "title": "5.2.12.030 Special Provisions where Elected Official Causes Special Election and Runs as Candidate in Subsequent Special Election.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.12.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.13", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.13 Oath of Office 5.2.13.010 Oath of Office.", "num": "5.2.13", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.13", "title": "Part 5.2.13 Oath of Office", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.13"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.13.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.13.010 Oath of Office. After the Election Commission has certified the results of the election and the winners are announced, and any challenges are finally decided, a Justice or Judge shall administer the oath of office on January 2 at a location within the Pueblo's lands. An Acknowledgement of the Oath of Office form shall be signed by the candidate, Justice or Judge and the Commission Chair and retained by the Commission. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.13.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.13|5.2.13.010", "title": "5.2.13.010 Oath of Office.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.13.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.14", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 5.2.14 Amendment and Severability 5.2.14.010 Amendment. 5.2.14.020 Severability.", "num": "5.2.14", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.14", "title": "Part 5.2.14 Amendment and Severability", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.14"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.14.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.14.010 Amendment. The Council may amend this law upon a majority vote of the Council in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement for making laws. The Election Commission may submit to the Council suggested amendments to the law as deemed necessary. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.14.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.14|5.2.14.010", "title": "5.2.14.010 Amendment.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.14.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.14.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 5.2.14.020 Severability. The provisions of this law are severable and if any part or provision shall be held void by any court of competent jurisdiction, the decision of the court so holding shall not affect or impair any of the remaining parts or provisions of this law. ( June 11, 2019, SI-R19-011 .)", "num": "5.2.14.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|5|5.2|5.2.14|5.2.14.020", "title": "5.2.14.020 Severability.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/5.2.14.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Title 6 ADMINISTRATION Chapter 6.1 Department of Tribal Administration \u00a7\u00a7 6.1.1.010 \u2013 6.1.1.120 Chapter 6.2 Department of Accounting and Finance \u00a7\u00a7 6.2.1.010 \u2013 6.2.4.040 Chapter 6.3 Budgets \u00a7\u00a7 6.3.1.010 \u2013 6.3.29.040 Chapter 6.4 Fiscal Procedures \u00a7\u00a7 6.4.1.010 \u2013 6.4.4.020 Chapter 6.5 Grant and Contracts \u00a7\u00a7 6.5.1.010 \u2013 6.5.37.040 Chapter 6.6 Investments \u00a7\u00a7 6.6.1.010 \u2013 6.6.12.040 Chapter 6.7 Personnel Policies \u00a7\u00a7 6.7.1.010 \u2013 6.7.5.040 Chapter 6.8 Department of Project Management \u00a7\u00a7 6.8.1.010 \u2013 6.8.1.070 Chapter 6.9 Tewa Language Department \u00a7\u00a7 6.9.1.010 \u2013 6.9.1.070", "num": "6", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6", "title": "Title 6 ADMINISTRATION", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 6.1 Department of Tribal Administration Part 6.1.1 Department of Tribal Administration Enabling Act \u00a7\u00a7 6.1.1.010 \u2013 6.1.1.120", "num": "6.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1", "title": "Chapter 6.1 Department of Tribal Administration", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.1.1 Department of Tribal Administration Enabling Act 6.1.1.010 Findings 6.1.1.020 Short Title 6.1.1.030 Definitions 6.1.1.040 Purpose 6.1.1.050 Findings 6.1.1.060 General Policy 6.1.1.070 Organization of the Department of Tribal Administration 6.1.1.080 Office of the Tribal Administrator Goals and Objectives 6.1.1.090 Legal Counsel 6.1.1.100 Amendment 6.1.1.110 Sovereign Immunity 6.1.1.120 Severability Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R12-027, dated June 18, 2012.", "num": "6.1.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1", "title": "Part 6.1.1 Department of Tribal Administration Enabling Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.010 Findings (a) Annual Budget items may only be included if they have first been authorized by law as required by Section 5(a)(ii)(A) of the Agreement; (b) The Council finds that reorganizing the structure of governmental departments and Programs will promote efficiency within the Tribe; (c) The Council finds that establishing a Department of Tribal Administration will assist the Tribe in oversight of all departments, programs, and related projects of the Pueblo. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.010", "title": "6.1.1.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.020 Short Title (a) This enactment shall be known as the Department of Tribal Administration Enabling Act (\"Act\"). ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.020", "title": "6.1.1.020 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.030 Definitions (a) \"Agreement\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso governing Agreement. (b) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (c) \"Pueblo\"means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.030", "title": "6.1.1.030 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.040 Purpose (a) The Purpose of the Act is to establish the Department of Tribal Administration. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.040", "title": "6.1.1.040 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.050 Findings (a) The Council hereby finds and declares that: (1) reorganizing the structure of governmental departments and programs will promote efficiency within the Tribe; and (2) establishing a Department of Tribal Administration will assist the Tribe in achieving oversight of all departments, programs, and related projects of the Pueblo. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.050", "title": "6.1.1.050 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.060 General Policy (a) Department of Tribal Administration. This act shall establish a Department of Tribal Administration to oversee all departments, programs, and related projects of the Pueblo. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.060", "title": "6.1.1.060 General Policy", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.070 Organization of the Department of Tribal Administration (a) There shall be one Tribal Administrator in the Department of Tribal Administration who shall oversee and provide general supervision of all departments under the direction of the Governor. The Office of the Tribal Administrator shall include administrative staff as necessary. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.070", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.070", "title": "6.1.1.070 Organization of the Department of Tribal Administration", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.080 Office of the Tribal Administrator Goals and Objectives (a) The overall goal of the Office of the Tribal Administrator is to provide oversight of all departments, programs, and related projects of the Pueblo. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.080", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.080", "title": "6.1.1.080 Office of the Tribal Administrator Goals and Objectives", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.090", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.090 Legal Counsel (a) The Governor shall be authorized to employ and pay an attorney or a law firm to provide legal advice and assistance to the Governor within the budgetary constraints set by the Council in the Annual Budget, so long as the attorney or law firm is/are licensed member(s) in good standing of a State bar association; provided, that no attorney or law firm shall be employed in any capacity by the Pueblo if the attorney, or if any attorney presently or formerly associated with the law firm in any capacity, is the subject of any pending criminal charge in any court and the criminal charge is related to alleged conduct of the attorney, whether directly or indirectly, in his or her role as any attorney. Such attorney or law firm shall have in effect legal malpractice insurance at a minimum amount of $1,000,000.00. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.090", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.090", "title": "6.1.1.090 Legal Counsel", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.090"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.100", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.100 Amendment (a) The Council may amend this enabling act or reorganize the Office of the Tribal Administrator at any time upon majority vote of the Council. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.100", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.100", "title": "6.1.1.100 Amendment", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.100"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.110", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.110 Sovereign Immunity (a) Nothing in this Act waives the sovereign immunity of the Pueblo or any of its representatives, officers, or employees. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.110", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.110", "title": "6.1.1.110 Sovereign Immunity", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.110"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.120", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.1.1.120 Severability (a) If a court of competent jurisdiction finds any provision of this Act to be invalid or illegal under applicable tribal and/or federal law, such provision shall be severed from this Act and the remainder of this Act shall remain in full force and effect. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-027 .)", "num": "6.1.1.120", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.1|6.1.1|6.1.1.120", "title": "6.1.1.120 Severability", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.1.1.120"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 6.2 Department of Accounting and Finance Part 6.2.1 Department of Accounting and Finance Enabling Act \u00a7\u00a7 6.2.1.010 \u2013 6.2.1.110 Part 6.2.2 The Accounting Policies &amp; Procedures Manual Act of 2017 \u00a7\u00a7 6.2.2.010 \u2013 6.2.2.040 Part 6.2.3 Audit Authorization, Acceptance, and Responsibility Act \u00a7\u00a7 6.2.3.010 \u2013 6.2.3.040 Part 6.2.4 Accounting Policies and Procedures Manual Amendments of 2022 \u00a7\u00a7 6.2.4.010 \u2013 6.2.4.040", "num": "6.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2", "title": "Chapter 6.2 Department of Accounting and Finance", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.2.1 Department of Accounting and Finance Enabling Act 6.2.1.010 Findings 6.2.1.020 Short Title 6.2.1.030 Definitions 6.2.1.040 Purpose 6.2.1.050 Findings 6.2.1.060 General Policy 6.2.1.070 Organization of the Department of Accounting and Finance 6.2.1.080 Department of Accounting and Finance Goals and Objectives 6.2.1.090 Amendment 6.2.1.100 Sovereign Immunity 6.2.1.110 Severability Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R12-020, dated June 18, 2012.", "num": "6.2.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1", "title": "Part 6.2.1 Department of Accounting and Finance Enabling Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.010 Findings (a) Annual budget items may only be included if they have first been authorized by law as required by Section 5(a)(ii)(A) of the Agreement; (b) The Council finds that reorganizing the structure of governmental departments and programs will promote efficiency within the Tribe; (c) The Council finds that establishing a Department of Accounting and Finance will assist the Tribe in providing direction and management of the Pueblo's financial matters. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.010", "title": "6.2.1.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.020 Short Title (a) This enactment shall be known as the Department of Accounting and Finance Enabling Act (\"Act\"). ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.020", "title": "6.2.1.020 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.030 Definitions (a) \"Agreement\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso governing Agreement. (b) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (c) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.030", "title": "6.2.1.030 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.040 Purpose (a) The Purpose of the Act is to establish the Department of Accounting and Finance. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.040", "title": "6.2.1.040 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.050 Findings (a) The Council hereby finds and declares that: (1) reorganizing the structure of governmental departments and programs will promote efficiency within the Tribe; and (2) establishing a Department of Accounting and Finance will assist the Tribe in providing direction and management of the Pueblo's financial matters. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.050", "title": "6.2.1.050 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.060 General Policy (a) Department of Accounting and Finance. This act shall establish the Department of Accounting and Finance to direct and manage the Pueblo's financial matters. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.060", "title": "6.2.1.060 General Policy", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.070 Organization of the Department of Accounting and Finance (a) There shall be a Director of the Department of Accounting and Finance who shall oversee the general supervision of the department. (b) In order to promote efficiency within the Department of Accounting and Finance, program offices will be established as necessary. A program director shall oversee the general supervision of the each program office and shall report to the Director of Accounting and Finance. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.070", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.070", "title": "6.2.1.070 Organization of the Department of Accounting and Finance", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.080 Department of Accounting and Finance Goals and Objectives (a) The overall goals of the Accounting Department (\"Department\") are to manage the financial affairs of the Pueblo. The Department shall oversee the operations for all accounting departments, programs, and projects and shall effectively manage all revenues, assets and property of the Pueblo. The Department shall ensure compliance with federal, state, and any additional reporting requirements. The Department shall implement the generally accepted accounting principles (\"GAAP\") and provide technical advice and assistance as requested. The Department shall address internal control matters, manage the annual audit process, and maintain and operate the Indirect cost pool. The Department shall keep the Governor and Council informed of the Tribe's financial position by providing monthly financial statements to the Governor and Council. The Department shall recommend policy changes to improve the Tribe's accounting policies, procedures, and practices. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.080", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.080", "title": "6.2.1.080 Department of Accounting and Finance Goals and Objectives", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.090", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.090 Amendment (a) The Council may amend this enabling act or reorganize the Department of Accounting and Finance at any time upon majority vote of the Council. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.090", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.090", "title": "6.2.1.090 Amendment", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.090"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.100", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.100 Sovereign Immunity (a) Nothing in this Act waives the sovereign immunity of the Pueblo or any of its representatives, officers, or employees. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.100", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.100", "title": "6.2.1.100 Sovereign Immunity", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.100"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.110", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.1.110 Severability (a) If a court of competent jurisdiction finds any provision of this Act to be invalid or illegal under applicable tribal and/or federal law, such provision shall be severed from this Act and the remainder of this Act shall remain in full force and effect. ( June 18, 2012, SI-R12-020 .)", "num": "6.2.1.110", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.1|6.2.1.110", "title": "6.2.1.110 Severability", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.1.110"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.2.2 The Accounting Policies &amp; Procedures Manual Act of 2017 6.2.2.010 Short Title 6.2.2.020 Purpose 6.2.2.030 Findings 6.2.2.040 Authorization to Implement the Accounting Policies and Procedures Manual", "num": "6.2.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.2", "title": "Part 6.2.2 The Accounting Policies & Procedures Manual Act of 2017", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.2.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as, \"THE ACCOUNTING POLICIES &amp; PROCEDURES MANUAL ACT OF 2017 (\"Act\").\" ( November 4, 2017, SI-R17-034 .)", "num": "6.2.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.2|6.2.2.010", "title": "6.2.2.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.2.020 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to authorize the Governor, in consultation with the Controller, to implement the Accounting Policies &amp; Procedures Manual. ( November 4, 2017, SI-R17-034 .)", "num": "6.2.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.2|6.2.2.020", "title": "6.2.2.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.2.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) The Pueblo has operated its government in a fiscally prudent manner and has, over the years, developed a sophisticated automated financial management system. (b) The Pueblo must ensure that its books of account are prepared to conform to sound accounting principles and practices. (c) The Council and Governor require accurate and timely financial reports on a monthly basis to ensure sound financial management and to satisfy their fiduciary responsibilities. (d) The on-going financial well-being of the Pueblo requires accountable use of funds and other resources in accordance with Federal and State regulations and Grant requirements. (e) All Pueblo employees and agents have a role to play in the implementation and maintenance of sound financial management practices. ( November 4, 2017, SI-R17-034 .)", "num": "6.2.2.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.2|6.2.2.030", "title": "6.2.2.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.2.040 Authorization to Implement the Accounting Policies and Procedures Manual (a) The Council hereby authorizes and directs the Governor, based on the recommendation of the Controller, to implement the Manual as approved. (b) Implementation is to be supported by formal training for all affected Pueblo employees, and by periodic review and modification as necessary. ( November 4, 2017, SI-R17-034 .)", "num": "6.2.2.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.2|6.2.2.040", "title": "6.2.2.040 Authorization to Implement the Accounting Policies and Procedures Manual", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.2.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.2.3 Audit Authorization, Acceptance, and Responsibility Act 6.2.3.010 Short Title 6.2.3.020 Purpose 6.2.3.030 Findings 6.2.3.040 Contract Authorization for Independent Auditors", "num": "6.2.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.3", "title": "Part 6.2.3 Audit Authorization, Acceptance, and Responsibility Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.3.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"AUDIT AUTHORIZATION, ACCEPTANCE, AND RESPONSIBILITY ACT (\"Act\").\" ( July 29, 2020, SI-R20-013 .)", "num": "6.2.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.3|6.2.3.010", "title": "6.2.3.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.3.020 Purpose The purpose of this act is to: (a) Authorize and direct the Governor to complete an external financial audit of the Pueblo in accordance with the requirements of the Governing Agreement; and (b) Authorize the Governor to procure an independent licensed auditor; and (c) Require the Governor to provide a copy of the annual audit report to the Council and to direct the auditor to make an in-person presentation to the Council, and to assign to the Governor the responsibility to accept or reject the annual audit prepared by the auditors; and (d) Require the Governor to develop and implement a plan to adequately address all audit findings identified in the annual audit. ( July 29, 2020, SI-R20-013 .)", "num": "6.2.3.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.3|6.2.3.020", "title": "6.2.3.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.3.030 Findings The Council hereby declares that: (a) the Governing Agreement requires the Pueblo to conduct an annual financial audit by an independent auditor; and (b) the annual audit is an important indicator of the Pueblo's accounting practices and financial health, and is a valuable tool to safeguard the financial assets of the Pueblo; and (c) the Governor of the Pueblo oversees and directs the Accounting Department personnel, engages the independent auditor, and is vested with the executive authority and responsibility to ensure that the annual audit is conducted and accepted by the Pueblo and that a plan to address all audit findings is developed and implemented. ( July 29, 2020, SI-R20-013 .)", "num": "6.2.3.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.3|6.2.3.030", "title": "6.2.3.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.3.040 Contract Authorization for Independent Auditors (a) The Governor is hereby authorized to negotiate and execute a contract with external and independent qualified auditors to conduct and complete an annual financial audit for the Pueblo in accordance with the requirements of the Governing Agreement. (b) The Governor shall provide a copy of the annual audit report to the Council prior to Governor's acceptance, and shall direct the auditor to make an in-person presentation to the Council regarding the annual audit. ( July 29, 2020, SI-R20-013 .)", "num": "6.2.3.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.3|6.2.3.040", "title": "6.2.3.040 Contract Authorization for Independent Auditors", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.3.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.2.4 Accounting Policies and Procedures Manual Amendments of 2022 6.2.4.010 Short Title 6.2.4.020 Purpose 6.2.4.030 Findings 6.2.4.040 Approval", "num": "6.2.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.4", "title": "Part 6.2.4 Accounting Policies and Procedures Manual Amendments of 2022", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.4.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"ACCOUNTING POLICY AND PROCEDURES MANUAL AMENDMENTS OF 2022.\" ( May 11, 2022, SI-R22-003 .)", "num": "6.2.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.4|6.2.4.010", "title": "6.2.4.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.4.020 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to approve amendments of the Accounting Policy and Procedures Manual. ( May 11, 2022, SI-R22-003 .)", "num": "6.2.4.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.4|6.2.4.020", "title": "6.2.4.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.4.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) The Council has enacted a 75-page, comprehensive Accounting Policy and Procedures Manual (\"Manual\") to govern the financial practices of the Pueblo. (b) The Finance Department and Governor have identified the need to amend the Manual to streamline certain accounting procedures and to clarify several accounting practices to bring greater efficiencies and cost-savings to the Pueblo. (c) The Finance Department, Tribal Administrator, and Governor have developed a set of proposed amendments to the Manual and have presented the proposed amendments to the Council for consideration and approval. ( May 11, 2022, SI-R22-003 .)", "num": "6.2.4.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.4|6.2.4.030", "title": "6.2.4.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.2.4.040 Approval The Council hereby approves and enacts the attached Accounting Policy and Procedures Manual amendments of 2022. ( May 11, 2022, SI-R22-003 .)", "num": "6.2.4.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.2|6.2.4|6.2.4.040", "title": "6.2.4.040 Approval", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.2.4.040"}
