{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.1 Act Authorizing the Governor to Enter into PL. 93-638 Contracts with the Bureau of Reclamation and Bureau of Indian Affairs to Fund the Aamodt Water Settlement Implementation Activities 6.5.1.010 Findings 6.5.1.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R12-041, dated September 15, 2012.", "num": "6.5.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.1", "title": "Part 6.5.1 Act Authorizing the Governor to Enter into PL. 93-638 Contracts with the Bureau of Reclamation and Bureau of Indian Affairs to Fund the Aamodt Water Settlement Implementation Activities", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.1.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo is a party to the federal water adjudication State v. Aamodt, U.S. District Court of New Mexico No. 66CV6639; (b) In 2006, after thirty-five years of litigation, and five years of negotiations, the Pueblo, the other three Pueblos, and other parties involved in the Aamodt case executed the Settlement Agreement (Jan. 19, 2006) to settle this water rights adjudication; (c) In 2010, the United States enacted the Aamodt Litigation Settlement Act, as part of the Claims Resolution Act of 2010, Pub. L. No. 11-291, Title VI, \u00a7\u00a7 601-626, 124 Stat. 3064, 3134-56 (2010), which was signed into law by the President on December 8, 2010 (\"Settlement Act\" or \"Act\"); (d) The Settlement Act approved the Settlement Agreement with certain changes, required the Pueblos to execute revised waivers and releases regarding their water rights defenses in the Pojoaque River Basin and any claims for more water rights in the Basin beyond what the Settlement Agreement provides (\"Waivers\"), and approved the Cost Sharing and System Integration Agreement (\"CSSIA\") previously prepared by the settlement parties; (e) The parties have now revised the Settlement Agreement (April 19, 2012) (\"Revised Agreement\") to reflect the terms of the Settlement Act, prepared Waivers consistent with the Act and completed the CSSIA as required by the Act; (f) The Revised Agreement, the Waivers and the CSSIA are consistent with the terms of the Act and provide for the present and future water needs of the Pueblo; (g) The completion and approval of the Revised Agreement, Waivers and the CSSIA are important milestones in completing the water adjudication involving the four Pueblos; (h) The Council recognizes that significant additional work will be needed for years ahead to complete the process described in the Settlement Act and the Revised Agreement; (i) The Bureau of Reclamation, at the Pueblo's request, approved a $30,000 award to help the Pueblo with implementing the Aamodt water settlement agreement, especially in carrying through its responsibilities under the federal National Environmental Protection Act; (j) The Bureau of Indian Affairs, at the Pueblo's request, said that it has approved an award to the Pueblo, but has not specified the amount to assist the Pueblo in carrying out the implementation of the Aamodt water settlement agreement activities. ( September 15, 2012, SI-R12-041 .)", "num": "6.5.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.1|6.5.1.010", "title": "6.5.1.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.1.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council authorizes and directs the Governor to sign on behalf of the Pueblo any 638 contract documents needed to fund the Aamodt settlement implementation activities, and to budget those funds for the Pueblo's Aamodt settlement implementation activities. ( September 15, 2012, SI-R12-041 .)", "num": "6.5.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.1|6.5.1.020", "title": "6.5.1.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.2 Authorizing Support For the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tewa Language Revitalization and Preservation Project 6.5.2.010 Findings 6.5.2.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R13-022, dated June 5, 2013.", "num": "6.5.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.2", "title": "Part 6.5.2 Authorizing Support For the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tewa Language Revitalization and Preservation Project", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.2.010 Findings (a) Since time immemorial the Pueblo de San Ildefonso has spoken the Tewa language; (b) It is of utmost concern to our Pueblo members that the Tewa language is not being reinforced as a primary language in our community; and it has always been the language through which the history, culture and governance have been passed on at the Pueblo de San Ildefonso; (c) In order for the Tewa language to survive as a primary language, Tewa language instruction must be implemented within all the learning environments of the Pueblo including the homes of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( June 5, 2013, SI-R13-022 .)", "num": "6.5.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.2|6.5.2.010", "title": "6.5.2.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.2.020 Be it resolved that: (a) The Tewa Language Revitalization and Preservation application be submitted and if funding is awarded, project activities be implemented to accomplish the goals and objectives during the thirty-six month project period; (b) The Tewa Language Committee be authorizes, in conjunction with the Pueblo Department of Education, and community to develop and present draft Resolutions on language issues to the Tribal Council for consideration and draft a Master Plan for language preservation into 2023. ( June 5, 2013, SI-R13-022 .)", "num": "6.5.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.2|6.5.2.020", "title": "6.5.2.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.3 Authorizing Tribal Management Grant Application 6.5.3.010 Findings 6.5.3.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R13-024, dated June 17, 2013.", "num": "6.5.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.3", "title": "Part 6.5.3 Authorizing Tribal Management Grant Application", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.3.010 Findings (a) The Santa Fe Service Unit Tribes are eligible under law to apply for federal grants and to contract services from the Indian Health Service for the benefit of our Tribal members under its authority for Public Law 93-638, the Indian Self-Determination Act; (b) The Santa Fe Service Unit Tribes intend to have a wide range of community health services available to tribal members under the direction of the Santa Fe Service Unit Health Board. ( June 17, 2013, SI-R13-024 .)", "num": "6.5.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.3|6.5.3.010", "title": "6.5.3.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.3.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.3.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby authorizes the Pueblo de Cochiti to apply for the Tribal Management Grant on behalf of the Santa Fe Service Unit Health Board for the purpose of conducting a feasibility study. ( June 17, 2013, SI-R13-024 .)", "num": "6.5.3.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.3|6.5.3.020", "title": "6.5.3.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.3.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.4 Authorizing Submittal of the FY 2013-2016 Johnson O'Malley Contract Application 6.5.4.010 Findings 6.5.4.020 6.5.4.030 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R13-029, dated July 29, 2013.", "num": "6.5.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.4", "title": "Part 6.5.4 Authorizing Submittal of the FY 2013-2016 Johnson O'Malley Contract Application", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.4.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo, by and through the United States Public Law 93-638, has contracted and administered key functions for assistance to the tribe through the Bureau of Indian Affairs and through the Bureau of Indian Education that include the Johnson O'Malley (JOM) program; (b) The Johnson O'Malley Act program funding provides programs to meet the special education needs of the Pueblo's eligible children, funding to administer the program and costs related to the Indian Education Committee; (c) The Pueblo currently operates and administers the JOM program under the Pueblo's Education Department in compliance with all components of the application for contract; (d) The Pueblo wishes to continue contracting JOM funding for the 3-year period, FY 2013-2016 to assist in meeting the needs of our children. ( July 29, 2013, SI-R13-029 .)", "num": "6.5.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.4|6.5.4.010", "title": "6.5.4.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.4.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves submittal of the Application for Contract for the Johnson O'Malley program for a three-year term, 2013-2016. ( July 29, 2013, SI-R13-029 .)", "num": "6.5.4.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.4|6.5.4.020", "title": "6.5.4.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.4.030 The Pueblo wishes to enter into a P.L. 93-638 Contract for these funds. ( July 29, 2013, SI-R13-029 .)", "num": "6.5.4.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.4|6.5.4.030", "title": "6.5.4.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.4.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.5", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.5 Authorization for 2014-2016 Early Childhood Program (BIE \u2013 Part B and C) 6.5.5.010 Findings 6.5.5.020", "num": "6.5.5", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.5", "title": "Part 6.5.5 Authorization for 2014-2016 Early Childhood Program (BIE \u2013 Part B and C)", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.5"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.5.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.5.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo, by and through the United States Public Law 93-638, has contracted and administered key functions for assistance to the tribe through the Bureau of Indian Affairs and through the Bureau of Indian Education that include the Early Childhood Program; (b) The Pueblo has been informed that funding is available through the Bureau of Indian Education (BIE) to allow the Early Childhood Program to operate for 2014-2016; (c) The Pueblo wishes to continue contracting Early Childhood funding for 2014-2016 to assist in meeting the needs of our children.", "num": "6.5.5.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.5|6.5.5.010", "title": "6.5.5.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.5.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.5.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.5.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves and authorizes the Governor to submit an application package to the Bureau of Indian Education to request 2014-2016 funds for the Early Childhood Program (Part B and C).", "num": "6.5.5.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.5|6.5.5.020", "title": "6.5.5.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.5.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.6 Support and Approval for Submission of Title VI Federal Application for Continued Funding for the ENIPC, Inc. Senior Citizens Program 6.5.6.010 Findings 6.5.6.020 6.5.6.030 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R13-047, dated December 2, 2013.", "num": "6.5.6", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.6", "title": "Part 6.5.6 Support and Approval for Submission of Title VI Federal Application for Continued Funding for the ENIPC, Inc. Senior Citizens Program", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.6.010 Findings (a) Eight Northern Indian Pueblos Council, Inc. (\"ENIPC\") was established to provide community-based services in the areas of education, employment and training, behavioral health, domestic violence counseling, senior services, environmental support services, child care provision, commodity distribution, women and infant services, and administrative support services; (b) The ENIPC, Inc. Senior Citizens Program currently provides nutritional meals to our homebound and congregate elders five days a week, and also provides respite caser, transportation, case management, health and wellness promotions, etc. on behalf of four of the Eight Northern Pueblos; Picuris, Pojoaque, Nambe and San Ildefonso Pueblos; (c) The 1978 Amendments to the Older Americans Act created Title VI, Grants for Indian Tribal Organizations, to promote the delivery of supportive and nutritional services for Indian elders that are comparable to the services provided under Title III of the Older Americans Act; (d) The Federal Application under Title VI is for continued Federal Funding with estimated funding of $391,911.13 to be received for FY April 1, 2014-March 31, 2017; (e) The ENIPC, Inc. Senior Citizens Program will apply for services required by the Older Americans Act Title VI to include: Nutrition, Information and Assistance, Other Support Services, Counseling/Support Groups/Training, Respite Care and Supplemental Services. ( December 2, 2013, SI-R13-047 .)", "num": "6.5.6.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.6|6.5.6.010", "title": "6.5.6.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.6.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council recognizes that the ENIPC, Inc. Senior Citizens Program requests support and approval for submission of the Title VI Federal Application for the continuation of funding and services delivered to the Pueblos of Picuris, Pojoaque, Nambe and San Ildefonso. ( December 2, 2013, SI-R13-047 .)", "num": "6.5.6.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.6|6.5.6.020", "title": "6.5.6.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.6.030 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso supports and approves the submission of the Title VI Federal Application for continued funding for the ENICP, Inc. Senior Citizen Program. ( December 2, 2013, SI-R13-047 .)", "num": "6.5.6.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.6|6.5.6.030", "title": "6.5.6.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.6.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.7", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.7 Act Authorizing the Governor to Enter Into a P.L. 93-638 Contract with the Bureau of Reclamation to Fund the Aamodt Water Settlement Implementation Activities 6.5.7.010 Findings 6.5.7.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R15-007, dated March 13, 2015.", "num": "6.5.7", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.7", "title": "Part 6.5.7 Act Authorizing the Governor to Enter Into a P.L. 93-638 Contract with the Bureau of Reclamation to Fund the Aamodt Water Settlement Implementation Activities", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.7"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.7.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.7.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo is a party to the federal water adjudication State v. Aamodt, U.S. District Court of New Mexico No. 66CV6639; (b) In 2006, after thirty-five years of litigation, and five years of negotiations, the Pueblo, the other three Pueblos, and other parties involved in the Aamodt case executed the Settlement Agreement (Jan. 19, 2006) to settle this water rights adjudication; (c) In 2010, the United States enacted the Aamodt Litigation Settlement Act, as part of the Claims Resolution Act of 2010, Pub. L. No. 11-291, Title VI, \u00a7\u00a7 601-626, 124 Stat. 3064, 3134-56 (2010), which was signed into law by the President on December 8, 2010 (\"Settlement Act\" or \"Act\"); (d) The Settlement Act approved the Settlement Agreement with certain changes, required the Pueblos to execute revised waivers and releases regarding their water rights defenses in the Pojoaque River Basin and any claims for more water rights in the Basin beyond what the Settlement Agreement provides (\"Waivers\"), and approved the Cost Sharing and System Integration Agreement (\"CSSIA\") previously prepared by the settlement parties; (e) The parties have now revised the Settlement Agreement (April 19, 2012) (\"Revised Agreement\") to reflect the terms of the Settlement Act, prepared Waivers consistent with the Act and completed the CSSIA as required by the Act; (f) The Revised Agreement, the Waivers and the CSSIA are consistent with the terms of the Act and provide for the present and future water needs of the Pueblo; (g) The completion and approval of the Revised Agreement, Waivers and the CSSIA are important milestones in completing the water adjudication involving the four Pueblos; (h) The Council recognizes that significant additional work will be needed for years ahead to complete the process described in the Settlement Act and the Revised Agreement; (i) The Bureau of Reclamation, at the Pueblo's request, approved a $30,000 award to help the Pueblo with implementing the Aamodt water settlement agreement, especially in carrying through its responsibilities under the federal National Environmental Protection Act; ( March 13, 2015, SI-R15-007 .)", "num": "6.5.7.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.7|6.5.7.010", "title": "6.5.7.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.7.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.7.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.7.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council authorizes and directs the Governor to sign on behalf of the Pueblo any 638 contract documents needed to fund the Aamodt settlement implementation activities, and to budget those funds for the Pueblo's Aamodt settlement implementation activities. ( March 13, 2015, SI-R15-007 .)", "num": "6.5.7.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.7|6.5.7.020", "title": "6.5.7.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.7.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.8", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.8 Act Authorizing a Contract with the Bureau of Reclamation For Funding Under the New Mexico Rio Grande Pueblos Irrigation Infrastructure Project 6.5.8.010 Findings 6.5.8.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R15-016, dated June 22, 2015.", "num": "6.5.8", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.8", "title": "Part 6.5.8 Act Authorizing a Contract with the Bureau of Reclamation For Funding Under the New Mexico Rio Grande Pueblos Irrigation Infrastructure Project", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.8"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.8.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.8.010 Findings (a) The agriculture lands at Pueblo de San Ildefonso are serviced by tribal ditches, diversion structures, and other irrigation infrastructure; (b) The Pueblo has consented to participate in Bureau of Reclamation's New Mexico Rio Grande Pueblos Irrigation Infrastructure Project (Public Law 111-11 Section 9106); (c) The Bureau of Reclamation has made funding available for the study required by Public Law 111-11 Section 9106, and may continue to make additional funds available in the future for this study and other purposes; (d) The Pueblo seeks to obtain funding from the Bureau of Reclamation for any and all studies. ( June 22, 2015, SI-R15-016 .)", "num": "6.5.8.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.8|6.5.8.010", "title": "6.5.8.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.8.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.8.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.8.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Council authorizes and directs the Governor to enter into and execute a contract with the Bureau of Reclamation pursuant to Public Law 93-638, as amended, in order to work cooperatively with the Bureau of Reclamation on irrigation infrastructure and other water resource improvement project studies at the Pueblo and to obtain any available funding for his work from the Bureau of Reclamation through the Public Law 93-638 (as amended) contract. ( June 22, 2015, SI-R15-016 .)", "num": "6.5.8.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.8|6.5.8.020", "title": "6.5.8.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.8.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.9 Authorizing Submittal of FY 2016-2019 Johnson O'Malley Contract Application 6.5.9.010 Findings 6.5.9.020 6.5.9.030 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R15-017, dated June 22, 2015.", "num": "6.5.9", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.9", "title": "Part 6.5.9 Authorizing Submittal of FY 2016-2019 Johnson O'Malley Contract Application", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.9.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo, by and through the United States Public Law 93-638, has contracted and administered key functions for assistance to the tribe through the Bureau of Indian Affairs and through the Bureau of Indian Education that include the Johnson O'Malley (JOM) program; (b) The Johnson O'Malley Act program funding provides programs to meet the special education needs of the Pueblo's eligible children, funding to administer the program and costs related to the Indian Education Committee; (c) The Pueblo currently operates and administers the JOM program under the Pueblo's Education Department in compliance with all components of the application for contract; (d) The Pueblo wishes to continue contracting JOM funding for the 3-year period, FY 2016-2019 to assist in meeting the needs of our children. ( June 22, 2015, SI-R15-017 .)", "num": "6.5.9.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.9|6.5.9.010", "title": "6.5.9.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.9.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves submittal of the Application for Contract for the Johnson O'Malley program for a three-year term, 2016-2019. ( June 22, 2015, SI-R15-017 .)", "num": "6.5.9.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.9|6.5.9.020", "title": "6.5.9.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.9.030 The Pueblo wishes to enter into a P.L. 93-638 Contract for these funds. ( June 22, 2015, SI-R15-017 .)", "num": "6.5.9.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.9|6.5.9.030", "title": "6.5.9.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.9.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.10 Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2015 6.5.10.010 Findings 6.5.10.020 Short Title 6.5.10.030 Definitions 6.5.10.040 Purpose 6.5.10.050 Findings 6.5.10.060 Grant Authorization Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R15-021, dated August 11, 2015.", "num": "6.5.10", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.10", "title": "Part 6.5.10 Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2015", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.10.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo receives significant funds through grants from governmental and private sources to operate the Pueblo's government and programs for the benefit of the People; (b) The Council supports and encourages the Governor and Executive Branch Departments to apply for and obtain available grant funds for the benefit of the Pueblo; (c) The Council finds it in the best interests of the Pueblo to provide the Governor and Executive Branch with an efficient and streamlined process to authorize the Pueblo to apply for and receive grant funds. ( August 11, 2015, SI-R15-021 .)", "num": "6.5.10.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.10|6.5.10.010", "title": "6.5.10.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.10.020 Short Title (a) This enactment shall be known as the \"Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2015\" or \"Act\". ( August 11, 2015, SI-R15-021 .)", "num": "6.5.10.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.10|6.5.10.020", "title": "6.5.10.020 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.10.030 Definitions (a) \"Agreement\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso governing Agreement. (b) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (c) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( August 11, 2015, SI-R15-021 .)", "num": "6.5.10.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.10|6.5.10.030", "title": "6.5.10.030 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.10.040 Purpose (a) The purpose of this Act is to provide the Governor and Executive Branch Departments with standing authority for one year to apply for and obtain grant funds for the Pueblo without the need to seek legal authorization from the Council for each grant application on a case-by-case basis. ( August 11, 2015, SI-R15-021 .)", "num": "6.5.10.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.10|6.5.10.040", "title": "6.5.10.040 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.10.050 Findings (a) The Council hereby finds and declares that: (1) the Pueblo receives significant funds through grants from governmental and private sources to operate the Pueblo's government and programs for the benefit of the People; and, (2) the Council supports and encourages the Governor and Executive Branch Departments to apply for and obtain available grant funds for the benefit of the Pueblo; and, (3) Section 5(a)(ii)(A) of the Governing Agreement permits the Council to make budget modifications without limitation at any time to obtain and expend new grant funds or to appropriate matching funds for new grants, which demonstrates the Pueblo's support for a streamlined and efficient grant application and expenditure process; and, (4) the Council finds it in the best interests of the Pueblo to provide the Governor and Executive Branch with an efficient and streamlined process to authorize the Pueblo to apply for, receive, and expend grant funds. ( August 11, 2015, SI-R15-021 .)", "num": "6.5.10.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.10|6.5.10.050", "title": "6.5.10.050 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.10.060 Grant Authorization (a) The Governor and Executive Branch Departments are hereby authorized to apply for and receive grant funds from any governmental or private source for the benefit of the Pueblo for FY 2015-2016; provided, that any matching funds that may be required to obtain a grant shall be separately appropriated in a budget or budget modification prior to the acceptance of such grant, and; provided further, that no grant shall be accepted unless such grant includes funds for the Pueblo's indirect costs or the Council has specifically authorized the acceptance of the grant without indirect costs. (b) The Governor is hereby authorized to prepare the necessary documents to apply for and obtain grant funds in a form and manner acceptable to the funding source, including the authorization to prepare and certify a Council Resolution that may be required by the funding source and such Resolution shall include the date and vote tallies of this Act and such Resolution shall not be required to be presented to the Council for another approval. (c) The Governor shall provide written notice to the Council of all grants applied for and/or obtained by the Pueblo on a quarterly basis. ( August 11, 2015, SI-R15-021 .)", "num": "6.5.10.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.10|6.5.10.060", "title": "6.5.10.060 Grant Authorization", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.10.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.11 Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2016 6.5.11.010 Findings 6.5.11.020 Short Title 6.5.11.030 Definitions 6.5.11.040 Purpose 6.5.11.050 Findings 6.5.11.060 Grant Authorization Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R16-019, dated September 8, 2016.", "num": "6.5.11", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.11", "title": "Part 6.5.11 Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2016", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.11.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo receives significant funds through grants from governmental and private sources to operate the Pueblo's government and programs for the benefit of the People; (b) The Council supports and encourages the Governor and Executive Branch Departments to apply for and obtain available grant funds for the benefit of the Pueblo; (c) The Council finds it is in the best interests of the Pueblo to provide the Governor and Executive Branch with an efficient and streamlined process to authorize the Pueblo to apply for and receive grants. (d) The Council hereby enacts the attached law entitled, \"Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2016.\" (e) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves and adopts this resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor, or his designee, to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this resolution. ( September 8, 2016, SI-R16-019 .)", "num": "6.5.11.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.11|6.5.11.010", "title": "6.5.11.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.11.020 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2016\" (\"Act\"). ( September 8, 2016, SI-R16-019 .)", "num": "6.5.11.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.11|6.5.11.020", "title": "6.5.11.020 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.11.030 Definitions (a) \"Agreement\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governing Agreement. (b) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (c) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( September 8, 2016, SI-R16-019 .)", "num": "6.5.11.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.11|6.5.11.030", "title": "6.5.11.030 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.11.040 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to provide the Governor and Executive Branch Departments with standing authority for two years to apply for and obtain grant funds for the Pueblo without the need to seek legal authorization from the Council for each grant application on a case-by-case basis. ( September 8, 2016, SI-R16-019 .)", "num": "6.5.11.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.11|6.5.11.040", "title": "6.5.11.040 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.11.050 Findings The Council hereby finds that: (a) The Pueblo receives significant funds through grants from governmental and private sources to operate the Pueblo's government and programs for the benefit of the People; (b) The Council supports and encourages the Governor and Executive Branch Departments to apply for and obtain available grant funds for the benefit of the Pueblo; (c) Section 5(a)(ii)(A) of the Governing Agreement permits the Council to make budget modifications without limitation at any time to obtain and expend new grants funds or to appropriate matching funds for new grants, which demonstrates the Pueblo's support for a streamlined and efficient application and expenditure process; and (d) The Council finds it in the best interest of the Pueblo to provide the Governor and Executive Branch with an efficient and streamlined process to authorize the Pueblo to apply for, receive, and expend grant funds. ( September 8, 2016, SI-R16-019 .)", "num": "6.5.11.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.11|6.5.11.050", "title": "6.5.11.050 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.11.060 Grant Authorization (a) The Governor and Executive Branch Departments are hereby authorized to apply for and receive grant funds from any governmental or private source for the benefit of the Pueblo for the Fiscal Years 2016-2017 and 2017-2018; provided that any matching funds that may be required to obtain a grant shall be separately appropriated in a budget or budget modification prior to the acceptance of such grant, and provided further, that no grant shall be accepted unless such grant includes funds for the Pueblo's indirect costs or the Council has specifically authorized the acceptance of the grant without indirect costs; (b) The Governor is hereby authorized to prepare the necessary documents to apply for and obtain grant funds in a form and manner acceptable to the funding source, including the authorization to prepare and certify a Council Resolution that may be required by the funding source and such Resolution shall include the date and vote tallies of this Act and such Resolution shall not be required to be presented to Council for another approval; (c) The Governor shall provide written notice to the Council of all grants applied for and/or obtained by the Pueblo on a quarterly basis. ( September 8, 2016, SI-R16-019 .)", "num": "6.5.11.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.11|6.5.11.060", "title": "6.5.11.060 Grant Authorization", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.11.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.12 Submittal For 23 Usc 202(C) Tribal Transportation Planning (66k) And The Tribal Transportation Program (TTP) (6k1) Funding 6.5.12.010 Findings 6.5.12.020 6.5.12.030 6.5.12.040 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R16-014, dated July 7, 2016.", "num": "6.5.12", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.12", "title": "Part 6.5.12 Submittal For 23 Usc 202(C) Tribal Transportation Planning (66k) And The Tribal Transportation Program (TTP) (6k1) Funding", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.12.010 Findings (a) Under the authority granted by Chapter 2 of Title 23, United States Code, as amended by the Fixing America's Surface Transportation (FAST) Act, Pub. L. 114-94, and in accordance with the requirements of Public Law (Pub. L.) 93-638, as amended; 25 CFR Part 170 (TTP Regulations); the Southwest Regional Office, Department of Transportation (SWRO-DOT) hereby offers the Tribe the first right-of-refusal to contract available funds; (b) To enter into contracts for the Tribal Transportation Planning (66K) or Tribal Transportation Program (TTP)(6K1) funds, the Tribe is required to submit to the SWRO-DOT the following documents: TTP Transportation Improvement Plan (TIP)/Control Schedule Statement of Work for Planning, Design, Construction, and/or Road Maintenance Supplemental Budget Tribal Resolution to Enter into a Pub. L. 93-638 Contract (c) The SWRO-DOT encourages the Tribe to submit the TTP-TIP/Control Schedule for review and approval; and (d) The Pueblo has prepared a TTP-TIP/Control Schedule for the following projects: IRR Projects: Transportation Planning Road Maintenance Supplemental NP 421 Hay Gan Po NP401 Povi Kaa Drive 23 U.S.C. 202(c): Planning ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-014 .)", "num": "6.5.12.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.12|6.5.12.010", "title": "6.5.12.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.12.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves the FY2016 Control Schedule, Proposed Statement of Work and Budgets [ATTACHED]; ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-014 .)", "num": "6.5.12.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.12|6.5.12.020", "title": "6.5.12.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.12.030 The Pueblo requests to enter into a new Pub. L. 93-638 contract with the funds; ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-014 .)", "num": "6.5.12.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.12|6.5.12.030", "title": "6.5.12.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.12.040 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves and adopts this resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor, or his designee, to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this resolution. ( July 7, 2016, SI-R16-014 .)", "num": "6.5.12.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.12|6.5.12.040", "title": "6.5.12.040", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.12.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.13", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.13 Submittal for 23 USC 202 Tribal Transportation Planning (66K) and the Tribal Transportation Program (TTP)(6K1) Funding 6.5.13.010 Findings 6.5.13.020 6.5.13.030 6.5.13.040", "num": "6.5.13", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.13", "title": "Part 6.5.13 Submittal for 23 USC 202 Tribal Transportation Planning (66K) and the Tribal Transportation Program (TTP)(6K1) Funding", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.13"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.13.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.13.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Pueblo') is a sovereign and self-governing Tribe, recognized as such by the United States of America. (b) The Council is authorized to make laws for the Pueblo de San Ildefonso pursuant to Section 5 of the Agreement, the governing document of the Pueblo. (c) Under the authority granted by Chapter 2 of Title 23, United States Code, as amended by the Fixing America's Surface Transportation (FAST) Act, Pub. L. 114-94, and in accordance with the requirements of Public Law (Pub. L.) 93-638, as amended; 25 CFR Part 170 (TTP Regulations); the Southwest Regional Office, Department of Transportation (SWRO-DOT) hereby offers the Tribe the first right-of-refusal to contract available funds. (d) To contract the Tribal Transportation Planning (66K) and the Tribal Transportation Program (TTP)(6K1) funds, the Tribe is required to submit to the SWRO-DOT the following documents: (1) TTP Tribal Transportation Improvement Plan (TTIP/Control Schedule) (2) Proposed Statement of Work for Planning, Design, Construction and/or Road Maintenance Supplemental (3) Budget (4) Tribal Resolution to Enter into a Pub. L. 93-638 contract (e) The SWRO-DOT encourages the Tribe to submit the TTP-TTIP/Control Schedule for review and approval. (f) The Pueblo has prepared a TTP-TTIP/Control Schedule for the following projects: (1) TTP Projects: (A) Planning (B) Road Maintenance Supplemental (C) NP421 Hay Gan Po (2) 23 U.S.C 204(j): (A) Planning ( September 1, 2017, SI-R17-024 .)", "num": "6.5.13.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.13|6.5.13.010", "title": "6.5.13.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.13.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.13.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.13.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves the FY2017-FY2021 Control Schedule, Statement of Work and Budgets (attached). ( September 1, 2017, SI-R17-024 .)", "num": "6.5.13.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.13|6.5.13.020", "title": "6.5.13.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.13.020"}
