{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.19 Approving the I.H.S. Community Health Representative Program Beginnig FY 2019 6.5.19.010 Findings 6.5.19.020 6.5.19.030", "num": "6.5.19", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.19", "title": "Part 6.5.19 Approving the I.H.S. Community Health Representative Program Beginnig FY 2019", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.19"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.19.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.19.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Pueblo') is a sovereign and self-governing Tribe, recognized as such by the United States of America. (b) The voters of the Pueblo approved a new Governing Agreement (\"Agreement\") for the Pueblo on November 19, 2011, and the Bureau of Indian Affairs approved the Agreement on December 21, 2011 pursuant to Federal law. (c) The Pueblo Council (\"Council\") is the duly constituted Legislative body acting for the Pueblo. (d) The Council is authorized to make laws for the Pueblo pursuant to Section 5 of the Agreement. (e) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso is currently a participant in the Public Health Service, Indian Health Service (IHS), Community Health Representative (CHR) Program. (f) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso acknowledges the benefits received from the CHR Program, both previous and current, in the area of community health care. (g) The Tribal Government recognizes the need to continue the CHR Program for a period of three years during which the program will provide those services for the community that cannot otherwise be provided. ( September 20, 2018, SI-R18-021 .)", "num": "6.5.19.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.19|6.5.19.010", "title": "6.5.19.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.19.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.19.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.19.020 (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council requests the Public Health Service, Indian Health Service, to enter a new contract agreement with the Pueblo de San Ildefonso for a Community Health Representative Program for a three year period beginning January 1, 2019 and ending December 31, 2021 , and (b) The authority granted by the Resolution shall remain in effect until withdrawn by the Tribal Council or until the term of the contract has expired, and that the Governor is the authorized agent for the Tribe and shall represent the Council in any negotiations, changes and/or approval of the contract agreement. ( September 20, 2018, SI-R18-021 .)", "num": "6.5.19.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.19|6.5.19.020", "title": "6.5.19.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.19.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.19.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.19.030 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves and adopts this Resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor, or his designee, to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this Resolution. ( September 20, 2018, SI-R18-021 .)", "num": "6.5.19.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.19|6.5.19.030", "title": "6.5.19.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.19.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.20 Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2018 6.5.20.010 Short Title 6.5.20.020 Definitions 6.5.20.030 Purpose 6.5.20.040 Findings 6.5.20.050 Grant Authorization", "num": "6.5.20", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.20", "title": "Part 6.5.20 Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2018", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.20.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"Grant Application and Authorization Act of 2018\" (\"Act\"). ( November 28, 2018, SI-R18-028 .)", "num": "6.5.20.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.20|6.5.20.010", "title": "6.5.20.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.20.020 Definitions (a) \"Agreement\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governing Agreement. (b) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (c) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( November 28, 2018, SI-R18-028 .)", "num": "6.5.20.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.20|6.5.20.020", "title": "6.5.20.020 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.20.030 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to provide the Governor and Executive Branch Departments with standing authority for two years to apply for and obtain grant funds for the Pueblo without the need to seek legal authorization from the Council for each grant application on a case-by-case basis. ( November 28, 2018, SI-R18-028 .)", "num": "6.5.20.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.20|6.5.20.030", "title": "6.5.20.030 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.20.040 Findings The Council hereby finds that: (a) The Pueblo receives significant funds through grants from governmental and private sources to operate the Pueblo's government and programs for the benefit of the People; and (b) The Council supports and encourages the Governor and Executive Branch Departments to apply for and obtain available grant funds for the benefit of the Pueblo; and (c) Section 5(a)(ii)(A) of the Governing Agreement permits the Council to make budget modifications without limitation at any time to obtain and expend new grants funds or to appropriate matching funds for new grants, which demonstrates the Pueblo's support for a streamlined and efficient application and expenditure process; and (d) The Council finds it in the best interest of the Pueblo to provide the Governor and Executive Branch with an efficient and streamlined process to authorize the Pueblo to apply for, receive, and expend grant funds. ( November 28, 2018, SI-R18-028 .)", "num": "6.5.20.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.20|6.5.20.040", "title": "6.5.20.040 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.20.050 Grant Authorization (a) The Governor and Executive Branch Departments are hereby authorized to apply for and receive grant funds from any governmental or private source for the benefit of the Pueblo through the end of the Fiscal Year 2024; provided that any matching funds that may be required to obtain a grant shall be separately appropriated in a budget or budget modification prior to the acceptance of such grant, and provided further, that no grant shall be accepted unless such grant includes funds for the Pueblo's indirect costs or the Council has specifically authorized the acceptance of the grant without indirect costs; and (b) The Governor is hereby authorized to prepare the necessary documents to apply for and obtain grant funds in a form and manner acceptable to the funding source, including the authorization to prepare and certify a Council Resolution that may be required by the funding source and such Resolution shall include the date and vote tallies of this Act and such Resolution shall not be required to be presented to Council for another approval; and (c) The Governor shall provide written notice to the Council of all grants applied for and/or obtained by the Pueblo on a quarterly basis. ( November 28, 2018, SI-R18-028 .)", "num": "6.5.20.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.20|6.5.20.050", "title": "6.5.20.050 Grant Authorization", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.20.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.21", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 6.5.21 Authorizing the 2019-2022 Contracting of the Indian Child Welfare Act (ICWA) Program through Public Law 93-638 6.5.21.010 Findings 6.5.21.020 6.5.21.030 6.5.21.040", "num": "6.5.21", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.21", "title": "Part 6.5.21 Authorizing the 2019-2022 Contracting of the Indian Child Welfare Act (ICWA) Program through Public Law 93-638", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.21"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.21.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.21.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Pueblo') is a sovereign and self-governing Tribe, recognized as such by the United States of America. (b) The Council is authorized to make laws for the Pueblo de San Ildefonso pursuant to Section 5 of the Agreement, the governing document of the pueblo. (c) The Pueblo, by and through United States Public Law 93-638, has contracted and administered key functions for assistance to the Tribe through the Bureau of Indian Affairs (BIA) to include the Indian Child Welfare Act (ICWA) Program. (d) The Indian Child Welfare Act (ICWA) Program, receives funding from the BIA to administer the ICWA Program in compliance with the respective scope of work. (e) The Pueblo wishes to continue contracting ICWA for a four (4)-year period, 2019 through 2022. ( January 30, 2019, SI-R19-002 .)", "num": "6.5.21.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.21|6.5.21.010", "title": "6.5.21.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.21.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.21.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 6.5.21.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves submission of the Application for Contract for the Indian Child Welfare Act (ICWA) Program for a four-year term (2019-2022). ( January 30, 2019, SI-R19-002 .)", "num": "6.5.21.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|6|6.5|6.5.21|6.5.21.020", "title": "6.5.21.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.5.21.020"}
