{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.020 Civil Rights Protection (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.020", "title": "12.1.1.020 Civil Rights Protection", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.030 Appointment of Civil Rights Commission There is hereby created a Civil Rights Commission which shall consist of three members appointed by the Governor with the concurrence of the Council who shall hold office until removed. (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.030", "title": "12.1.1.030 Appointment of Civil Rights Commission", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.040 Authority The Commission shall have authority to enforce the provisions of this Chapter and to issue appropriate rules and regulations for the protection of the civil rights of members of the Pueblo and non-members who came under the jurisdiction of the Pueblo for any purpose. (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.040", "title": "12.1.1.040 Authority", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.050 Complaint of Civil Rights Violation Any person who has probably cause to believe that his or her civil rights guaranteed by the Indian Civil Rights Act of April 11, 1968, PL 90-284 (82 Stat. 77) or by the traditions and customs of the Pueblo, may file a complaint with the Tribal Court pursuant to the Rules of Civil Procedure set forth in this Code, except for testing the legality of detention by order of the Pueblo which must be filed in the Federal Court. The complaint, together with the summons or citation, will be served in accordance with civil procedures. The complaint must be directed personally against the alleged violator or violators and an opportunity will be provided for the defendant or defendants to answer after which a hearing will be set following the Rules of Civil Procedure of this Code, and the hearing will be a civil matter held by the Tribal Court. (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.050", "title": "12.1.1.050 Complaint of Civil Rights Violation", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.060 Waiver of Immunity The Pueblo of San Ildefonso Tribal Council hereby expressly waives immunity of its members, officers, employees and staff from suit in matter relating to alleged violation of civil rights but for no other purpose. (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.060", "title": "12.1.1.060 Waiver of Immunity", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.070 Remedies After a hearing following the Civil Procedures of this Code and a finding for the plaintiff, the Tribal Court may issue appropriate orders that will provide the relief prayed for or as the Court may deem appropriate. If the finding is for the defendant, the suit shall be dismissed. (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.070", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.070", "title": "12.1.1.070 Remedies", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.080 Appeals form Orders of the Tribal Court Appeals from decisions of the Tribal Court may be made to the Tribal council following the procedures established for appeals under the Civil Procedures of this Code. The decisions of the Tribal Council shall be final. (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.080", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.080", "title": "12.1.1.080 Appeals form Orders of the Tribal Court", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.090", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 12.1.1.090 Additional Penalties In addition to the relief prayed for in the complaint and granted to the plaintiff, any violator or violators may be subject to pay a penalty assessment not to exceed $500.00 and costs or such other orders of the Court. (1984 Code.)", "num": "12.1.1.090", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.1|12.1.1|12.1.1.090", "title": "12.1.1.090 Additional Penalties", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.1.1.090"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 12.2 Consumer Rights Protection Part 12.2.1 Consumer Civil Rights and Welfare Protections \u00a7\u00a7 12.2.1.010 \u2013 12.2.1.030 Part 12.2.2 Violations to be Reported to San Ildefonso Tribal Courts \u00a7\u00a7 12.2.2.010 \u2013 12.2.2.020 Part 12.2.3 Pawned Goods \u00a7\u00a7 12.2.3.010 \u2013 12.2.3.020", "num": "12.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|12|12.2", "title": "Chapter 12.2 Consumer Rights Protection", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/12.2"}
