ng and Authorizing the Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the White Rock Convenience Store \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.12.010 \u2013 17.2.12.060 Part 17.2.13 Act Approving Tax Subsidy to San Ildefonso Services, LLC \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.13.010 \u2013 17.2.13.040 Part 17.2.14 Amending the Effective Date of the Amended Articles of Organization for San Ildefonso Services, LLC \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.14.010 \u2013 17.2.14.030 Part 17.2.15 Approving San Ildefonso Services, LLC, to Evaluate Options to Establish a Tribally-owned and Operated Telecommunications Cell Tower aka \"Totavi Cell Tower Project\" \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.15.010 \u2013 17.2.15.020 Part 17.2.16 Reappointing and Establishing the Term of Office of the Board of Managers of San Ildefonso Services, LLC \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.16.010 \u2013 17.2.16.030 Part 17.2.17 Approving and Enacting the Sixth Amended Operating Agreement of the San Ildefonso Services, LLC \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.17.010 \u2013 17.2.17.020 Part 17.2.18 Approving and Enacting the Fifth Amended Articles of Organization for San Ildefonso Services, LLC \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.18.010 \u2013 17.2.18.020 Part 17.2.19 Act Authorizing Amendments to the Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC, for the Totavi Convenience Store \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.19.010 \u2013 17.2.19.050 Part 17.2.20 Act Authorizing Amendments to the Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC, for the White Rock Convenience Store \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.20.010 \u2013 17.2.20.050 Part 17.2.21 San Ildefonso Services, LLC Member's Representatives Compensation Act of 2019 \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.21.010 \u2013 17.2.21.040 Part 17.2.22 Extension and Restatement of the Act Approving Tax Subsidy to San Ildefonso Services, LLC \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.22.010 \u2013 17.2.22.040 Part 17.2.23 Act Authorizing Second Amendment to the Business Lease with the San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Totavi Gas Station and Convenience Store [Repealed] Part 17.2.24 Act Authorizing Second Amendment to the Business Lease with the San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the White Rock Gas Station and Convenience Store [Repealed] Part 17.2.25 Amendment and Restatement of the Act Approving Tax Subsidy to San Ildefonso Services, LLC \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.25.010 \u2013 17.2.25.050 Part 17.2.26 Act Authorizing Loan to San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Purchase of Vigil Enterprises, Inc., a California Corporation \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.26.010 \u2013 17.2.26.040 Part 17.2.27 Act Authorizing Loan to San Ildefonso Services, LLC for C-Store Improvements \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.27.010 \u2013 17.2.27.040 Part 17.2.28 Approving and Authorizing the Third Amended Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Totavi Gas Station and Convenience Store [Repealed] Part 17.2.29 Approving and Authorizing the Third Amended Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the White Rock Gas Station and Convenience Store [Repealed] Part 17.2.30 Act Rescinding SI-R20-022 and SI-R22-027 and Authorizing Revised Second Amended Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Totavi Gas Station and Convenience Store \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.30.010 \u2013 17.2.30.060 Part 17.2.31 Act Rescinding SI-R20-023 and SI-R22-028 and Authorizing Revised Second Amended Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the White Rock Gas Station and Convenience Store \u00a7\u00a7 17.2.31.010 \u2013 17.2.31.060", "num": "17.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2", "title": "Chapter 17.2 Department of Economic Development", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.1 Department of Economic Development Enabling Act 17.2.1.010 Findings 17.2.1.020 Short Title 17.2.1.030 Definitions 17.2.1.040 Purpose 17.2.1.050 Findings 17.2.1.060 General Policy 17.2.1.070 Organization of the Department of Education 17.2.1.080 Department of Economic Development Goals and Objectives 17.2.1.090 Amendment 17.2.1.100 Sovereign Immunity 17.2.1.110 Severability", "num": "17.2.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1", "title": "Part 17.2.1 Department of Economic Development Enabling Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.010 Findings (a) Annual budget items may only be included if they have first been authorized by law as required by Section 5(a)(ii)(A) of the Agreement; (b) The Council finds that reorganizing the structure of governmental departments and programs will promote efficiency within the Tribe; (c) The Council finds that establishing a Department of Economic Development will assist the Tribe in achieving its economic endeavors.", "num": "17.2.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.010", "title": "17.2.1.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.020 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the Department of Economic Development Act (\"Act\").", "num": "17.2.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.020", "title": "17.2.1.020 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.030 Definitions (a) \"Agreement\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso governing Agreement. (b) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (c) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso.", "num": "17.2.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.030", "title": "17.2.1.030 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.040 Purpose The Purpose of the Act is to establish the Department of Economic Development.", "num": "17.2.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.040", "title": "17.2.1.040 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.050 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) reorganizing the structure of governmental departments and programs will promote efficiency within the Tribe; and (b) establishing a Department of Economic Development will assist the Tribe in achieving its economic endeavors.", "num": "17.2.1.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.050", "title": "17.2.1.050 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.060 General Policy Department of Economic Development. This act shall establish the Department of Economic Development to carry out the Tribe's economic development initiatives.", "num": "17.2.1.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.060", "title": "17.2.1.060 General Policy", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.070 Organization of the Department of Education (a) There shall be a Director of the Department of Economic Development who shall oversee the general supervision of the department. (b) In order to promote efficiency within the Department of Economic Development, program offices will be established as necessary. A program director shall oversee the general supervision of the each program office and shall report to the Director of the Department of Economic Development.", "num": "17.2.1.070", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.070", "title": "17.2.1.070 Organization of the Department of Education", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.080 Department of Economic Development Goals and Objectives Department of Economic Development. The overall goals of the Department of Economic Development (\"Department\") are to manage the convenience stores/gas stations (\"Phillips 66\") located at Totavi and White Rock. The Department shall work towards maximizing revenue, utilizing resources, and managing marketing efforts. The Department shall provide technical advice and assistance to tribal leadership in economic development improvements and opportunities.", "num": "17.2.1.080", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.080", "title": "17.2.1.080 Department of Economic Development Goals and Objectives", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.090", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.090 Amendment The Council may amend this enabling act or reorganize the Department of Economic Development at any time upon majority vote of the Council.", "num": "17.2.1.090", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.090", "title": "17.2.1.090 Amendment", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.090"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.100", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.100 Sovereign Immunity Nothing in this Act waives the sovereign immunity of the Pueblo or any of its representatives, officers, or employees.", "num": "17.2.1.100", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.100", "title": "17.2.1.100 Sovereign Immunity", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.100"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.110", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.1.110 Severability If a court of competent jurisdiction finds any provision of this Act to be invalid or illegal under applicable tribal and/or federal law, such provision shall be severed from this Act and the remainder of this Act shall remain in full force and effect.", "num": "17.2.1.110", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.1|17.2.1.110", "title": "17.2.1.110 Severability", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.1.110"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.2 Reassumption of Authority and Control Over the San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC 17.2.2.010 Findings 17.2.2.020 17.2.2.030 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R13-034, dated August 28, 2013.", "num": "17.2.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.2", "title": "Part 17.2.2 Reassumption of Authority and Control Over the San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.2.010 Findings (a) The Council formed San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC (\"Custodial\") pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R07-020; (b) Pursuant to Article IV of the Articles of Organization, San Ildefonso Custodial is a single member limited liability corporation wholly owned by the Pueblo de San Ildefonso; (c) Pursuant to Article IV of the Articles of Organization, all shares in the limited liability corporation are owned by the Pueblo de San Ildefonso for the benefit of the Pueblo and its members and the Pueblo Governor and Council shall serve as the Member's representatives, with all rights of a Member; (d) On September 16, 2009, the Council, through Resolution No. SI-R09-031 entitled \"Authorizing the San Ildefonso Pueblo Enterprise Corporation to Own and Operate the San Ildefonso Custodial Services, LLC,\" assigned San Ildefonso Custodial to San Ildefonso Pueblo Enterprise Corporation (\"SIPEC\") the Pueblo's federally chartered corporation, so that San Ildefonso Custodial would be a wholly-owned and operated subsidiary of SIPEC; (e) The Council, by Council Resolution No. SI-R09-031, also authorized the transfer of the Teaming Agreement with Tsay Building Services, LLC, from the Pueblo to SIPEC; (f) The Articles of Organization authorize the adoption of an Operating Agreement for the conduct of business and affairs of the San Ildefonso Custodial; (g) The Second Amended Operating Agreement for San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, at Section 3.1 states that the Council by Resolution No. SI-R09-031 assigned to the SIPEC Board of Directors the responsibility to serve as the Pueblo's Member Representative for San Ildefonso Custodial; (h) The SIPEC Board has served as the Member's Representative for San Ildefonso Custodial since 2009; (i) The transfer of San Ildefonso Custodial to SIPEC has not met the Pueblo's expectations; (j) The Council has determined that for the protection and continued viability of San Ildefonso Custodial, it is in the best interest of the Pueblo to rescind Tribal Council Resolution No. SI-R09-031and reassume any and all interest and authorities in San Ildefonso Custodial that were previously assigned to SIPEC. ( August 28, 2013, SI-R13-034 .)", "num": "17.2.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.2|17.2.2.010", "title": "17.2.2.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.2.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby rescinds in its entirety the Tribal Council Resolution No. SI-R09-031 \"Authorizing the San Ildefonso Pueblo Enterprise Corporation to Own and Operate the San Ildefonso Custodial Services, LLC,\" effectively immediately. ( August 28, 2013, SI-R13-034 .)", "num": "17.2.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.2|17.2.2.020", "title": "17.2.2.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.2.030 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council, on behalf of the single member, the Pueblo de San Ildefonso, shall reassume any and all interests and all authorities of the San Ildefonso Custodial Services, LLC, previously assigned to SIPEC, and shall reassume all authorities as the Member's Representative under the Articles of Organization for the San Ildefonso Custodial Services, effectively immediately. ( August 28, 2013, SI-R13-034 .)", "num": "17.2.2.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.2|17.2.2.030", "title": "17.2.2.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.2.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.3 Approving Resolution to Petition the Secretary of the Interior to Amend the Federal Charter of Incorporation of Pueblo Insurance Agency, Inc. 17.2.3.010 Findings 17.2.3.020 17.2.3.030 17.2.3.040 17.2.3.050", "num": "17.2.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.3", "title": "Part 17.2.3 Approving Resolution to Petition the Secretary of the Interior to Amend the Federal Charter of Incorporation of Pueblo Insurance Agency, Inc.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.3.010 Findings (a) On November 2, 2001, the Secretary of the Interior issued a federal charter of incorporation to the All Indian Pueblo Council for the Pueblo Insurance Agency, Inc. (\"Federal Charter\") under Section 17 of the Indian Reorganization Act of 1934, 25 U.S.C. \u00a7 477, for the benefit of the Pueblo of Acoma, Pueblo of Cochiti, Pueblo of Isleta, Pueblo of Jemez, Pueblo of Laguna, Pueblo of Santa Ana, Pueblo of Sandia, Pueblo of San Felipe, Pueblo of Santo Domingo, Pueblo of Zia, Pueblo of Zuni, Pueblo of Nambe, Pueblo of Picuris, Pueblo of Pojoaque, Pueblo of Santa Clara, Pueblo de San Ildefonso, Ohkay Owingeh, Pueblo of Tesuque, and Pueblo of Taos (the \"19 Pueblos\"); (b) The Federal Charter, Art. XX (A), authorizes the All Indian Pueblo Council, as the shareholder's representative of the 19 Pueblos, to petition the Secretary to amend the Federal Charter; (c) There is no requirement or procedure under the law of the Pueblo requiring a referendum by the members of the Pueblo or any other procedure or requirement beyond this resolution in order to petition the Secretary for the Amended Federal Charter under 25 U.S.C. \u00a7 477; (d) The 19 Pueblos dissolved the All Indian Pueblo Council in 2011; (e) In light of the dissolution of the All Indian Pueblo Council, the 19 Pueblos desire to remove all references to the All Indian Pueblo Council from the Federal Charter and clarify the role of the 19 Pueblos as the sole shareholders under the Federal Charter as shown on the amended Federal Charter (\"Amended Federal Charter\"), which is attached as Exhibit A; (f) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso finds that it is in the best interests of the Pueblo to petition the Secretary to approve the Amended Federal Charter.", "num": "17.2.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.3|17.2.3.010", "title": "17.2.3.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.3.020 Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Council hereby petitions the Secretary to approve the Amended Federal Charter, or in such modified form as the Secretary may approve with the concurrence of the Pueblo.", "num": "17.2.3.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.3|17.2.3.020", "title": "17.2.3.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.3.030 Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Council requests that the Secretary issue the Amended Federal Charter jointly to the 19 Pueblos at the earliest feasible date.", "num": "17.2.3.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.3|17.2.3.030", "title": "17.2.3.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.3.040 Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Council authorizes the Governor of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso to work with the Pueblo Insurance Agency, Inc., and the other Pueblos to secure the timely issuance of the Amended Federal Charter.", "num": "17.2.3.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.3|17.2.3.040", "title": "17.2.3.040", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.3.050 That, as required by 25 U.S.C. \u00a7 477, the Amended Federal Charter requested in this resolution will not be effective until ratified by vote of the governing bodies of all the 19 Pueblos.", "num": "17.2.3.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.3|17.2.3.050", "title": "17.2.3.050", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.3.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.4 Resolution Ratifying Amendments to Federal Charter of Pueblo Insurance Agency, Inc. 17.2.4.010 Findings 17.2.4.020 17.2.4.030 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R15-019, dated July 30, 2015.", "num": "17.2.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.4", "title": "Part 17.2.4 Resolution Ratifying Amendments to Federal Charter of Pueblo Insurance Agency, Inc.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.4.010 Findings (a) On November 2, 2001, the Secretary of the Interior issued a federal charter of incorporation to the All Indian Pueblo Council for the Pueblo Insurance Agency, Inc. (\"Federal Charter\") under Section 17 of the Indian Reorganization Act of 1934, 25 U.S.C. \u00a7 477, for the benefit of the Pueblo of Acoma, Pueblo of Cochiti, Pueblo of Isleta, Pueblo of Jemez, Pueblo of Laguna, Pueblo of Santa Ana, Pueblo of Sandia, Pueblo of San Felipe, Pueblo of Santo Domingo, Pueblo of Zia, Pueblo of Zuni, Pueblo of Nambe, Pueblo of Picuris, Pueblo of Pojoaque, Pueblo of Santa Clara, Pueblo de San Ildefonso, Ohkay Owingeh, Pueblo of Tesuque, and Pueblo of Taos (the \"19 Pueblos\"); (b) The Pueblo, by Tribal Council Resolution No. SI-R15-006 (March 13, 2015) (\"Tribal Council Resolution\"), petitioned the Secretary to approve certain amendments to PIA's federal charter (the \"Amended Federal Charter\") to, among other things, remove all references to the All Indian Pueblo Council, which the 19 Pueblos dissolved in 2013; (c) On May 15, 2015, the Secretary approved the Amended Federal Charter, which is attached as Exhibit A, subject to ratification by the governing body of each of the 19 Pueblos; (d) The Amended Federal Charter is in the form requested by the Pueblo in the Tribal Council Resolution, and is acceptable to the Tribal Council; (e) There is no requirement under the laws of the Pueblo that would require a referendum by the members of the Pueblo or any other procedure beyond this resolution in order to ratify the Amended Federal Charter. ( July 30, 2015, SI-R15-019 .)", "num": "17.2.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.4|17.2.4.010", "title": "17.2.4.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.4.020 The Tribal Council hereby ratifies the Amended Federal Charter. ( July 30, 2015, SI-R15-019 .)", "num": "17.2.4.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.4|17.2.4.020", "title": "17.2.4.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.4.030 The Amended Federal Charter shall be effective upon the ratification by all the 19 Pueblos. ( July 30, 2015, SI-R15-019 .)", "num": "17.2.4.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.4|17.2.4.030", "title": "17.2.4.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.4.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.5", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.5 Ratifying The Formal Name Change Of San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, And Approving The Fourth Amended Operating Agreement Of San Ildefonso Services, LLC, (Formerly Known As San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC) 17.2.5.010 Findings 17.2.5.020 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R13-034, dated August 28, 2013.", "num": "17.2.5", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.5", "title": "Part 17.2.5 Ratifying The Formal Name Change Of San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, And Approving The Fourth Amended Operating Agreement Of San Ildefonso Services, LLC, (Formerly Known As San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC)", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.5"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.5.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.5.010 Findings (a) On May 14, 2007, by Tribal Council Resolution No. SI-R07-020, the Tribal Council chartered San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, by approving its Articles of Organization; (b) San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, is chartered under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo and the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governor and Tribal Council serve as the Member's Representatives, as stipulated in the Operating Agreement; (c) On January 7, 2009, by Tribal Council Resolution No.SI-R07-001, the Tribal Council approved the Operating Agreement of San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC; (d) The Operating Agreement has been amended on three prior occasions; (e) On August 5, 2015, the Member's Representatives approved a name change whereby San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, would become San Ildefonso Services, LLC; (f) On August 5, 2015, the Member's Representatives approved the \"San Ildefonso Services, LLC (aka San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC) Fourth Amended Operating Agreement;\" (g) The Council desires to ratify its actions on August 5, 2015, by formal resolution. ( August 28, 2013, SI-R13-034 .)", "num": "17.2.5.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.5|17.2.5.010", "title": "17.2.5.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.5.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.5.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.5.020 The Council ratifies its actions on August 5, 2015, to: (1) Approve a name change whereby San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, is now known as San Ildefonso Services, LLC; and (2) Approve the \"San Ildefonso Services, LLC (aka San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC) Fourth Amended Operating Agreement.\" ( August 28, 2013, SI-R13-034 .)", "num": "17.2.5.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.5|17.2.5.020", "title": "17.2.5.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.5.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.6 Amending Section 2.1 Of The Fourth Amended Operating Agreement Of San Ildefonso Services, Llc (F/K/A San Ildefonso Custodial, Llc) To Identify Current Board Of Managers 17.2.6.010 Findings 17.2.6.020 17.2.6.030 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R17-007, dated March 21, 2017.", "num": "17.2.6", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.6", "title": "Part 17.2.6 Amending Section 2.1 Of The Fourth Amended Operating Agreement Of San Ildefonso Services, Llc (F/K/A San Ildefonso Custodial, Llc) To Identify Current Board Of Managers", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.6.010 Findings (a) on May 14, 2007, by Council Resolution No. SI-R07-020, the Council chartered San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, by approving its Articles of Organization; (b) San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, is chartered under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo, and the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governor and Council serve as the Member's Representatives; (c) On January 7, 2009, by Council Resolution No. SI-R07-001, the Council approved the Operating Agreement of San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC; (d) On August 5, 2015, the Member's Representatives approved a name change whereby San Ildefonso Custodial, LLC, would become San Ildefonso Services, LLC, and further approved the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement for San Ildefonso Services, LLC, which was later ratified by Council Resolution No. SI-R16-031; (e) The \"Fourth Amended Operating Agreement\" at Section 2.1 identifies the Board of Managers as Dominic Pruitt, Barbara Gonzales, and Pamela Garcia; (f) On March 8, 2017, the Member's Representatives appointed Martin Lovato as a Manager to fulfill the remaining unexpired term following the resignation of Board Member Pamela Garcia; ( March 22, 2017, SI-R17-007 .)", "num": "17.2.6.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.6|17.2.6.010", "title": "17.2.6.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.6.020 The Member's Representatives hereby amend and replace Section 2.1 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement for San Ildefonso Services, LLC, as follows: 2.1 Management by Managers. This LLC will be managed by a Board of Managers selected by the Member's Representatives, in accordance with the Articles of Organization. The Board of Managers shall select the LLC's program development manager and other employees not based at Los Alamos National Laboratory. The LLC Board of Managers selected by the Member's Representatives are: Names: Dominic Pruitt Barbara Gonzales Martin Lovato ( March 22, 2017, SI-R17-007 .)", "num": "17.2.6.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.6|17.2.6.020", "title": "17.2.6.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.6.030 That as a Manager, Martin Lovato shall provide a signed certification consistent with Section 9 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement stating that he has read the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement and agrees to be bound by its terms in discharging his duties as a Manager. ( March 22, 2017, SI-R17-007 .)", "num": "17.2.6.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.6|17.2.6.030", "title": "17.2.6.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.6.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.7 Act to Transfer Ownership and Operation of C-Stores to San Ildefonso Services, LLC 17.2.7.010 Short Title 17.2.7.020 Definitions 17.2.7.030 Purpose 17.2.7.040 Findings 17.2.7.050 Conditions of Transfer 17.2.7.060 Authority of Tribal Governor to Execute Transfer", "num": "17.2.7", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.7", "title": "Part 17.2.7 Act to Transfer Ownership and Operation of C-Stores to San Ildefonso Services, LLC", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.7.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"ACT TO TRANSFER OWNERSHIP AND OPERATION OF C-STORES TO SAN ILDEFONSO SERVICES, LLC.\" ( June 23, 2017, SI-R17-018 .)", "num": "17.2.7.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.7|17.2.7.010", "title": "17.2.7.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.7.020 Definitions (a) \"C-Stores\" means the Totavi and White Rock Phillips 66 Convenience Stores and Gas Stations located within the external boundaries of the Pueblo. (b) \"SIS LLC\" means San Ildefonso Services, LLC, a single member limited liability company organized under tribal law and wholly owned by the Pueblo. ( June 23, 2017, SI-R17-018 .)", "num": "17.2.7.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.7|17.2.7.020", "title": "17.2.7.020 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.7.030 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to authorize the transfer of ownership and operation of the C-Stores from the Pueblo to SIS LLC. ( June 23, 2017, SI-R17-018 .)", "num": "17.2.7.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.7|17.2.7.030", "title": "17.2.7.030 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.7.040 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) The Pueblo owns and operates two C-Stores within the Pueblo's lands; and (b) The Council has determined that it is in the best interests of the Pueblo to transfer the ownership and operation of the C-Stores to SIS LLC. ( June 23, 2017, SI-R17-018 .)", "num": "17.2.7.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.7|17.2.7.040", "title": "17.2.7.040 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.7.050 Conditions of Transfer This Act establishes the following essential terms pursuant to which the ownership and operation of the C-Stores shall be transferred from the Pueblo to SIS LLC: (a) The asset transfer will be effective beginning July 1, 2017. (b) The Pueblo will grant, convey, assign, transfer and deliver to SIS LLC all of the Pueblo's rights, title and interest in and to the C-Stores, with the exception of any trust or fee land underlying the C-Stores, free and clear of all liens, pledges, security interests, charges, claims, restrictions and encumbrances of any nature whatsoever. (c) The Pueblo will provide any and all necessary consent and authorization to allow SIS LLC to assume its rights and obligations under any financial accounts, insurance policies, or other accounts necessary to own and operate the C-Stores. (d) SIS LLC will assume all liabilities, including contracts and accounts, of the C-Stores existing on or accrued after July 1, 2017, and SIS LLC will be responsible for the timely payment of any applicable taxes related to the operation of or otherwise imposed on the C-Stores. (e) SIS LLC will not assume any liability existing or accrued prior to July 1, 2017, whether such liability is due to a debt, tax, or other obligation, and should SIS LLC learn of any liability existing or accrued prior to July 1, 2017, it must promptly notify the Pueblo of such liability and the Pueblo shall indemnify SIS LLC for such liability or its pro rata portion of such liability. (f) All employees of the C-Stores will become employees of SIS LLC effective July 1, 2017, and SIS LLC will be responsible for payroll, benefits, and related human resources matters for employees of the C-Stores. (g) Prior to September 30, 2017, SIS LLC will develop and provide to the Pueblo a balance sheet, income statement, and cash flow statement for the C-Stores, and propose terms of a lease agreement for the lease of the Pueblo's lands on which the C-Stores are located. (h) SIS LLC will assume full responsibility for insuring, maintaining, and repairing the C-Stores, and will be responsible for continuing or maintaining any and all policies of insurance with coverage and limits at or exceeding the coverage and limits of the current policies and as mandated by law or agreement. ( June 23, 2017, SI-R17-018 .)", "num": "17.2.7.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.7|17.2.7.050", "title": "17.2.7.050 Conditions of Transfer", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.7.060 Authority of Tribal Governor to Execute Transfer The Council hereby authorizes the Governor of the Pueblo to carry out and execute all documents necessary to effect the transfer of the C-Stores to SIS LLC pursuant to the terms of this Act. ( June 23, 2017, SI-R17-018 .)", "num": "17.2.7.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.7|17.2.7.060", "title": "17.2.7.060 Authority of Tribal Governor to Execute Transfer", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.7.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.8", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.8 Amending Article XI(I) of the Third Amended Articles of Organization and Section 2.7.3 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement of San Ildefonso Services, LLC 17.2.8.010 Findings 17.2.8.020", "num": "17.2.8", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.8", "title": "Part 17.2.8 Amending Article XI(I) of the Third Amended Articles of Organization and Section 2.7.3 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement of San Ildefonso Services, LLC", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.8"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.8.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.8.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Pueblo\") is a sovereign and self-governing Tribe, recognized as such by the United States of America, with the authority to govern its people, lands and other resources. (b) San Ildefonso Services, LLC, is chartered under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo, and the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governor and Council serve as the Member's Representatives. (c) Pursuant to the Third Amended Articles of Organization and the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement of San Ildefonso Services, LLC, the company is a Manager-Managed LLC with the authority to manage the business affairs of the company vested in a Board of Managers that shall contain three (3) managers elected by the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council, acting as the Member's Representatives. (d) Article XI(I) of the Third Amended Articles of Organization and Section 2.7.3 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement both require that a quorum for any Managers' Meeting shall consist of three (3) Managers, and if a quorum is not present, the meeting shall be adjourned to a new place and time. (e) Due to temporary vacancies on the Board of Managers or the occasional unavailability of Managers, the quorum requirement in Article XI(I) of the Third Amended Articles of Organization and Section 2.7.3 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement may create an inability of the Board of Managers to hold Managers' Meetings and otherwise act to manage the business affairs of the company. (f) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governor and Council, as Member's Representatives, have determined that it is prudent and in the best interests of San Ildefonso Services, LLC to amend the quorum requirement contained in Article XI(I) of the Third Amended Articles of Organization and Section 2.7.3 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement to allow a quorum of two (2) Managers for Managers' Meetings. (g) The sole authority to make amendments to the Articles of Organization is vested in the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council as Member's Representatives, and any amendments must be written in a Council Resolution. (h) The Fourth Amended Operating Agreement can only be amended or modified through a written instrument executed by the Member's Representatives. ( September 8, 2017, SI-R17-028 .)", "num": "17.2.8.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.8|17.2.8.010", "title": "17.2.8.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.8.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.8.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.8.020 (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council as Member's Representatives hereby amend and replace Article XI(I) of the Third Amended Articles of Organization in its entirety as follows: Managers' Meetings, Notices, Quorum, and Procedure. A quorum for any Managers' Meeting shall consist of two (2) Managers, and if a quorum is not present, the meeting shall be adjourned to a new place and time. An adjournment shall not be necessary, however, and a Managers' Meeting with less than a quorum may be held, if all non-attending Managers agreed in writing prior to the meeting to the holding of the meeting. All such written consents to the holding of a formal meeting shall be kept and filed with the records of the meeting. A Manager may participate telephonically, with the consent of the other Managers. (b) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council as Member's Representatives hereby amend and replace Section 2.7.3 of the Fourth Amended Operating Agreement in its entirety as follows: Quorum. A quorum for any Manager's Meeting shall consist of two (2) Managers, and if a quorum is not present, the meeting shall be adjourned to a new place and time with notice of the adjourned meeting given to all Managers. An adjournment shall not be necessary, however, and a Manager's Meeting with less than a quorum may be held, if all non-attending Managers agreed in writing prior to the meeting to the holding of the meeting. All such written consents to the holding of a formal management meeting shall be kept and filed with the records of the meeting. Ex-officio managers of the LLC shall not be counted in reaching a quorum of the LLC. A Manager may participate telephonically, with the consent of the other Managers. (c) Such amendments are incorporated into a Fourth Amended Articles of Organization for San Ildefonso Services, LLC and a Fifth Amended Operating Agreement which are hereby approved. ( September 8, 2017, SI-R17-028 .)", "num": "17.2.8.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.8|17.2.8.020", "title": "17.2.8.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.8.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.9", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.9 Approving and Enacting Amended Articles of Organization and Amended Operating Agreement for San Ildefonso Services, LLC 17.2.9.010 Findings 17.2.9.020 Editor's Notes See San Ildefonso Servs. Fourth Amended Arts. of Org.", "num": "17.2.9", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.9", "title": "Part 17.2.9 Approving and Enacting Amended Articles of Organization and Amended Operating Agreement for San Ildefonso Services, LLC", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.9"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.9.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.9.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Pueblo') is a sovereign and self-governing Tribe, recognized as such by the United States of America. (b) The sovereign authority of the Pueblo is vested in its Council and Governor. (c) San Ildefonso Services, LLC, is chartered under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo, and the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governor and Council currently serve as the Member's Representatives. (d) The Council has determined it is prudent and in the best interests of the Pueblo and San Ildefonso Services, LLC to reorganize the Member's Representatives and the Management of San Ildefonso Services, LLC to allow for more efficient oversight and management of the entity. (e) The Council has reviewed and approved the attached amended Articles of Organization and the Operating Agreement for San Ildefonso Services, LLC, effective as of March 31, 2018. ( December 29, 2017, SI-R17-047 .)", "num": "17.2.9.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.9|17.2.9.010", "title": "17.2.9.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.9.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.9.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.9.020 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves and adopts this resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor, or his designee, to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this resolution. ( December 29, 2017, SI-R17-047 .)", "num": "17.2.9.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.9|17.2.9.020", "title": "17.2.9.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.9.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.10 Amending the Effective Date of the Amended Articles of Organization for San Ildefonso Services, LLC 17.2.10.010 Findings 17.2.10.020 17.2.10.030", "num": "17.2.10", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.10", "title": "Part 17.2.10 Amending the Effective Date of the Amended Articles of Organization for San Ildefonso Services, LLC", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.10.010 Findings (a) The Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Pueblo') is a sovereign and self-governing Tribe, recognized as such by the United States of America. (b) The sovereign authority of the Pueblo is vested in its Council and Governor. (c) San Ildefonso Services, LLC, is chartered under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo, and the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Governor and Council currently serve as the Member's Representatives. (d) The Council enacted Council Resolution No. SI-R17-047, titled \"Approving and Enacting Amended Articles of Organization and Operating Agreement for San Ildefonso Services, LLC\". (e) By Council Resolution No. SI-R17-047, the amendments to the Articles of Organization were to be effective as of March 31, 2018. (f) The Council has determined that it is prudent and in the best interests of the Pueblo and San Ildefonso Services, LLC to amend and change the effective date of the Amended Articles of Organization to September 1, 2018. ( April 2, 2018, SI-R18-004 .)", "num": "17.2.10.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.10|17.2.10.010", "title": "17.2.10.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.10.020 The Council hereby amends the \"Fourth Amended Articles of Organization for San Ildefonso Services, a Limited Liability Company Chartered by the Pueblo de San Ildefonso, a federally recognized sovereign\" to extend the effective date from March 31, 2018 to September 1, 2018, all other terms of Council Resolution No. SI-R17-047 shall remain in effect. ( April 2, 2018, SI-R18-004 .)", "num": "17.2.10.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.10|17.2.10.020", "title": "17.2.10.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.10.030 The Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council hereby approves and adopts this resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor, or his designee, to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this resolution. ( April 2, 2018, SI-R18-004 .)", "num": "17.2.10.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.10|17.2.10.030", "title": "17.2.10.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.10.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.11 Approving and Authorizing the Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Totavi Convenience Store 17.2.11.010 Short Title 17.2.11.020 Definitions 17.2.11.030 Purpose 17.2.11.040 Findings 17.2.11.050 Council Authorizations and Waivers 17.2.11.060 Authority of Tribal Governor to Execute the Business Lease", "num": "17.2.11", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.11", "title": "Part 17.2.11 Approving and Authorizing the Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Totavi Convenience Store", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.11.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the Act, \"APPROVING AND AUTHORIZING THE BUSINESS LEASE WITH SAN ILDEFONSO SERVICES, LLC FOR THE TOTAVI CONVENIENCE STORE.\" ( May 10, 2018, SI-R18-005 .)", "num": "17.2.11.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.11|17.2.11.010", "title": "17.2.11.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.11.020 Definitions (a) \"Totavi Convenience Store\" means the Totavi Convenience Store and Gas Station located within the external boundaries of the Pueblo. (b) \"SIS LLC\" means San Ildefonso Services, LLC, a single member limited liability company organized under tribal law and wholly owned by the Pueblo . ( May 10, 2018, SI-R18-005 .)", "num": "17.2.11.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.11|17.2.11.020", "title": "17.2.11.020 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.11.030 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to authorize and direct the Governor of the Pueblo to negotiate and execute a Business Lease with SIS LLC for the Totavi Convenience Store. ( May 10, 2018, SI-R18-005 .)", "num": "17.2.11.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.11|17.2.11.030", "title": "17.2.11.030 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.11.040 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) SIS LLC is chartered under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo. (b) On June 21, 2017, the Pueblo de San Ildefonso enacted a law entitled \"Act to Transfer Ownership and Operation of C-Stores to San Ildefonso Services, LLC.\" (c) To carry out the Act, San Ildefonso Services, LLC will need to obtain a business lease for the premises of the Totavi Convenience Store, which is located on the Pueblo's lands. (d) Under Article VIII of its Articles of Organization, San Ildefonso Services LLC has authority to \"buy, sell, lease and otherwise acquire and maintain buildings, offices, shops and other appurtenances proper and necessary for the carrying on of said business.\" (e) A copy of the proposed Business Lease for the Totavi Convenience Store is attached to this Resolution (\"Proposed Business Lease\" or \"Proposed Lease\"). ( May 10, 2018, SI-R18-005 .)", "num": "17.2.11.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.11|17.2.11.040", "title": "17.2.11.040 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.11.050 Council Authorizations and Waivers (a) The Council has reviewed the proposed monetary compensation that must be paid under the Proposed Business Lease and has determined the amount to be satisfactory to the Pueblo, and the Council hereby waives valuation that may otherwise be required under the Code of Federal Regulations, and has determined that accepting such negotiated compensation and waiving valuation is in the best interests of the Pueblo. (b) The Council has determined that it is in the Pueblo's best interest that no periodic review of the adequacy of compensation or adjustment be required for the Proposed Business Lease. (c) The Council has determined that it is in the Pueblo's best interest to waive the requirement of a performance bond or an alternative form of security that may otherwise be required under the Code of Federal Regulations, and further requests that the Bureau of Indian Affairs, Department of the Interior, defer to the Council's express waiver of such bond or security. (d) The Council has determined that it is in the Pueblo's best interest to provide an express and limited waiver of its immunity from suit, subject to the limitations herein, only as to actions to enforce the Business Lease or any settlement agreement reached in mediation under the Business Lease, provided that the Pueblo's limited waiver of sovereign immunity is granted only to San Ildefonso Services, LLC and not to any other individual or entity, and that the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Court shall have exclusive jurisdiction over any lawsuit brought pursuant to this limited waiver of immunity. (e) The Council has determined that the Governor may execute said Business Leases or any other certification required by federal or tribal law. ( May 10, 2018, SI-R18-005 .)", "num": "17.2.11.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.11|17.2.11.050", "title": "17.2.11.050 Council Authorizations and Waivers", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.11.060 Authority of Tribal Governor to Execute the Business Lease The Council hereby authorizes and directs the Governor of the Pueblo to negotiate and execute a final Business Lease in substantially the same form as the attached Proposed Business Lease consistent with this Act, make any revisions and amendments that may be necessary and required to support the execution of a final Business Lease, and execute any certification that may be required by federal or tribal law to support the execution of a final Business Lease. ( May 10, 2018, SI-R18-005 .)", "num": "17.2.11.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.11|17.2.11.060", "title": "17.2.11.060 Authority of Tribal Governor to Execute the Business Lease", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.11.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.12", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.12 Approving and Authorizing the Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the White Rock Convenience Store 17.2.12.010 Short Title 17.2.12.020 Definitions 17.2.12.030 Purpose 17.2.12.040 Findings 17.2.12.050 Council Authorizations and Waivers 17.2.12.060 Authority of Tribal Governor to Execute the Business Lease", "num": "17.2.12", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.12", "title": "Part 17.2.12 Approving and Authorizing the Business Lease with San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the White Rock Convenience Store", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.12"}
