{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.25 Amendment and Restatement of the Act Approving Tax Subsidy to San Ildefonso Services, LLC 17.2.25.010 Short Title 17.2.25.020 Purpose 17.2.25.030 Definitions 17.2.25.040 Findings 17.2.25.050 Authorizations", "num": "17.2.25", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.25", "title": "Part 17.2.25 Amendment and Restatement of the Act Approving Tax Subsidy to San Ildefonso Services, LLC", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.25.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"AMENDMENT AND RESTATEMENT OF THE ACT APPROVING TAX SUBSIDY TO SAN ILDEFONSO SERVICES, LLC.\" ( August 30, 2021, SI-R21-019 .)", "num": "17.2.25.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.25|17.2.25.010", "title": "17.2.25.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.25.020 Purpose The Purpose of this Act is to approve and restate and extend the 2018-2019 Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tax Subsidy to San Ildefonso Services, LLC for a five-year period beginning June 1, 2021 to May 31, 2026. ( August 30, 2021, SI-R21-019 .)", "num": "17.2.25.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.25|17.2.25.020", "title": "17.2.25.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.25.030 Definitions (a) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council. (b) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( August 30, 2021, SI-R21-019 .)", "num": "17.2.25.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.25|17.2.25.030", "title": "17.2.25.030 Definitions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.25.040 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) San Ildefonso Services, LLC (\"SIS, LLC\") was chartered by the Pueblo under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo; and (b) SIS, LLC owns and operates two businesses within Pueblo lands commonly referred to as the Totavi and White Rock Convenience Stores and Gas Stations (\"C-Stores\"); and (c) The Council transferred ownership and operation of the C-Stores to SIS, LLC, effective July 1, 2017, pursuant to the, \"Act to Transfer Ownership and Operation of C-Stores to San Ildefonso Services, LLC\", dated June 21, 2017; and (d) Since the acquisition of the C-Stores, SIS, LLC has endeavored to improve the operations and profitability of the C-Stores; and (e) On June 6, 2018, the Council formally approved a subsidy for the benefit of SIS, LLC in the amount of $0.06 for every gallon of gasoline sold in the C-Stores (\"Subsidy\") pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R18-011, titled \"Act Approving Tax Subsidy to San Ildefonso Services, LLC\" (\"Subsidy Act\"); and (f) the Subsidy Act was subsequently extended and restated on October 14, 2019, but has since expired; and (g) SIS, LLC has requested that the Subsidy be restated and continue in force for a five-year period, effective on June 1, 2021, and expiring on May 31, 2026, to reduce costs of gasoline in order to make upgrades to the fuel pumps and the C-Stores; and (h) The Council has determined that it is in the Pueblo's best interests to support SIS, LLC and its operation of the C-Stores by extending the Subsidy in the amount of $0.06 for every gallon of gasoline sold in the C-Stores for a five-year period beginning on June 1, 2021 and expiring on May 31, 2026, and has identified that such subsidy could be paid from revenues generated by the Pueblo's $0.17 per gallon fuel tax. ( August 30, 2021, SI-R21-019 .)", "num": "17.2.25.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.25|17.2.25.040", "title": "17.2.25.040 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.25.050 Authorizations (a) The Council hereby approves and reauthorizes the Subsidy to SIS LLC of $0.06 for every gallon of gasoline sold by the C-Stores. (b) The Subsidy shall be paid by the Pueblo from revenues received by the Pueblo from the $0.17 per gallon fuel tax paid by the C-Stores. (c) The Subsidy shall be used by SIS exclusively to reduce costs of gasoline in order to make upgrades to the fuel pumps and the C-Stores, and the Subsidy shall not be used for any other purpose. (d) The Subsidy shall be effective as of June 1, 2021, and shall expire on May 31, 2026. (e) SIS, LLC shall provide monthly financial statements and fuel reports, and such other information and documents to the Governor and Council to support the expenditure and continuation of the Subsidy. (f) The Council authorizes the Governor to continue the Subsidy and execute any documents that may be necessary to support the provision of the Subsidy. (g) The Governor is authorized to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent this Act. ( August 30, 2021, SI-R21-019 .)", "num": "17.2.25.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.25|17.2.25.050", "title": "17.2.25.050 Authorizations", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.25.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.26 Act Authorizing Loan to San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Purchase of Vigil Enterprises, Inc., a California Corporation 17.2.26.010 Short Title 17.2.26.020 Purpose 17.2.26.030 Findings 17.2.26.040 Authorizations", "num": "17.2.26", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.26", "title": "Part 17.2.26 Act Authorizing Loan to San Ildefonso Services, LLC for the Purchase of Vigil Enterprises, Inc., a California Corporation", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.26.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"ACT AUTHORIZING LOAN TO SAN ILDEFONSO SERVICES, LLC FOR THE PURCHASE OF VIGIL ENTERPRISES, INC. A CALIFORNIA CORPORATION (\"Act\").\" ( October 15, 2021, SI-R21-023 .)", "num": "17.2.26.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.26|17.2.26.010", "title": "17.2.26.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.26.020 Purpose The Purpose of this Act is to authorize a Loan Agreement between the Pueblo and SIS LLC for the acquisition of VEI. ( October 15, 2021, SI-R21-023 .)", "num": "17.2.26.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.26|17.2.26.020", "title": "17.2.26.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.26.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) San Ildefonso Services, LLC (\"SIS, LLC\") was established and chartered by the Pueblo under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo; and (b) In accordance with the Fifth Amended Articles of Organization of SIS, LLC (\"Articles of Organization\"), the duly-appointed members of the five (5) person Member's Representative group (the \"Member's Representatives\") together exercise all rights of the Pueblo in its role as the single member of SIS, LLC\"); and (c) SIS LLC is a Manager-Managed limited liability company, and Peter Fant currently serves as the appointed Manager and the Manager possesses the exclusive authority to manage the business affairs of SIS LLC; and (d) Pursuant to Article VII of the Articles of Organization, the business purpose of SIS LLC is to engage in federal contracting and other lawful business ventures that serve the best interest of SIS LLC, the Pueblo and its members; and (e) In furtherance of SIS LLC's business purpose, SIS LLC intends to acquire Vigil Enterprises, Inc., (\"VEI\"), a California Corporation, from Miller Engineers Inc., d/b/a Souder Miller &amp; Associates; and (f) The Member's Representatives of SIS LLC determined it was in the best interest of SIS LLC to begin negotiations for the acquisition of VEI and to explore funding options for the purposes of further developing SIS LLC's federal contracting capabilities; and (g) SIS LLC seeks partial funding for the acquisition of VEI from the Pueblo which terms are detailed in the Loan Agreement; and (h) The Council has reviewed the general terms of the proposed Loan Agreement and believes it is in the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize the Governor to negotiate and enter into a final Loan Agreement with SIS LLC for the purpose of acquiring VEI; and (i) The Loan Agreement is not intended to be a capital contribution by the Member's Representatives. ( October 15, 2021, SI-R21-023 .)", "num": "17.2.26.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.26|17.2.26.030", "title": "17.2.26.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.26.040 Authorizations (a) The Council hereby authorizes the Governor to negotiate and execute a Loan Agreement with SIS LLC for the purchase of VEI. (b) The Term of the Loan Agreement shall be for a five-year period beginning October 1, 2021 to September 30, 2026. (c) The Council hereby authorizes up to $750,000 of Pueblo funds for the Loan to be taken from available federal grant funds or other available funds. (d) The Governor, or his designee, is authorized to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent this Act ( October 15, 2021, SI-R21-023 .)", "num": "17.2.26.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.26|17.2.26.040", "title": "17.2.26.040 Authorizations", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.26.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 17.2.27 Act Authorizing Loan to San Ildefonso Services, LLC for C-Store Improvements 17.2.27.010 Short Title 17.2.27.020 Purpose 17.2.27.030 Findings 17.2.27.040 Authorizations", "num": "17.2.27", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.27", "title": "Part 17.2.27 Act Authorizing Loan to San Ildefonso Services, LLC for C-Store Improvements", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.27.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"ACT AUTHORIZING LOAN TO SAN ILDEFONSO SERVICES, LLC FOR C-STORE IMPROVEMENTS (\"Act\").\" ( November 12, 2021, SI-R21-025 .)", "num": "17.2.27.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.27|17.2.27.010", "title": "17.2.27.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.27.020 Purpose The Purpose of this Act is to authorize a Loan Agreement between the Pueblo and SIS LLC for necessary equipment upgrades and capital improvements at the Totavi and White Rock convenience stores (\"C-Stores\"). ( November 12, 2021, SI-R21-025 .)", "num": "17.2.27.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.27|17.2.27.020", "title": "17.2.27.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.27.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) San Ildefonso Services, LLC (\"SIS, LLC\") was established and chartered by the Pueblo under tribal law as a single member limited liability company wholly owned by the Pueblo; and (b) In accordance with the Fifth Amended Articles of Organization of SIS, LLC (\"Articles of Organization\"), the duly-appointed members of the five (5) person Member's Representative group (the \"Member's Representatives\") together exercise all rights of the Pueblo in its role as the single member of SIS, LLC\"); and (c) SIS LLC is a Manager-Managed limited liability company, and Peter Fant currently serves as the appointed Manager and the Manager possesses the exclusive authority to manage the business affairs of SIS LLC; and (d) SIS LLC operates the Totavi and White Rock convenience stores (\"C-Stores\"); and (e) Both C-Stores are in serious need of equipment upgrades and capital improvements necessary for continued operation and improved sales; and (f) The Member's Representatives of SIS LLC determined it was in the best interest of SIS LLC to seek funding for the necessary improvements at the C-stores; and (g) SIS LLC seeks a loan from the Pueblo which terms are detailed in a proposed Loan Agreement and SIS LLC intends to utilize Pueblo tax subsidy funding to repay the loan; and (h) The Council has reviewed the general terms of the proposed Loan Agreement and believes it is in the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize the Governor to negotiate and enter into a final Loan Agreement with SIS LLC for funding for the C-Store improvements; and (i) The Loan Agreement is not intended to be a capital contribution by the Member's Representatives. ( November 12, 2021, SI-R21-025 .)", "num": "17.2.27.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.27|17.2.27.030", "title": "17.2.27.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 17.2.27.040 Authorizations (a) The Council hereby authorizes the Governor to negotiate and execute a Loan Agreement with SIS LLC for necessary improvements at the C-Stores. (b) The Term of the Loan Agreement shall be for a five-year period beginning June 1, 2021 and ending on May 31, 2026 to match the term of the tribal tax subsidy. (c) The Council hereby authorizes up to $450,000 of Pueblo funds for the Loan to be taken from available federal grant funds or other available funds. (d) The Governor, or his designee, is authorized to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent this Act ( November 12, 2021, SI-R21-025 .)", "num": "17.2.27.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|17|17.2|17.2.27|17.2.27.040", "title": "17.2.27.040 Authorizations", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.27.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/17.2.28", "_type": "page"}}
