{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 19.4.1 Distributions 19.4.1.010 Findings 19.4.1.020 Short Title 19.4.1.030 Purpose 19.4.1.040 Findings 19.4.1.050 Distribution Process Requirements Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R17-001, dated January 18, 2017.", "num": "19.4.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.4|19.4.1", "title": "Part 19.4.1 Distributions", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.4.1.010 Findings (a) The Council finds that it is in the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize distributions of available funds to all members of the Pueblo from time to time. (b) The Council hereby enacts the attached law entitled the \"TRIBAL MEMBER DISTRIBUTION AUTHORIZATION ACT.\" ( January 18, 2017, SI-R17-001 .)", "num": "19.4.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.4|19.4.1|19.4.1.010", "title": "19.4.1.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.4.1.020 Short Title This enactment shall be known as, the \"TRIBAL MEMBER DISTRIBUTION AUTHORIZATION\" (\"Act\"). ( January 18, 2017, SI-R17-001 .)", "num": "19.4.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.4|19.4.1|19.4.1.020", "title": "19.4.1.020 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.4.1.030 Purpose The purpose of the Act is to authorize distributions of money to all members of the Pueblo on an equitable basis when funds for such purposes become available, subject to the appropriation of such funds by the Council. ( January 18, 2017, SI-R17-001 .)", "num": "19.4.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.4|19.4.1|19.4.1.030", "title": "19.4.1.030 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.4.1.040 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) From time to time, the Pueblo receives discretionary funds from various sources including proceeds from lawsuits, settlements, leases, rights-of-way, investment proceeds, and other sources; (b) In the past, the Pueblo has authorized and distributed discretionary funds it has received to all members of the Pueblo; (c) The Council has determined that it is in the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize the distribution of discretionary funds to all members of the Pueblo when such funds become available and no other overriding need exists for the use of such funds. (d) In 2017, the Council enacted the original Tribal Member Distribution Act to provide for an annual distribution of funds to all Members of the Tribe from discretionary funds received from various sources; and (e) since 2017, the Pueblo has authorized and distributed discretionary funds directly to all members of the Pueblo typically at the beginning of each year; and (f) the Council has determined that it is the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize and direct an immediate distribution of discretionary funds to all members of the Pueblo to address the immediate economic hardships caused by the COVID-19 pandemic. (g) Due to the ongoing effects of the COVID-19 pandemic, the Council has determined that it is in the best interest of the Members of the Pueblo to authorize and direct a one-time distribution to begin in June 2021 to members of the Pueblo with a financial incentive to encourage all Members of the Pueblo to obtain a COVID-19 vaccination. ( May 27, 2021, SI-R21-009 ; August 14, 2020, SI-R20-016 ; January 18, 2017, SI-R17-001 .)", "num": "19.4.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.4|19.4.1|19.4.1.040", "title": "19.4.1.040 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.4.1.050 Distribution Process Requirements (a) The Governor is hereby authorized to provide a distribution of funds in an equal amount to all members of the Pueblo when funds for such purposes are specifically appropriated by the Council in an approved Annual Budget or Budget Modification. (b) The Governor shall not be authorized to distribute any funds to members of the Pueblo that have not been specifically appropriated by the Council for such purposes. (c) The Governor shall establish and implement fair and equitable procedures to notify members of the Pueblo of the availability of funds for distribution and to distribute such funds. (d) The Governor is hereby authorized and directed to issue an immediate distribution of funds in an equal amount to all members of the Pueblo from the line item designated for such purposes in the current 2020-2021 Annual Budget. (e) The Governor is hereby authorized and directed to issue a one-time distribution of available funds to members of the Pueblo as follows: (i) Tribal Members enrolled as of April 30, 2021 who are age 15 or younger shall receive $500 distribution; (ii) Tribal Members enrolled as of April 30, 2021 who are over the age of 15 shall receive a $400 distribution; (iii) Tribal Members enrolled as of April 30, 2021 who are over the age of 15 , who have been fully vaccinated and who submit a copy of their CDC vaccination card shall receive an additional $100 distribution; provided, that the deadline for submitting a copy of a CDC vaccination card is September 30, 2021. ( May 27, 2021, SI-R21-009 ; August 14, 2020, SI-R20-016 ; January 18, 2017, SI-R17-001 .)", "num": "19.4.1.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.4|19.4.1|19.4.1.050", "title": "19.4.1.050 Distribution Process Requirements", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 19.5 Master Planning Part 19.5.1 Act Adopting and Ratifying the 2014 Master Land Use Plan Scheme 3 \u00a7\u00a7 19.5.1.010 \u2013 19.5.1.040 Part 19.5.2 Master Land Use Plan Authorization Act \u00a7\u00a7 19.5.2.010 \u2013 19.5.2.040 Part 19.5.3 Approving and Adopting the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Comprehensive Land Use Plan of 2022 \u00a7\u00a7 19.5.3.010 \u2013 19.5.3.040 Part 19.5.4 Emergency Response Development Act \u00a7\u00a7 19.5.4.010 \u2013 19.5.4.040", "num": "19.5", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5", "title": "Chapter 19.5 Master Planning", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 19.5.1 Act Adopting and Ratifying the 2014 Master Land Use Plan Scheme 3 19.5.1.010 Short Title 19.5.1.020 Purpose 19.5.1.030 Findings 19.5.1.040 Authorizations", "num": "19.5.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.1", "title": "Part 19.5.1 Act Adopting and Ratifying the 2014 Master Land Use Plan Scheme 3", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.1.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"ACT ADOPTING AND RATIFYING THE 2014 MASTER LAND USE PLAN SCHEME 3 (\"Act\").\" ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 .)", "num": "19.5.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.1|19.5.1.010", "title": "19.5.1.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.1.020 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to adopt and ratify a selection of one of the \"Schemes (schematics)\" from the 3 Schemes (options) outlined in the 2014 Master Land Use Plan, a study which was contracted through the Northern Pueblos Housing Authority and prepared for the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 .)", "num": "19.5.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.1|19.5.1.020", "title": "19.5.1.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.1.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) The Pueblo, through the Northern Pueblos Housing Authority, contracted a study by Indigenous Design Studio + Architecture, LLC, to examine land use within the Pueblo boundaries, and as a result, the 2014 Land Use Plan (report) was developed. (b) The 2014 Land Use Plan has been provided to the Pueblo de San Ildefonso through both hard copy and electronic forms, provided to the Executive and Legislative Branches, as well as housed at the Northern Pueblos Housing Authority offices. (c) The 2014 Land Use Plan that was prepared for the Pueblo identifies 3 Schemes (or schematics) as options for use as a foundation to do further, detailed land use planning. (d) The Council understands that none of the 3 Schemes currently fit the dynamic of the stages of planning and development that has been and is occurring since the document was presented in 2014, however, in order to continue enhancing and preparing for planning, preparation and development, one selection is needed to move forward. (e) In order for pueblo to proceed into the next phase of developing a Master Community Land Use Plan, the Council needs to select one \"Scheme\" from the 2014 Land Use Plan as a basis to work off of and to use as a framework for long-term planning. (f) The Council has determined the need to adopt and ratify a selection of one of the schematics from three (3) viable alternatives that were provided and discussed. (g) The Council has chosen to adopt and ratify the selection of 'Scheme 3' for use in development of the Master Community Plan. A copy of Scheme 3 is attached as Exhibit A. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 .)", "num": "19.5.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.1|19.5.1.030", "title": "19.5.1.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.1.040 Authorizations The Council hereby approves and adopts this resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor or his designee to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this resolution. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 .)", "num": "19.5.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.1|19.5.1.040", "title": "19.5.1.040 Authorizations", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 19.5.2 Master Land Use Plan Authorization Act 19.5.2.010 Short Title 19.5.2.020 Purpose 19.5.2.030 Findings 19.5.2.040 Master Land Use Plan", "num": "19.5.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.2", "title": "Part 19.5.2 Master Land Use Plan Authorization Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.2.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"MASTER LAND USE PLAN AUTHORIZATION ACT.\" ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; June 15, 2021, SI-R21-012 .)", "num": "19.5.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.2|19.5.2.010", "title": "19.5.2.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.2.020 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to authorize and direct the completion of a Master Land Use Plan to identify and analyze the Pueblo's lands, including existing and proposed uses, in order to make well-informed land use decisions. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; June 15, 2021, SI-R21-012 .)", "num": "19.5.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.2|19.5.2.020", "title": "19.5.2.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.2.030 Findings (a) The population of the Pueblo is increasing putting pressure on existing land uses including the need for additional land for housing, economic development, and other purposes; and (b) The Pueblo has some land parcels available that could be utilized for new housing and other purposes; however, these land parcels often lack adequate infrastructure; and (c) The Pueblo has issued land assignments to members of the Pueblo initially for farming purposes although some members and their descendants have utilized or desire to utilize their land assignments for non-farming purposes; and (d) Many years ago, the Pueblo completed a Land Use Plan that began to analyze the current and proposed future uses of the Pueblo's lands; however, the Plan was incomplete, flawed, and is now outdated; and (e) The Pueblo finds the need to identify lands that are available for economic development, housing, and other purposes while taking into account the impacts any development will likely have on neighboring lands, existing land uses, the natural environment, culturally- sensitive areas, aesthetics, infrastructure, utilities, and the overall policies established by the Pueblo; and (f) The Pueblo has identified the need to commission a new, comprehensive, Master Land Use Plan to professionally study and analyze the Pueblo's lands, including existing and proposed uses, in order to make well-informed decisions regarding the current and future land uses and zoning. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; June 15, 2021, SI-R21-012 .)", "num": "19.5.2.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.2|19.5.2.030", "title": "19.5.2.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.2.040 Master Land Use Plan The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) The Council hereby authorizes and directs the Governor to negotiate and execute a contract or contracts to engage professional services to conduct and complete a Master Land Use Plan for the Pueblo including necessary services to assist with the preparation of a professional Request for Proposal for the Master Land Use Plan contractor; and (b) The Master Land Use Plan shall include an up-to-date and comprehensive analysis of the lands held by the Pueblo, and shall include recommendations for land preservation and conservation, housing development, and economic development activities; and (c) The Master Land Use Plan shall include an analysis of current land uses, current land policies and practices, proposed land uses, rights-of-way, easements, public property, private property interests including leases and assignments, and any zoning or similar requirements; and (d) The Governor shall notify the Council of the estimated cost of contracting for the Master Land Use Plan. The Council hereby authorizes up to $100,000 for the completion of the Master Land Use Plan, subject to an appropriation of funds in the Annual Budget or in a Budget Modification. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; June 15, 2021, SI-R21-012 .)", "num": "19.5.2.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.2|19.5.2.040", "title": "19.5.2.040 Master Land Use Plan", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.2.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 19.5.3 Approving and Adopting the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Comprehensive Land Use Plan of 2022 19.5.3.010 Short Title 19.5.3.020 Purpose 19.5.3.030 Findings 19.5.3.040 Authorization", "num": "19.5.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.3", "title": "Part 19.5.3 Approving and Adopting the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Comprehensive Land Use Plan of 2022", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.3.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"PUEBLO DE SAN ILDEFONSO COMREHENSIVE LAND USE PLAN OF 2022.\" ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; October 24, 2022, SI-R22-017 .)", "num": "19.5.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.3|19.5.3.010", "title": "19.5.3.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.3.020 Purpose The purpose of this resolution is to approve the Comprehensive Land Use Plan of 2022 for a short-term and long-term planning guide for the Pueblo. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; October 24, 2022, SI-R22-017 .)", "num": "19.5.3.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.3|19.5.3.020", "title": "19.5.3.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.3.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) the Pueblo de San Ildefonso (Pueblo) received $50,000 from the New Mexico State Legislature in 2018 to \"Design and Construct Phase 4 of a wastewater collection system (IGA Number 609-18-C2364); and, (b) on July 27, 2021 per House Bill 296, Laws of 2021, Chapter 139 Section 72, funds were reauthorized to \"Plan and Develop a Comprehensive Land use Plan\" (IGA Number 609-21-F4070); and, (c) IGA Number 609-21-F4070 to \"Plan and Develop a Comprehensive Land Use Plan\" expires on June 30, 2023; and (d) on November 30, 2021 the Pueblo entered in to a Contract Agreement with Sites Southwest LLC, Santa Fe, NM, to complete the Comprehensive Land Use Plan; and (e) Sites Southwest, LLC has worked with the Pueblo's Programs and Administration over the past nine months and has completed the final draft of the Comprehensive Land Use Plan (CLUP); and (f) the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Council approves the Comprehensive Land Use Plan with the intention that the Plan is a working document serving as a short and long-term planning guide for the Pueblo. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; October 24, 2022, SI-R22-017 .)", "num": "19.5.3.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.3|19.5.3.030", "title": "19.5.3.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.3.040 Authorization The Council hereby approves and adopts the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Comprehensive Land Use Plan of 2022. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; October 24, 2022, SI-R22-017 .)", "num": "19.5.3.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.3|19.5.3.040", "title": "19.5.3.040 Authorization", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.3.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 19.5.4 Emergency Response Development Act 19.5.4.010 Short Title 19.5.4.020 Purpose 19.5.4.030 Findings 19.5.4.040 Authorizations", "num": "19.5.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.4", "title": "Part 19.5.4 Emergency Response Development Act", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.4.010 Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"Emergency Response Development Act\" (\"Act\"). ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; January 3, 2023, SI-R22-026 .)", "num": "19.5.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.4|19.5.4.010", "title": "19.5.4.010 Short Title", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.4.020 Purpose The purpose of this Act is to further develop, update and implement the Pueblo's Emergency Response Plan and to prepare and protect the Pueblo and its People, Employees and Visitors from natural disasters and various emergencies. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; January 3, 2023, SI-R22-026 .)", "num": "19.5.4.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.4|19.5.4.020", "title": "19.5.4.020 Purpose", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.4.030 Findings The Council hereby finds and declares that: (a) the Pueblo de San Ildefonso has several outdated Emergency Management Plans dating back to December 2001 and 2006; and (b) the Pueblo de San Ildefonso must prepare and protect its People, Employees and visitors from natural disasters, pandemics and infectious diseases, facility emergencies, and etc.; and (c) the Pueblo has identified the need to update and further develop its Emergency Response Plan to better care for the community, lands and infrastructure and to protect cultural resources, sites, and residential and traditional homes; and (d) there are appropriate resources through Federal, State, Municipal and Tribal, most recent plans available, and all other resources in the past 10-15 years, which can and need to be utilized to assist in this development; and (e) the Pueblo has identified the need to enact a law to allow the Governor and Tribal Administration to work with the Tribal Council to develop, update and implement an Emergency Response plan to protect the People and Pueblo. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; January 3, 2023, SI-R22-026 .)", "num": "19.5.4.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.4|19.5.4.030", "title": "19.5.4.030 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 19.5.4.040 Authorizations The Tribal Council hereby, (a) directs that appropriate departments or programs shall review their budgets, as well as all federal and state funds needed to be reviewed to collaborate and ensure that emergency response plans are collaborative and cohesive to include all departments and agencies; and, (b) directs the Governor and Tribal Administration to utilize and exhaust all outside sources of funding before utilizing Tribal Funds (General Fund); and, (c) directs the Governor and Tribal Administration to research and utilize all available funding avenues for this Emergency Response development; and, (d) directs the Governor and Tribal Administration to ensure that Safety is the priority and appropriate steps are taken to develop a budget and provide a draft plan by April 28, 2023 and provide bi-annual updates to the Tribal Council thereafter; and, (e) directs that Tribal Council approval be required for the implementation of an Emergency Response Plan here in the Pueblo de San Ildefonso and that this plan shall be reviewed yearly and as needed to ensure safety updates are made on all structures and vehicles; and, (f) approves and adopts this resolution in accordance with the requirements of the Agreement, according to published Council procedures, and authorizes and directs the Governor or his designee to take such actions as deemed necessary to carry out the intent of this resolution. ( July 8, 2017, SI-R17-020 ; January 3, 2023, SI-R22-026 .)", "num": "19.5.4.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|19|19.5|19.5.4|19.5.4.040", "title": "19.5.4.040 Authorizations", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.5.4.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Title 20 LIQUOR Chapter 20.1 Liquor \u00a7\u00a7 20.1.1.010 \u2013 20.1.5.050", "num": "20", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20", "title": "Title 20 LIQUOR", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 20.1 Liquor Part 20.1.1 Background \u00a7\u00a7 20.1.1.010 \u2013 20.1.1.040 Part 20.1.2 ADMINISTRATION \u00a7\u00a7 20.1.2.010 \u2013 20.1.2.050 Part 20.1.3 SALE OF LIQUOR; RESTRICTED AREAS \u00a7\u00a7 20.1.3.010 \u2013 20.1.3.050 Part 20.1.4 OFFENSES, ENFORCEMENT AND PENALTIES \u00a7\u00a7 20.1.4.010 \u2013 20.1.4.060 Part 20.1.5 Miscellaneous \u00a7\u00a7 20.1.5.010 \u2013 20.1.5.050 Editor's Notes This law was originally enacted pursuant to Council Resolution No. SI-R15-004, dated March 29, 2015.", "num": "20.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1", "title": "Chapter 20.1 Liquor", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 20.1.1 Background 20.1.1.010 Findings 20.1.1.020 20.1.1.030 20.1.1.040", "num": "20.1.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.1", "title": "Part 20.1.1 Background", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.1.010 Findings (a) The Council desires to regulate the sale, possession and consumption of liquor within the Pueblo lands; (b) The Council has determined that the management of such should be through the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Liquor Control Act of 2015. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.1|20.1.1.010", "title": "20.1.1.010 Findings", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.1.020 Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Council hereby enacts the attached law entitled \"Pueblo de San Ildefonso Liquor Control Act of 2015.\" ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.1|20.1.1.020", "title": "20.1.1.020", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.1.030 Any and all Tribal Council resolution or provisions in the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Law and Order Code which conflict in any way with the provisions of this Act are hereby repealed to the extent they are inconsistent with or conflict with or are contrary to the spirit and/or purpose of this Act. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.1|20.1.1.030", "title": "20.1.1.030", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.1.040 Pueblo de San Ildefonso Liquor Control Act of 2015 ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.1.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.1|20.1.1.040", "title": "20.1.1.040", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.1.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 20.1.2 ADMINISTRATION 20.1.2.010 Title. 20.1.2.020 Purpose. 20.1.2.030 Authority. 20.1.2.040 Definitions. 20.1.2.050 Tribal Liquor License.", "num": "20.1.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.2", "title": "Part 20.1.2 ADMINISTRATION", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.2.010 Title. This Act shall be known as the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Liquor Act. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.2|20.1.2.010", "title": "20.1.2.010 Title.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.2.020 Purpose. The purpose of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Liquor Act is to regulate and control the sale, possession, and consumption of liquor within the Pueblo de San Ildefonso lands for the public health, safety, and welfare. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.2|20.1.2.020", "title": "20.1.2.020 Purpose.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.2.030 Authority. The Pueblo has enacted this Liquor Act in exercise of its inherent governmental authority over its lands and activities occurring thereon and in accordance with its governing Agreement, The Government, Section 5. Authority. This Liquor Act is in conformance with the laws of New Mexico, as required by Federal law and 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1161. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.2.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.2|20.1.2.030", "title": "20.1.2.030 Authority.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.2.040 Definitions. As used in this Act, the following terms shall apply: (a) \"Alcohol\" or \"Liquor\" includes the four varieties of liquor commonly referred to as alcohol, spirits, wine, and beer, and all fermented, spirituous, vinous, or malt liquor, or combinations thereof, and mixed liquor, a part of which is fermented, spirituous, vinous, or malt liquor or otherwise intoxicating, and every liquor or solid or semisolid or other substance, patented or not, containing alcohol, spirits, wine, or beer. (b) \"Council\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Council. (c) \"Governor\" means the Governor of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso, or his or her designee. (d) \"Licensed premises\" means the location within Pueblo lands at which a licensee is permitted to sell and allow the consumption of liquor. Includes such buildings and surrounding land as designated in the liquor license. (e) \"Licensee\" means a person who has been issued tribal liquor license by the Pueblo, to sell liquor on the licensed premises under the provisions of this Act. (f) \"Minor\" means any person under the age of twenty-one (21) years. (g) \"Package sale\" means any sale of liquor in a container or containers filled or packed by a manufacturer or wine bottler and sold by a liquor licensee in an unbroken package for consumption off the licensed liquor establishment premises, and not for resale. (h) \"Person\" means any individual, business, or other legal entity, and includes the Pueblo and its wholly owned commercial entities. (i) \"Pueblo\" means the Pueblo de San Ildefonso, a federally recognized Tribe of Indians. (j) \"Public place\" means any location or premises on Pueblo lands to which the general public has unrestricted access. (k) \"Pueblo de San Ildefonso lands\" means all lands within the exterior boundaries of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso, including rights-of-way, lands owned by or for the benefit of the Pueblo, tribally purchased lands, and lands that may be leased by the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. Also referred to as \"Pueblo Lands.\" (l) \"Sale\" or \"sales\" means the exchange, barter, donation, selling, supplying, or distribution of liquor. (m) \"Server\" means a person who sells, serves or dispenses liquor for consumption on or off licensed premises, and includes persons who manage, direct or control the sale or service of liquor. (n) \"Tribal Court\" means the trial court of the Pueblo. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.2.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.2|20.1.2.040", "title": "20.1.2.040 Definitions.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.2.050 Tribal Liquor License. (a) Every person who sells liquor on Pueblo lands must hold a tribal liquor license issued by the Pueblo for each location on Pueblo Lands where liquor is sold. (b) A liquor license shall not be transferred, sold or assigned and is only valid for the licensed premises identified on the License. (c) A liquor license shall designate whether the licensed premises is permitted to have package sales and/or by the drink. (d) The Pueblo in its discretion may place terms, conditions, and/or restrictions on the sale of liquor at licensed premises, including, but not limited to, the hours and days of operation and the type of liquor sold. (e) The term of a liquor license shall be two (2) years. (f) All persons issued a Liquor License shall: (1) prominently display the license in the business location; (2) be responsible for the sale of liquor on Pueblo Lands by their business, and for the conduct of his or her officers, agents, and employees in relation to the sale of liquor; (3) ensure that all servers have successfully completed, within the past three (3) years, an alcohol server education program and examination approved by the director of the New Mexico Alcohol and Gaming Division. (4) ensure all handling, stocking, and sale of liquor shall be made by persons twenty-one (21) years of age or older. Proof of age must be shown by a current and valid state driver's license, tribal identification card, or other government issued identification that contains birth date and photo of the holder of the license or identification. (g) Any person licensed to sell liquor within the Pueblo shall obtain general public liability insurance insuring the licensee and the Pueblo against any claims, losses or liability whatsoever for any acts or omissions of the licensee or business invitee on the licensed premises resulting in injury, loss or damage to any other party, with coverage limits in the amount not less than $1,000,000 (one million dollars) per occurrence. (h) The Pueblo has the authority to suspend, revoke or terminate a Tribal liquor license for any violations arising from this Act or other Pueblo Criminal and Civil Code violations. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.2.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.2|20.1.2.050", "title": "20.1.2.050 Tribal Liquor License.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.2.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 20.1.3 SALE OF LIQUOR; RESTRICTED AREAS 20.1.3.010 Sales Limited. 20.1.3.020 Sales for Personal Use; Resale Prohibited. 20.1.3.030 Right to Refuse Sale. 20.1.3.040 Acceptable Proof of Age for Purchase. 20.1.3.050 Liquor in Undesignated Areas.", "num": "20.1.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.3", "title": "Part 20.1.3 SALE OF LIQUOR; RESTRICTED AREAS", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.3.010 Sales Limited. Sales of liquor are allowed at the following locations only: (a) The Pueblo's convenience stores. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.3|20.1.3.010", "title": "20.1.3.010 Sales Limited.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.3.020 Sales for Personal Use; Resale Prohibited. All sales allowed by this Act shall be for personal use of the individual purchaser. Such sales for personal non-commercial use must be in package form or by the drink. Resale of any liquor by a person not licensed under this Act is prohibited. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.3.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.3|20.1.3.020", "title": "20.1.3.020 Sales for Personal Use; Resale Prohibited.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.3.030 Right to Refuse Sale. Any person authorized to sell liquor within the Pueblo shall have the authority to refuse to sell liquor to any person unable to produce proof of age and identity, or to any person who appears intoxicated. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.3.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.3|20.1.3.030", "title": "20.1.3.030 Right to Refuse Sale.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.3.040 Acceptable Proof of Age for Purchase. If there is a question of a Person's age to purchase liquor, such person shall be required to present any one of the following identification cards which shows his or her correct age and bears his or her signature and photograph: (a) A driver's license of any state or identification card issued by any state department of motor vehicles; (b) United States active duty military ID; (c) A passport; (d) An official identification or tribal membership card issued by a federally recognized tribe. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.3.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.3|20.1.3.040", "title": "20.1.3.040 Acceptable Proof of Age for Purchase.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.3.050 Liquor in Undesignated Areas. The sale and possession of liquor in areas of the Pueblo Lands which are not designated or licensed for the sale and possession of liquor pursuant to this Act is prohibited. (a) This prohibition does not pertain to the otherwise lawful transportation of liquor through Pueblo de San Ildefonso lands by persons remaining upon public highways or other areas paved for motor vehicles and where such liquor is not delivered, sold or offered for sale to anyone within Pueblo Lands. (b) This prohibition does not pertain to liquor wholesalers selling, transporting or delivering liquor to a person licensed by the Pueblo to sell liquor, or to a location designated for the sale of liquor. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.3.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.3|20.1.3.050", "title": "20.1.3.050 Liquor in Undesignated Areas.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.3.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 20.1.4 OFFENSES, ENFORCEMENT AND PENALTIES 20.1.4.010 Offenses. 20.1.4.020 Enforcement Powers and Authorities. 20.1.4.030 Civil Penalty. 20.1.4.040 Criminal Penalty. 20.1.4.050 Exclusion. 20.1.4.060 Contraband.", "num": "20.1.4", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.4", "title": "Part 20.1.4 OFFENSES, ENFORCEMENT AND PENALTIES", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.4.010 Offenses. Any person who violates this Act is subject to a civil penalty, at a minimum. Offenses include, but are not limited to, the following: (a) No person under the age of twenty-one (21) shall consume, purchase, attempt to purchase, or have in his or her possession any liquor. Any person violating this section shall be guilty of a separate violation of this Act for each container acquired, bought or possessed. (b) Any person who sells, provides, or attempts to sell or provide any liquor to any person under the age of twenty-one (21) shall be guilty of violation of this Act for each sale or drink provided. (c) Any person who transfers in any manner an identification of age to a minor for purposes of permitting such minor to obtain liquor shall be guilty of a violation of this Act. (d) Any person who attempts to purchase liquor through the use of a false or altered identification shall be guilty of a violation of this Act. (e) It shall be a violation of this Act for any person within Pueblo Lands to buy liquor from any person other than those properly authorized and licensed by the Pueblo and in compliance with this Act. (f) It shall be a violation of this Act for any person within Pueblo Lands to sell liquor without a license. (g) It shall be a violation of this Act for any person licensed by this Act to sell liquor off of the licensed premises. (h) Any person who is not licensed pursuant to this Act who purchases liquor on Pueblo Lands and resells it, whether in the original container or not, shall be guilty of a violation of this Act. (i) It shall be a violation of this Act for any person to sell liquor to a person who is visibly intoxicated or appears to be intoxicated. (j) It shall be a violation of this Act for any person to sell or possess any liquor in any area of the Pueblo's lands which is not designated or licensed for the sale and possession of liquor pursuant to this Act. (k) Any person who violates any other provision of this Act shall be guilty of a violation of this Act. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.4.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.4|20.1.4.010", "title": "20.1.4.010 Offenses.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.4.020 Enforcement Powers and Authorities. The Governor, or his or her designee, shall have the following powers and authorities for the enforcement of this Act: (a) To adopt rules, regulations or polices necessary to carry out the intent of this Act to regulate and control the sale, possession and consumption of liquor. (b) To inspect all licensed premises on which liquor is sold, consumed, possessed or distributed at all reasonable times for the purposes of ascertaining whether the requirements of this Act and any rules or regulations promulgated under this Act are being met and adhered to. (c) To work with the Tribal Prosecutor or Law Enforcement Officer to bring proceedings in Tribal Court to enforce this Act, and any related rules or regulations, as necessary. (d) To suspend, revoke or terminate a liquor license for any violations arising from this Act or other Pueblo Criminal and Civil Code violations. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.4.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.4|20.1.4.020", "title": "20.1.4.020 Enforcement Powers and Authorities.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.4.030 Civil Penalty. Any person, purchasing, possessing, selling, delivering, bartering, or manufacturing liquor products in violation of any part of this Act, or of any rule or regulation adopted pursuant to this Act, shall be subject to a civil assessment of not more than five thousand dollars ($5,000) for each violation. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.4.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.4|20.1.4.030", "title": "20.1.4.030 Civil Penalty.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.4.040 Criminal Penalty. In addition to civil penalties, a person may be subject to criminal prosecution by the Pueblo for the purchasing, possessing, selling, delivering, bartering, or manufacturing liquor products in violation of any part of this Act, or of any rule or regulation adopted pursuant to this Act. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.4.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.4|20.1.4.040", "title": "20.1.4.040 Criminal Penalty.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.4.050 Exclusion. For good and sufficient cause found, the Tribal Court may exclude from the Pueblo Lands any person who engages in an activity or activities prohibited by this Act to the extend such exclusion is not inconsistent with Pueblo law. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.4.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.4|20.1.4.050", "title": "20.1.4.050 Exclusion.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.4.060 Contraband. Any liquor that is possessed contrary to the terms of this Act are declared to be contraband. Any tribal agent, employee or officer who is authorized by the Governor to enforce this Act shall have the authority to, and shall seize all contraband. Any officer seizing contraband shall preserve the contraband in accordance with the applicable law of the Pueblo or state law. Upon being found in violation of this Act by the Tribal Court, the person shall forfeit all right, title, and interest in the items seized and they shall become the property of the Pueblo. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.4.060", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.4|20.1.4.060", "title": "20.1.4.060 Contraband.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.4.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 20.1.5 Miscellaneous 20.1.5.010 Effective Date. 20.1.5.020 Repeal of Inconsistent Law or Provisions. 20.1.5.030 Severability. 20.1.5.040 Amendment. 20.1.5.050 Sovereign Immunity.", "num": "20.1.5", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.5", "title": "Part 20.1.5 Miscellaneous", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.5.010 Effective Date. This Act shall take effect upon the date of publication in the Federal Register by the Secretary of the Interior or the Secretary's designee. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.5.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.5|20.1.5.010", "title": "20.1.5.010 Effective Date.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.5.020 Repeal of Inconsistent Law or Provisions. The Pueblo's Ordinance Legalizing the Introduction, Possession and Sale of Intoxicants, dated January 15, 1976 and published in the January 22, 1976 Federal Register is hereby repealed in its entirety. Further, any and all Council resolutions, or provisions in the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Civil and Criminal Code, or other laws, which conflict in any way with the provisions of this Act are hereby repealed to the extent that they are inconsistent with or conflict with or are contrary to the spirit and/or purpose of this Act. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.5.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.5|20.1.5.020", "title": "20.1.5.020 Repeal of Inconsistent Law or Provisions.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.5.030 Severability. If any provision of this Act is found to be unconstitutional or unlawful by the Pueblo de San Ildefonso Tribal Courts or Federal Courts, such provision(s) shall be stricken and the remainder of this Act shall continue in full force and effect. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.5.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.5|20.1.5.030", "title": "20.1.5.030 Severability.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.5.040 Amendment. The Council may amend this Act upon majority vote of the Council, subject to the publication in the Federal Register by the Secretary of the Interior or his designee. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.5.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.5|20.1.5.040", "title": "20.1.5.040 Amendment.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 20.1.5.050 Sovereign Immunity. Nothing in this Act shall be construed as a waiver of sovereign immunity or rights of the Pueblo. ( March 29, 2015, SI-R15-004 .)", "num": "20.1.5.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|20|20.1|20.1.5|20.1.5.050", "title": "20.1.5.050 Sovereign Immunity.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/20.1.5.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Title 21 PROBATE Chapter 21.1 Probate \u00a7\u00a7 21.1.1.010 \u2013 21.1.3.050 Chapter 21.2 Descent and Distribution \u00a7\u00a7 21.2.1.010 \u2013 21.2.1.030", "num": "21", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21", "title": "Title 21 PROBATE", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 21.1 Probate Part 21.1.1 Probate Procedure \u00a7\u00a7 21.1.1.010 \u2013 21.1.1.010 Part 21.1.2 Small Estates \u00a7\u00a7 21.1.2.010 \u2013 21.1.2.030 Part 21.1.3 Administration \u00a7\u00a7 21.1.3.010 \u2013 21.1.3.050", "num": "21.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1", "title": "Chapter 21.1 Probate", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 21.1.1 Probate Procedure 21.1.1.010 Jurisdiction", "num": "21.1.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.1", "title": "Part 21.1.1 Probate Procedure", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.1.010 Jurisdiction (a) When a member of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso or any other person residing in the jurisdiction of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso dies intestate, the heirs of the decedent, the claims of the creditors, and the distribution of the estate shall be determined by the San Ildefonso Trial Court under this Code. The jurisdiction of the Court in such cases covers all of the decedent's property that is located anywhere within the territorial jurisdiction of the Trial Court except property and funds which are restricted or held in trust by the Federal Government. All proceedings under the Probate Code shall be conducted under the Riles of Civil Procedure of this Code. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.1|21.1.1.010", "title": "21.1.1.010 Jurisdiction", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 21.1.2 Small Estates 21.1.2.010 Small Estates. 21.1.2.020 Information Required. 21.1.2.030 Findings and Final Order.", "num": "21.1.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.2", "title": "Part 21.1.2 Small Estates", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.2.010 Small Estates. Any interested person may file a petition with the Clerk of the Court for the distribution, without administration of estate of a decedent who died testate or intestate and in which the total estate consisting of nontrust property not exceeding $5,000.00 in value, provided that the decedent is survived by a widow or widower or by one (1) or more minor children, otherwise the procedures of Chapters 30 and 31 of this Title shall be followed. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.2.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.2|21.1.2.010", "title": "21.1.2.010 Small Estates.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.2.020 Information Required. The petition for distribution of a small estate shall contain the information required by Sec. 30.5. The petition shall be sworn to before the Clerk of the Court or other officer authorized to administer oaths. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.2.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.2|21.1.2.020", "title": "21.1.2.020 Information Required.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.2.030 Findings and Final Order. If the Court finds that the estate does not exceed $5,000.00 in value, and that more than thirty (30) days have elapsed since the death of the decedent, the Court may order the estate distributed pursuant to the decedent's will, if any, or according to t e rules of the descent and distribution of this Title. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.2.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.2|21.1.2.030", "title": "21.1.2.030 Findings and Final Order.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.2.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 21.1.3 Administration 21.1.3.010 Petition for Administrator or Executor. 21.1.3.020 Wills. 21.1.3.030 Appraisal of Property. 21.1.3.040 Claims. 21.1.3.050 Administration of Estate.", "num": "21.1.3", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.3", "title": "Part 21.1.3 Administration", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.3.010 Petition for Administrator or Executor. (a) Immediately upon the death of a member of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso and prior to appointment of the executor or administrator, the Court shall have authority to seal the estate, including all belongings and property, of the decedent, and to appoint a caretaker to take possession and control of the property of the decedent, and to care for and maintain the property. (b) Any person claiming to be the heir of any member of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso or any other person residing on the Pueblo of San Ildefonso or surviving spouse of the decedent, surviving children, creditors, or the Pueblo may file a petition for the appointment of an executor, if there is a will, or administrator of the estate with the Clerk of the Trial Court. All procedures shall be conducted accordance with the Civil Procedures of this Code. (c) The Court shall thereupon appoint an administrator or executor of the estate who shall take possession and control of the property of the decedent from the caretaker until the administration of the estate has been completed and he has been discharged by order of the Court. (d) It shall be the duty of the executor or administrator to preserve and protect the property for the benefit of the estate and heirs. (e) Upon petition of the caretaker, administrator or executor, the Court may authorize the unsealing of the estate, including all belongings and property, for the purposes of a traditional give-away under the customs of the Pueblo of San Ildefonso; however, only persons designated by the decedent or eligible under Pueblo custom and tradition shall be eligible to take. (f) Reasonable maintenance may be authorized by the Court to any surviving spouse or surviving minor children pending settlement of the estate. (g) The caretaker, administrator or executor shall petition the Court for the appointment of guardians for any minor children or any person deemed to be incompetent who may be probable heirs or devisees of the decedent. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.3.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.3|21.1.3.010", "title": "21.1.3.010 Petition for Administrator or Executor.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.3.020 Wills. Every custodian of a will must deliver the will to the Trial Court within five (5) days of the death of its maker. Failure to do so may subject that person to the damages sustained by any person injured thereby. (a) A will may be proved by the affidavit of two (2) attesting witnesses identifying the signature of the testator and affirming that the will was executed by the decedent in the presence of the witnesses and declared by him to be his last will and testament. (b) In the event that any person contests the validity of the will, the Court shall take no further action except to set a date for a hearing to establish the validity of the will and until the Court rules on the validity of the will. (c) Upon the completion of the hearing or hearings regarding the validity of the will, the Judge of the Trial Court shall either affirm the will and order it admitted to probate or reject the will and order the administration of the decedent's estate as if the decedent had died intestate without executing the will. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.3.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.3|21.1.3.020", "title": "21.1.3.020 Wills.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.3.030 Appraisal of Property. When any action is filed under this Title for the probate of a decedent's estate, the Court shall appoint a qualified appraiser to appraise all of the property within the jurisdiction of the Court who shall file the appraisal report with the Clerk of the Court. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.3.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.3|21.1.3.030", "title": "21.1.3.030 Appraisal of Property.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.3.040 Claims. Creditors of the estate or those having a claim against the decedent shall file their claim with the Clerk of the Court or the executor or administrator within sixty (60) days from official notice of the appointment of the executor or administrator published locally by the press or posting of signs at the Tribal and other offices, giving appropriate notice for the filing of claims. (a) The Court or Administrator or executor shall examine all claims within ninety (90) days of his appointment and notify the claimant whether his claim is accepted or rejected. If the claimant is notified of rejection, the claimant any appeal to the Trial Court before the date set for distribution of the estate for determination of the appeal at the distribution hearing. (b) Claims shall be preferred in the following order: (1) All reasonable expenses of last illness and burial. (2) Reasonable expenses of administration. (3) All other claims, including claims filed by agencies of the State and Federal Government. (4) Any amount due the Pueblo of San Ildefonso, including notice of all Tribal liens on any part of the estate of the decedent. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.3.040", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.3|21.1.3.040", "title": "21.1.3.040 Claims.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.1.3.050 Administration of Estate. (a) Within one-hundred (100) days after the appointment of the executor or administrator, he shall file a petition for the determination of heirs and distribution of the estate. (b) The petition shall be filed in duplicate and shall be sworn to or affirmed and shall contain: (1) The name of decedent. (2) Place and date of decedent's death. (3) Names, ages, and relationship to decedent of all heirs of decedent and, if decedent dies testate names, ages, and relationship, if any, of all beneficiaries under his will. (4) Nature and extent of decedent's property and location of same. (5) State of existence or absence of will with attachment of original will if decedent dies testate. (6) Copy of death certificate or other adequate proof of death. (7) Statement of all claims including those approved or rejected for payment. (8) A certificate of heirs signed by the Tribal Official in charge of Tribal Census Records. (9) Proof of service on persons personally served, names of persons served by mail, and the number of notices posted and their location. (10) The Court may file a petition for the determination of heirs and distribution of the estate in its own motion in the event an executor or administrator is not appointed or fails to act as required. (1984 Code.)", "num": "21.1.3.050", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.1|21.1.3|21.1.3.050", "title": "21.1.3.050 Administration of Estate.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.1.3.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Chapter 21.2 Descent and Distribution Part 21.2.1 Determination of the Court \u00a7\u00a7 21.2.1.010 \u2013 21.2.1.030", "num": "21.2", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.2", "title": "Chapter 21.2 Descent and Distribution", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Part 21.2.1 Determination of the Court 21.2.1.010 Determination of the Court. 21.2.1.020 Descent and Distribution. 21.2.1.030 Expenses and Fees.", "num": "21.2.1", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.2|21.2.1", "title": "Part 21.2.1 Determination of the Court", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.2.1.010 Determination of the Court. At the time set for hearing, the Trial Court shall proceed to examine all evidence relating to the distribution of the decedent's estate and determine any controversy relating to claims or as to those entitled to receive the decedent's estate. Upon conclusion of the hearing, the Court shall: (a) Enter its order determining the heirs or devisees. (b) Provide for payment of approved claims. (c) Provide for distribution of the decedent's estate by the executor or administrator as ordered by the Court. (d) Require a report in thirty (30) days from any executor or administrator that he has carried out the orders of the Court. (e) Discharge the executor or administrator and close the estate upon finding that the executor or administrator has faithfully discharged his duties.", "num": "21.2.1.010", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.2|21.2.1|21.2.1.010", "title": "21.2.1.010 Determination of the Court.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.2.1.020 Descent and Distribution. In the event there is no will admitted to probation and there is no Pueblo custom or ordinance to the contrary recognized by the Court, the estate shall be distributed by order of the Court as follows: (a) If a husband or wife survives and there is no issue over the age of eighteen (18) years, the husband or wife shall take the entire estate. (b) If a husband or wife survives and an issue over the age of eighteen (18) survives, the surviving husband or wife shall take one-half (1) and the balance is divided equally among the surviving issue over the age of eighteen (18) years. (c) Issue is any direct descendent of deceased person, whether child, grandchild, great-grandchild or more remote descendent. (d) If no husband or wife survives, the surviving children will take the entire estate in equal shares. (e) If neither husband or wife or issue survives, the parents of the decedent will take all of the estate, sharing it equally if both survive or the survivor taking all if but one (1) survives. (f) If no spouse, issue or father or mother survives, the brothers and sisters shall inherit in equal shares, except that if pre-deceased brothers and sisters left issue, the issue shall share equally in the interest of their predeceased parent. (g) If no spouse, issue, father or mother, brother or sister or nephew or niece or decedent survives the estate shall escheat or pass to the Pueblo of San Ildefonso. (h) An illegitimate child shall inherit from his mother the same as if born in lawful wedlock and shall inherit also from the person who, in writing and before a competent attesting witness, shall have declared himself to be his father or found to be the father in a paternity suit. (i) Adoptive children and parents shall share in the same manner as natural children and parents. (j) Family heirlooms, artifacts, articles or traditional or religious significance may be funeral gifted by or shall descend to the closest enrolled San Ildefonso male relative by blood of a paternal decedent and to the closest enrolled San Ildefonso Pueblo female relative by blood of a maternal decedent. (k) Any person who pleads guilty to or is convicted of homicide or murder of the first or second degree of the decedent, under any state or federal law, shall not be eligible to inherit any part of the decedent's estate under this Code by law, Pueblo custom or will of the decedent, and all property, including any trust property that must pass will escheat to the Tribe if there are no other heirs at law.", "num": "21.2.1.020", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.2|21.2.1|21.2.1.020", "title": "21.2.1.020 Descent and Distribution.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code 21.2.1.030 Expenses and Fees. After the payment of all expenses in connection with the distribution of the estate, the Court may charge such fees as may be deemed proper taking into consideration the appraised value of the estate of the decedent, but not to exceed $500.00.", "num": "21.2.1.030", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|21|21.2|21.2.1|21.2.1.030", "title": "21.2.1.030 Expenses and Fees.", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/21.2.1.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/22", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code Title 22 ENROLLMENT Chapter 22.1 Enrollment", "num": "22", "path": "library|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Code|22", "title": "Title 22 ENROLLMENT", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/22"}
