{"body": "Resolution No. SI-R20-017: New Funding Budget Modification to Appropriate Matching Funds At a duly called meeting of the Council of San Ildefonso Pueblo on the 13th day of August, 2020, the following Resolution was adopted: WHEREAS, the Council approved the FY 2020-2021 Annual Budget starting on July 1, 2020; and, WHEREAS, the Council has determined that a modification to the FY 2020-2021 Annual Budget is necessary to appropriate matching funds to the CARES Act funds recently received by the Pueblo in order to provide distributions directly to Members of the Pueblo to help address the economic hardships caused by COVID-19 pandemic. NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED, that the Council hereby enacts the Budget Modification No. 1 to the FY 2020-2021 Annual Budget (NF #1). CERTIFICATION The foregoing resolution was duly voted upon by the Council on August 13, 2020, at a meeting with a vote of 10 in favor, 0 opposed, 0 abstaining and 0 absent (Governor presiding and not voting) pursuant to the authority vested in the Council by the Agreement of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. William S. Christian, Council Secretary COUNCIL REPRESENTATIVE SPONSOR(S): Council Representatives COUNCIL REPRESENTATIVE YES NO ABSTAIN ABSENT William S. Christian X Terrence K. Garcia X Thelma Gonzales X Thomas Gonzales X M. Wayne Martinez, Jr. X Raymond J. Martinez X Christopher Moquino X James L. Naranjo X Leon T. Roybal X Irene Tse-Pe X DELIVERY OF THE RESOLUTION TO THE GOVERNOR: Resolution No. SI-R20-017 was presented to the Governor of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso on the 14th day of August, 2020, pursuant to the Governing document of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Agreement\"), GOVERNOR, Sec. 4 (c), and will become effective after signature by the Governor or veto override by the Council. William S. Christian, Council Secretary GOVERNOR'S ACTION: { X } APPROVED { } VETO - RETURNED TO COUNCIL WITH EXPLANATION: On this 14th day of August, 2020. Perry M. Martinez, Governor Presented by the Governor to the Council on the ____ day of ____________, 2020. COUNCIL'S ACTION: Override of Governor's veto: { } YES { } NO COUNCIL REPRESENTATIVE YES NO ABSTAIN ABSENT William S. Christian Terrence K. Garcia Thelma Gonzales Thomas Gonzales M. Wayne Martinez, Jr. Raymond J. Martinez Christopher Moquino James L. Naranjo Leon T. Roybal Irene Tse-Pe CERTIFICATION The foregoing resolution was duly voted upon by the Council on _________________, 2020, at a meeting with a vote of ______ in favor, _____ opposed, _____ abstaining and _____ absent (Governor presiding and not voting) pursuant to the authority vested in the Council by the Agreement of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. William S. Christian, Council Secretary NEW FUNDING BUDGET MODIFICATION TO APPROPRIATE MATCHING FUNDS New &lt;a class=\"no-wrap\" href=\"/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.3.22.010\"&gt;Section 6.3.22.010&lt;/a&gt; Section 1.1. Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"NEW FUNDING BUDGET MODIFICATION TO APPROPRIATE MATCHING FUNDS (\"NF #1\").\" New &lt;a class=\"no-wrap\" href=\"/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.3.22.020\"&gt;Section 6.3.22.020&lt;/a&gt; Section 1.2. Purpose The purpose of this budget modification is to appropriate matching funds to the CARES Act funds recently received from the federal government and to be taken from the Pueblo's investment funds in order to make an immediate distribution to all members of the Pueblo. New &lt;a class=\"no-wrap\" href=\"/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.3.22.030\"&gt;Section 6.3.22.030&lt;/a&gt; Section 1.3. Findings (a) The Council approved the FY 2020-2021 Annual Budget starting on July 1, 2020; and (b) The Council has determined that a modification to the FY 2020-2021 Annual Budget is necessary to appropriate matching funds from the Pueblo's investment funds to the CARES Act funds in order to use the matching funds to provide distributions directly to Members of the Pueblo to help address the economic hardships caused by the COVID-19 pandemic so long as all distributions are made exclusively from the matching funds; and (c) The NF-1 budget modification shall be considered a modification to the FY 2020-2021 Annual Budget as matching funds to a new grant as permitted by the Governing Agreement at any time. New &lt;a class=\"no-wrap\" href=\"/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/6.3.22.040\"&gt;Section 6.3.22.040&lt;/a&gt; Section 1.4. Budget Modification and Appropriation The Council hereby appropriates matching funds in the amount of $384,500 from the Pueblo's investment funds to the CARES Act funds received by the Pueblo in order to issue a distribution of $500 exclusively from such matching funds to each Member of the Pueblo who is enrolled as a member as of the effective date of this resolution.", "num": "SI-R20-017", "path": "library|us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/resolutions|2020|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council Res. No. SI-R20-017", "title": "Resolution No. SI-R20-017: New Funding Budget Modification to Appropriate Matching Funds", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/resolutions/2020/017"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/resolutions/2020/016", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "Resolution No. SI-R20-016: Tribal Member Distribution Authorization Act Amendment At a duly called meeting of the Council of San Ildefonso Pueblo on the 13th day of August, 2020, the following Resolution was adopted: WHEREAS, the Council finds that it is in the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize and direct immediate distribution of available funds to all members of the Pueblo to address the economic hardships caused by the COVID-19 pandemic. NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED, that the Council hereby enacts the attached amendment to the law entitled, \"TRIBAL MEMBER DISTRIBUTION AUTHORIZATION ACT.\" CERTIFICATION The foregoing resolution was duly voted upon by the Council on August 13, 2020, at a meeting with a vote of 9 in favor, 0 opposed, 0 abstaining and 1 absent (Governor presiding and not voting) pursuant to the authority vested in the Council by the Agreement of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. William S. Christian, Council Secretary COUNCIL REPRESENTATIVE SPONSOR(S): Council Representatives COUNCIL REPRESENTATIVE YES NO ABSTAIN ABSENT William S. Christian X Terrence K. Garcia X Thelma Gonzales X Thomas Gonzales X M. Wayne Martinez, Jr. X Raymond J. Martinez X Christopher Moquino X James L. Naranjo X Leon T. Roybal X Irene Tse-Pe X DELIVERY OF THE RESOLUTION TO THE GOVERNOR: Resolution No. SI-R20-016 was presented to the Governor of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso on the 14th day of August, 2020, pursuant to the Governing document of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso (\"Agreement\"), GOVERNOR, Sec. 4 (c), and will become effective after signature by the Governor or veto override by the Council. William S. Christian, Council Secretary GOVERNOR'S ACTION: { X } APPROVED { } VETO - RETURNED TO COUNCIL WITH EXPLANATION: On this 14th day of August, 2020. Perry M. Martinez, Governor Presented by the Governor to the Council on the ____ day of ____________, 2020. COUNCIL'S ACTION: Override of Governor's veto: { } YES { } NO COUNCIL REPRESENTATIVE YES NO ABSTAIN ABSENT William S. Christian Terrence K. Garcia Thelma Gonzales Thomas Gonzales M. Wayne Martinez, Jr. Raymond J. Martinez Christopher Moquino James L. Naranjo Leon T. Roybal Irene Tse-Pe CERTIFICATION The foregoing resolution was duly voted upon by the Council on _________________, 2020, at a meeting with a vote of ______ in favor, _____ opposed, _____ abstaining and _____ absent (Governor presiding and not voting) pursuant to the authority vested in the Council by the Agreement of the Pueblo de San Ildefonso. William S. Christian, Council Secretary TRIBAL MEMBER DISTRIBUTION AUTHORIZATION ACT AMENDMENT Section 1.1. Short Title This enactment shall be known as the \"TRIBAL MEMBER DISTRIBUTION AUTHORIZATION ACT AMENDMENT (\"Amendment\").\" Section 1.2. Purpose The purpose of this Amendment is to authorize and direct an immediate distribution of money to all members of the Pueblo on an equitable basis from the line item designated for such purposes in the current 2020-2021 Annual Budget. Amend &lt;a class=\"no-wrap\" href=\"/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.040\"&gt;Section 19.4.1.040&lt;/a&gt; Section 1.3. Findings Title 19, Chapter 19, Section 19.4.1.040 of the Code is hereby amended to add the following subsections (d), (e), and (f) as follows: (d) In 2017, the Council enacted the original Tribal Member Distribution Act to provide for an annual distribution of funds to all Members of the Tribe from discretionary funds received from various sources; and (e) since 2017, the Pueblo has authorized and distributed discretionary funds directly to all members of the Pueblo typically at the beginning of each year; and (f) the Council has determined that it is the best interest of the Pueblo to authorize and direct an immediate distribution of discretionary funds to all members of the Pueblo to address the immediate economic hardships caused by the COVID-19 pandemic. Amend &lt;a class=\"no-wrap\" href=\"/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/code/19.4.1.050\"&gt;Section 19.4.1.050&lt;/a&gt; Section 1.4. Amendment Title 19, Chapter 19, Section 19.4.1.050 of the Code is hereby amended to add the following subsection (d) as follows: (d) The Governor is hereby authorized and directed to issue an immediate distribution of funds in an equal amount to all members of the Pueblo from the line item designated for such purposes in the current 2020-2021 Annual Budget.", "num": "SI-R20-016", "path": "library|us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/resolutions|2020|Pueblo de San Ildefonso Council Res. No. SI-R20-016", "title": "Resolution No. SI-R20-016: Tribal Member Distribution Authorization Act Amendment", "url": "/us/nsn/san-ildefonso/council/resolutions/2020/016"}
